et with experience analysing campaign performance and translating insights into strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with confidence working across clinical, product, and commercial teams, as well as external agencies</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with the NHS including GP Networks and PCNs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with lead generation strategies and marketing automation best practices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using email marketing platforms such as Salesforce Marketing Cloud (or similar).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Content Strategy &amp; Execution</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, develop, and deliver creative content strategies for B2B marketing campaigns that align with Oviva's annual goals and audience needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create high-quality, impactful content across multiple formats, including email campaigns, blog posts, case studies, and web pages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> Repurpose and adapt content across channels and formats (including AI-assisted workflows) to maximise reach and efficiency.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Website &amp; SEO</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•   Maintain the Oviva website via WordPress, including landing pages, content updates and UX improvements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•   Develop the B2B SEO strategy (keyword research, on-page optimisation, technical basics) to grow organic search traffic and inbound enquiries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Event Organisation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the end-to-end organisation of industry conferences, including identification of sponsorship opportunities, merchandise, stand design and staffing coordination.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Podcast &amp; Video</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the filming and production of patient stories for Oviva's social media channels and website, and work on ur GP-facing podcast series - developing future episodes, identifying opportunities to grow the format, and shaping the distribution strategy to maximise reach across relevant channels.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration and Brand Alignment:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the clinical, product and service engagement teams to ensure all content aligns with Oviva's messaging and brand guidelines, and meets the needs of the target audience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance Analysis:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track SEO metrics and other key marketing indicators to generate insights that inform strategic decision-making.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industry Awareness:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay updated on trends and best practices in B2B marketing and content creation within healthcare and technology sectors, leveraging this knowledge to refine Oviva's strategies, ensure content relevance, and drive innovative approaches to engagement and lead generation..</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Job benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission-driven environment focused on making a real-world impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-growth opportunities with a clear path to broader strategic leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A flexible remote/hybrid work culture across the UK, Germany, Switzerland and Poland.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Annual learning &amp; development budget.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Home working allowance and flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation, benefits, and inclusive policies (enhanced leave, etc.)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Having a culture that people want to work in, is very important to us. We do this by keeping our values at the forefront of everything we do: <br />We put the patient first. We empower our teams. We make it happen.<br /><br />Oviva is passionate about creating an inclusive culture that celebrates diverse voices and perspectives. We are proud to be a Disability Confident Employer and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and identities.<br /><br /><strong>A note on our process:</strong> As part of our pre-screening, you may be invited to a short AI interview. Prefer to start with a conversation with one of our recruiters instead? No problem, just let us know in your reply to the invitation email.<br /><br />Ready to help shape the future of digital healthcare? Apply today. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/oviva/sr-marketing-manager-london-400588","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792723215},{"slug":"application-scientist-london-376231","company_name":"Cuspai","title":"Application Scientist","description":"<h2>About CuspAI </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">CuspAI is the frontier AI company on a mission to solve the breakthrough materials needed to power human progress. While nature took billions of years to perfect molecules, we are harnessing AI to unlock trillion-dollar materials breakthroughs in months, not millennia. Our founding team is the most cited in the world, comprised of world-class researchers in AI, chemistry and engineering.<br /><br />We are working on some of the hardest and most important challenges including energy, clean water, the future of compute, and carbon capture, and this is just the start of what our 'search engine' for next-generation materials will unlock.<br /><br />We invite you to be part of a diverse, innovative team at the intersection of AI and materials science, working to create impactful partnerships that drive innovation, scalability, and industry collaboration. This work matters. Your work matters.<br /><br /><strong>We’re on the cusp of the on-demand materials era. Join us.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire across a spectrum of backgrounds. Some Application Scientists are computational (atomistic and molecular simulation, machine-learned force fields), some are experimental (synthesis, processing, characterisation, lab automation), and some are data-driven (materials and cheminformatics, optimisation). What they share is the ability to turn a partner’s problem into a plan, deliver it, and translate fluently between experimental, computational, and machine learning teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate a matrix structure. You will have a home team, but may contribute to projects in another pillar as demand and your expertise evolve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your Impact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own the scientific delivery of partner projects, from scoping to results. Working with our technical programme managers, ML researchers, platform engineers, and lab integration team, you will make sure our platform answers the questions that matter to partners, and that what is learned on each project feeds back into tools and workflows used across the company.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside delivery, you will help build the cross-cutting capabilities that future projects depend on, such as validated workflows, harmonised data pipelines and agentic design campaigns.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Application Areas</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or more of the areas below. You do not need to cover a whole pillar.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Electronics</strong>: Semiconductor processing, device-level modelling and electronics, photonic and thermal materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Energy</strong>: Catalysis, batteries, photovoltaics and multiscale kinetics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Environment</strong>: Porous and soft materials, interfaces, and separations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-cutting</strong>: Materials informatics, automated experimentation and optimisation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Will Do</h2><h3>Project leadership and delivery</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead partner projects from scoping to delivery, as a key point of contact alongside the technical program managers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write technical scopes that define objectives, deliverables, success criteria, and timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare regular technical reports and presentations for partners and internal teams.</p></li></ul><h3>Science and campaigns</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply and extend our platform to partner problems, using simulation, machine learning, data-driven optimisation, or experiments as the project requires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and steer discovery campaigns, including agentic and closed-loop campaigns with partner labs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess when models, simulations, and data can be trusted, and contribute to validating them against experiments.</p></li></ul><h3>Bridging experimental and computational teams</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate platform recommendations into clear, executable experimental plans, and translate lab realities back into requirements for internal teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure data from partners and our own workflows are clean, structured, and consistent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with partner labs, including on-site visits at key stages of a project.</p></li></ul><h3>Capability and product development</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and automate workflows that run reliably at scale within our platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relay partner feedback to TPMs, ML researchers, and platform engineers to improve tools and workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay informed about advances in your field and contribute to the scientific direction of your team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Must Have Skills and Qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A PhD in chemistry, materials science, physics, chemical engineering, or a related field, or equivalent industry experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep, hands-on expertise in at least one of: atomistic simulation (including machine-learned force fields); experimental materials or chemistry, ideally with automation or high-throughput methods; materials or cheminformatics with machine learning and optimisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record in one or more of the application areas above.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python skills for data handling, analysis, automation or modelling, and familiarity with version control (Git).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional ability to communicate with both experimental and computational scientists, and to translate between them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A personal passion for CuspAI's mission and the potential of AI to unlock breakthroughs in materials science.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Bonus Points (But Not Critical)</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Industry experience, particularly in the semiconductor, electronics, energy, or chemical sectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading projects or collaborations with external partners, including writing technical scopes or proposals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multiscale modelling, from atomistic to mesoscale, continuum or device level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical synthesis or processing experience, with an understanding of what makes a route feasible and reproducible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional software engineering practice, such as code review, testing and deployment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience in a start-up or fast-growth technology company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Additional Considerations</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">These roles can be based in our <strong>London, Cambridge, Amsterdam, or Berlin</strong> offices, with the expectation of being in the office at least three days per week. There may be regular travel to partner sites and other CuspAI offices for collaboration and project work.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A competitive salary:</strong> We value and reward impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity in CuspAI:</strong> You have a stake in the success of the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off to stay fresh:</strong> 28 days holiday (DE, NL, UK) or 21 days holiday (JP, SG, US), in addition to local public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>‘Gold Standard’ parental leave:</strong> 26 weeks (primary caregiver) and 12 weeks (secondary caregiver) at full pay - we look after you and your family while we work on the most important materials discovery problems together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional development budget:</strong> We invest in your career development so you can stay up to date with the latest industry knowledge or add to your skills to increase impact and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solve meaningful problems:</strong> See how your work has a direct impact on advancing materials science and solving sustainability and climate-related problems through the creation and application of bleeding-edge SOTA technology and revolutionary techniques</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>True interdisciplinary teamwork:</strong> Be part of a deeply collaborative environment bridging AI research, computational chemistry, and experimental science - work with world-class researchers and engineers who enjoy sharing knowledge and supporting each other</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Join us in shaping the future of materials with AI. Together, we can create groundbreaking solutions for a more sustainable world.</strong><br /><br /><br /><strong>CuspAI is an equal opportunities employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace</strong>. We do not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), veteran status, or any other basis protected by applicable law.<br /><br /><strong>We actively encourage applications from all backgrounds and value the unique perspectives and contributions that diversity brings to our team.</strong><br /><br /><strong>Please let us know if you require any specific adjustments during or after the interview process. We will do everything we can within reason to accommodate.</strong></