 and restricted-product policies to less-defined reviews with minimal direction, weighing competing factors and making sound decisions with imperfect information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use reports, risk signals, case trends, operational data, and web-service tools to identify emerging threats, high-risk or suspicious activity, and opportunities for proactive mitigation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance portfolio protection and chargeback risk by assessing chargeback likelihood alongside the merchant’s capacity to repay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve compliance violations and complex cases, identify material risks, escalate unresolved issues appropriately, and contribute to resolution and follow-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify recurring issues, control gaps, and risk patterns across tools, workflows, queues, policies, and playbooks, and recommend practical improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce concise case summaries, findings, recommendations, and decision rationale; maintain accurate documentation and contribute to knowledge material, playbooks, and team learning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead complex customer communications and collaborate with Support, FS Merchant Services, Product, risk analysts, and other teams to resolve shared problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to incidents, complex reviews, trend investigations, projects, process improvements, and team best practices while prioritising competing work effectively.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you need to bring:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a highly analytical and collaborative professional with experience within a relevant analyst role along with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2 years of experience in payments, fraud, credit risk, compliance, or financial services operations or related discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to structured workflows, case management, queues, or service-level targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with written procedures and maintaining accurate records.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in deepening existing knowledge on fraud, credit risk, merchant risk, and payments and suggesting improvements based on said knowledge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of Card Scheme rules and regulations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of the full Chargeback flow and process - Understanding chargeback risk timeframes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong working knowledge of Excel/Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good conceptual thinking with proven analytic, problem-solving and effective reporting skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing structured case work with increasing complexity and limited direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work independently and make decisions based on available information</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work in a dynamic fast-paced environment with tight deadlines</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that people are more than what’s on their CV. If you’re unsure that you have the right profile for the role... hit the ‘Apply’ button and give it a try!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed Experience…</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career growth opportunities based on performance within a company that's continuously expanding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with highly skilled people who are as passionate about Fraud &amp; Risk as you are</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An environment that encourages initiatives and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fun activities with your teammates &amp; social events throughout the year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to learn, expand your skill set, forge wonderful relationships and make your mark within the diverse and inclusive Lightspeed culture, a true Canadian tech success story</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy and healthy:</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed equity scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible Paid Time Off - providing you the freedom to take time off however you like</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance and cash health plan for optical, dental and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 GBP per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the LifeWorks and Modern Health Apps- whether it is meditation, coaching or counselling you need - each employee gets access to this platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transit / parking benefit - for when you need to travel to the Belfast office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A variety of drinks &amp; snacks in our offices in Belfast.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: L