rong>Who we’re looking for</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">You probably have around <strong>2–3 years of recruitment experience within retail</strong> and a strong understanding of the UK market.</p><p class="MsoNormal">You’ll also be someone who:</p><ul><li><p>Has strong experience using <strong>LinkedIn Recruiter</strong> and genuinely enjoys proactive sourcing.</p></li><li><p>Knows how to connect with candidates and turn a first conversation into real interest.</p></li><li><p>Has a strong eye for talent and is confident assessing potential, not just matching CVs to job descriptions.</p></li><li><p>Understands fashion and retail and is curious about brands, competitors and the market.</p></li><li><p>Brings energy, personality and strong communication skills.</p></li><li><p>Is confident working with demanding stakeholders and comfortable challenging when needed.</p></li><li><p>Thinks outside the box and doesn’t accept “there are no candidates” as the final answer.</p></li><li><p>Takes ownership, works autonomously and brings ideas rather than waiting for direction.</p></li><li><p>Is organised enough to manage multiple recruitment processes, stakeholders and projects at the same time.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">Experience with <strong>Recruitee, Indeed or similar recruitment platforms</strong> is a plus.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">If you love fashion, people and the challenge of finding the right talent — and you want a role where your ideas can genuinely shape how we recruit — we’d love to meet you.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>INDINDITEXSM</p><p><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/inditex/talent-acquisition-maternity-cover-london-305638","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"LONDON, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792722670},{"slug":"senior-sales-executive-me-perform-london-306330","company_name":"Marcus Evans","title":"Senior Sales Executive (ME Perform)","description":"<p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Marcus Evans</span></strong><span style="color:#242424"> is a global leader in business intelligence, helping our clients grow by making connections, sharing knowledge, inspiring people, building relationships and creating new opportunities. Since 1983, we have brought decision-makers together through high-level summits, conferences, online platforms and performance programmes, working across all sectors and regions.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">Our overriding approach is one of collaboration, and our belief that “We’ll be our most successful when we work together.” We recognise excellence and actively develop top performers into future leaders. Our culture promotes teamwork, continuous learning and global career growth.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">About Perform</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">Perform by Marcus Evans is our performance-improvement consultancy. We don’t sell off-the-shelf training. We start with a diagnosis of what is actually holding a team or an organisation back, prescribe the programme that fixes it, deliver bespoke learning pathways facilitated by vetted trainers/coaches, and then assess what changed. Clients get a written view of the gaps, the fix and the result.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Job Summary</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">We are hiring a Senior Sales Executives to sell Perform to senior leaders at large organisations: Heads of HR, L&amp;D, Talent and Transformation, and the business executives who sponsor their programmes. You will own the sale from first conversation to signed contract, working with our Programme Scientist, who builds the diagnosis and prescription behind every proposal. This is a consultative sale with long cycles, several stakeholders and meaningful deal values. We are looking for someone who has done it before and wants to build a book of business from the start.</span></p><p class="elementtoproof" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">This is an onsite role based in our </span><strong><span style="color:#242424">London </span></strong><span style="color:#242424">office.</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Key Responsibilities</span></strong></p><ul><li><p>Generate and qualify your own pipeline through targeted outreach, networking, referrals and social selling to senior HR, L&amp;D and business leaders</p></li><li><p>Run structured discovery calls using our Initial Discovery Template, so the client’s real performance problem is clear before any proposal is written</p></li><li><p>Work with the Programme Scientist to turn discovery into a bespoke diagnosis, prescription and quote, and present it to the client sponsor</p></li><li><p>Position Perform as an expert advisor, qualify prospects rigorously, and manage intake so each quarter’s cohorts are full and the programme stays selective</p></li><li><p>Negotiate pricing and terms within our pricing framework, and take contracts through to signature</p></li><li><p>Keep every opportunity current in HubSpot CRM, from contact to lead to deal, so forecasting and reporting are accurate</p></li><li><p>Stay with the client after signature through delivery and assessment, and use the findings to open expansion and renewal conversations</p></li><li><p>Share what you learn from the market (objections, competitors, pricing pressure) with the leadership team so the offer keeps improving</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><span style="color:#242424">Qualifications</span></strong></p><p class="elementtoproof"><em><span style="color:#242424">Required:</span></em></p><ul><li><p>Bachelor’s degree or equivalent in Behavioural Science or related fields.</p></li><li><p>At least five years of B2B sales experience, including closing complex, high-value deals with multiple stakeholders</p></li><li><p>Proven experience selling leadership development, learning and development, coaching, talent, HR consulting or other professional services to senior buyers</p></li><li><p>A record of meeting or exceeding targets, with examples you can discuss</p></li><li><p>Excellent written and spoken English, and the credibility to hold a conversation with a C-suite executive</p></li><li><p>Comfort with discovery-led, consultative selling rather than product pitching</p></li><li><p>Right to work in the UK</p></li></ul><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><em><span style="color:#242424">Preferred:</span></em></p><ul><li><p>Experience selling to financial services, banking, technology or other regulated, multinational clients</p></li><li><p>An existing network among HR and L&amp;D decision-makers</p></li><li><p>Experience working alongside subject-matter experts or consultants to build proposals</p></li><li><p>HubSpot, LinkedIn Sales Navigator or comparable CRM and prospecting tools</p></li><li><p>Additional languages</p></li></ul><p class="elementtoproof"><span style="color:#242424">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="elementtoproof"><strong><em><span style="color:#242424">Marcus Evans</span></em></strong><em><span style="color:#242424"> is an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity, and all employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit and business need.</span></em></p><p>#LI-Onsite</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/marcus-evans/senior-sales-executive-me-perform-london-306330","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"London, Greater London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792722670},{"slug":"remote-participate-in-the-openai-experience-lab-ai-enthusiasts-wanted-location-london-uk-in-person-date-9-november-183782","company_name":"Tester Work","title":"Participate in the OpenAI Experience Lab – AI Enthusiasts Wanted! Location: London, UK (In-Person) Date: 9 November","description":"<p>Calling all AI enthusiasts, early adopters, and power users! We are hosting an exclusive in-person <strong>OpenAI Experience Lab</strong> in London on the 9th of November, and we want you to be a part of it.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>If you actively use generative AI tools (like ChatGPT, Claude, Midjourney, etc.) in your personal or professional life, this is your chance to test cutting-edge features, share your insights, and help shape the future of artificial intelligence.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Who we are looking for:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Currently based in or able to commute to London.</p></li><li><p>Frequent users of AI platforms and tools.</p></li><li><p>Comfortable sharing feedback and discussing technical concepts in a group or 1-on-1 setting.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Apply Now:</strong> Please complete the <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://experiencelabs.globalapptesting.com/united-kingdom">screening questionnaire</a> to confirm your eligibility and secure your spot!</p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tester-work/remote-participate-in-the-openai-experience-lab-ai-enthusiasts-wanted-location-london-uk-in-person-date-9-november-183782","tags":["Usability Research","Remote"],"job_types":["Entry","parttime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792722668},{"slug":"senior-field-marketing-manager-north-155119","company_name":"Twilio","title":"Senior Field Marketing Manager - North","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dedication to &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;remote-first work&lt;/a&gt;, and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;paid-scroll&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-inner&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-bcframe--off&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-thread&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-msg assistant&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-bubble assistant &quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paid-prose&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio&#39;s next &lt;strong&gt;Senior Field Marketing Manager&amp;nbsp; - North (UK &amp;amp; Nordics)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to lead and execute the regional field marketing and high-touch event strategy across the UK &amp;amp; Nordics, accelerating pipeline conversion and driving measurable revenue growth across key target accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Field Marketing Manager, you will serve as the field marketing engine for Twilio’s North region. Working closely with Sales Leadership, you will design and deliver targeted 1st-party events, C-level dinners, technical workshops, and partner co-marketing activations. You will engage key decision-makers, open doors in strategic accounts, and accelerate deal velocity across core products like WhatsApp for Business, Voice AI, and Conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner&lt;/strong&gt; closely with North Sales Leadership and Account Executives to align event programs directly with regional revenue targets and priority accounts across Strategic and New Business segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design&lt;/strong&gt; hyper-focused event experiences (e.g., C-level roundtables, founder dinners, technical deep-dive workshops, and roadshows) built to solve specific regional customer pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead&lt;/strong&gt; end-to-end strategy, content localisation, speaker sourcing, venue management, and execution for proprietary Twilio regional events across key North tech hubs (e.g., London, Stockholm, Copenhagen).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own&lt;/strong&gt; regional presence at strategic industry conferences and hyper-scaler co-marketing events (AWS, Meta, Google) in partnership with the Partner Marketing Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish&lt;/strong&gt; strict lead and attendee follow-up SLAs with regional SDR and AE teams to convert event engagement into qualified pipeline and deal velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop&lt;/strong&gt; targeted post-event content and micro-campaigns to enable Account Executives to maintain momentum with enterprise account teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure&lt;/strong&gt; and report on event success through commercial metrics: target account penetration rate, pipeline created/influenced, deal velocity, and closed-won revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage&lt;/strong&gt; the apportioned regional field marketing budget and local vendor relationships to ensure optimal ROI and flawless execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of enterprise software/SaaS field marketing experience, with a proven track record of owning event strategy and execution tied directly to pipeline and revenue generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with the UK &amp;amp; Nordics region, including regional business etiquette, key enterprise tech hubs, local event ecosystems, and localized content preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Impeccable English written and verbal communication skills to write compelling local messaging and engage with regional enterprise buyers and agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated commercial acumen with the ability to act as a trusted peer to Senior Sales Leadership and Enterprise Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using CRM and marketing automation tools (e.g., Salesforce, Marketo) to track event ROI, account attendance depth, and pipeline conversion across the funnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organisational discipline and project management skills to handle multiple complex event activations simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with account-based marketing (ABM) methodologies and account-level pipeline tracking within enterprise SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote, and based in the UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to learn from each other. For this role, approximately 25–30% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way across the DACH region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate&#39;s starting salary will be determined based on permissible, non-discriminatory factors such as skills, experience, and geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in our job application procedures. If you need assistance or an accommodation due to a disability, please contact us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio thinks big. Do you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like to solve problems, take initiative, pitch in when needed, and are always up for trying new things. That&#39;s why we seek out colleagues who embody our values — something we call &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt;Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt;. Additionally, we empower employees to build &lt;a href=&quot;https://twilio.org/support-and-resources/impact-fund&quot;&gt;positive change in their communities&lt;/a&gt; by supporting their volunteering and donation efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
