&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.coreweave.com/&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CoreWeave is taking its AI cloud and data center services to new countries. Each new market brings its own data protection, cybersecurity, and data residency requirements, and we have to meet them before we launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Technical Program Manager for International Security &amp;amp; Privacy Compliance, you will own the program that gets CoreWeave compliant in each new market. You will turn local legal and regulatory requirements into controls, timelines, and owners. Then you will lead Legal, Privacy, Security, Data Center Operations, Product, and Go-to-Market through to a compliant launch. The problem is defined; the solution is not. You will build the playbook as you go and make it repeatable for each market that follows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is based in London so you can work during business hours with US teams and with teams in the Middle East and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end compliance program for new-country launches, from early regulatory assessment through go-live and ongoing upkeep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Legal and Privacy counsel to turn local laws into concrete technical and operational requirements. These cover data protection and privacy, cybersecurity, data localization and residency, cross-border data transfer, incident reporting, and registration or licensing. Legal owns the interpretation; you own turning it into delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map country requirements to CoreWeave&#39;s existing control framework (SOC 2, ISO/IEC 27001, and related certifications). Find gaps and drive the work to close them with control owners in Security, Engineering, and Data Center Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain source-of-truth program plans, a requirements register, and a dependency map for each market. Use them to drive high-quality execution against timelines leadership can rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build country-specific incident and breach notification obligations into CoreWeave&#39;s incident response process before go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find risks and blockers early, such as data residency limits on architecture, local vendor or partner obligations, and regulator timelines. Drive them to resolution across teams, or escalate them with clear options and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate privacy reviews and data protection impact assessments for in-country services, working with Privacy and Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring compliance requirements into product and data center launch plans early, so customer-facing commitments, contracts, and Trust Center content reflect what we can actually deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report program status, risk, and decisions needed to Security, Legal, and business leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the work repeatable. Turn each market&#39;s lessons into a scalable country-entry playbook, templates, and workflows in Jira and our GRC tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[5+] years of relevant experience in international security and privacy compliance program management, GRC, or related technical program management, preferably at a cloud, data center, or infrastructure provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of managing end-to-end, large-scale, cross-functional programs with significant organizational impact under little or no supervision. You are comfortable with work that has a defined problem but no defined solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong execution skills. You get things done to high quality on timelines people can trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You identify risks and blockers early and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid grounding in industry best practices and frameworks such as ISO/IEC 27001, ISO/IEC 27701, SOC 2, NIST CSF, and GDPR-style data protection regimes. You can make well-reasoned decisions and tradeoffs that fit CoreWeave&#39;s context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You quickly learn and keep up with the requirements of unfamiliar jurisdictions, well enough to take an active part in decisions with Legal, Security, and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use feedback to shape priorities, and you make sure compliance solutions don&#39;t degrade the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You influence cross-functional decisions with a structured approach, data, and technical insight, to achieve the intended outcome. You also contribute to the wider CoreWeave community, for example by mentoring others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You win buy-in from critical stakeholders on your recommendations, define clear communication strategies tailored to the audience, from engineers to executives, and seek out feedback to improve how you work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running compliance programs across several countries, especially in Asia-Pacific or the Middle East.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data residency, sovereign cloud, or in-country hosting requirements for cloud or data center services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as CIPP/E, CIPM, CISSP, CISM, CISA, or PMP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GRC platforms and with Jira-based program tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who bring unique backgrounds, even if you don&#39;t check every box. Here are a few qualities we&#39;ve found make someone successful on our team. If some of this describes you, we&#39;d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable balancing compliance rigor with practical, scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership, bring structure to ambiguity, and follow issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly with technical and non-technical stakeholders and build strong cross-functional partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by building processes and systems that improve how teams work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/coreweaveu/senior-technical-program-manager-international-security-privacy-compliance-london-185710","tags":["Technology - G&A"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792713321},{"slug":"release-manager-ai-models-london-united-kingdom-67141","company_name":"Wayve","title":"Release Manager - AI Models","description":"<div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/c3dedbb7-82c2-4668-a1bf-b53c8f870af0/8c1bb54c-6e60-48b5-8dbb-5631ddd06204" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what this particular role covers.</p><h2><br />🛠️ About our Engineering Teams</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineering teams bring together ML engineering, evaluation and data science, software platform, testing, and product to turn breakthrough autonomous-driving technology into reliable products. Model releases connect these disciplines, taking AI models from early hypotheses through training, evaluation, and on-road testing to deployment across our vehicle fleet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Release Manager — AI Models, you’ll help ensure that a core part of our technology — the AI model — is released reliably, on time, and to the standard required for production. You’ll bring structure and disciplined release practices to the fast-paced, non-deterministic world of ML, building the processes and systems that support clarity, stability, and business goals.<br /></p><h2>🧠 Your day-to-day</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the model release cycle, maintaining a steady and predictable cadence while adapting to changing business priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate across ML engineering, evaluation and data science, software platform, testing, and product to keep releases moving and resolve dependencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the gates that promote models from hypothesis → training → evaluation → validation → deployment, making clear what is ready to ship and what needs more work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive investigations into regressions and integration issues, coordinate rollback or roll-forward decisions, and follow through on technical debt and corrective actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the central point of contact for model-release status, risks, and timelines, giving engineers and leadership the right level of detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run post-release reviews and turn lessons learned into practical improvements across teams.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>🧩 What you’ll be working on:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Release gates and promotion criteria:</strong> Define and justify what it takes for a model to progress, balancing performance gains, reproducibility, product requirements, safety, and compatibility with the onboard software stack and vehicle platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A release process that works for ML:</strong> Build frameworks that connect model development, evaluation, the Wayve onboard stack, and product needs — applying strong release-engineering practices while recognising where hypothesis-driven, non-deterministic systems need a different approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bottleneck identification and improvement:</strong> Find constraints in the release lifecycle, implement dashboards and KPIs to make them visible, and proactively escalate gaps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling and automation:</strong> Partner with ML platform and integration teams to shape end-to-end automated release tooling. Define requirements that improve developer experience, release efficiency, and stakeholder communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliable, stable deployments:</strong> Strengthen how teams handle model versions, integration issues, regressions, and recovery so that releases deliver value reliably.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>🙌 You should apply if:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have 5+ years of experience in release management, software engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) and release management practices, including testing strategy, system integration, branching, and versioning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a conceptual understanding of ML fundamentals: what training data is, the difference between training and inference, what a model version or checkpoint represents, and why model validation is probabilistic rather than simply pass/fail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have experience with CI/CD pipelines and automation tools such as GitHub, Buildkite, and CLI tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re skilled at managing releases in complex, fast-moving systems and comfortable adapting processes and tooling as requirements, architecture, and timelines change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring strong problem-solving and decision-making skills, including when release trade-offs depend on limited or ambiguous data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly with engineers and leadership, helping people understand priorities, risks, and decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re pragmatic, methodical, and system-minded. You bring strong release-engineering instincts and are keen to develop the judgment to know where ML systems require a different approach.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>It’s a bonus if you also bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in AI/ML, autonomous vehicles, or robotics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with MLOps methodologies and tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ML evaluation practices and tooling, especially for physical systems — including simulation, model leaderboards, and statistically powered experiments such as A/B or shadow-mode testing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awareness of model hardware and software dependencies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A BSc or equivalent in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical discipline.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay! If you’re passionate about autonomy and keen to learn, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every requirement.<br /></p><h2>More about Wayve:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Wayve is building the leading AI platform for autonomous driving. We are pioneering an end-to-end AI approach that enables vehicles to learn directly from real-world experience, developing the ability to adapt, generalise and improve at scale. Instead of relying on hand-coded rules or pre-mapped environments, our AI Driver learns to drive by understanding the world around it. The result is technology that navigates complex urban environments with intelligence, precision and natural flow, unlocking meaningful advances in both safety and efficiency. We believe autonomy represents a once-in-a-generation transformation in how people and goods move, comparable to the shift from horses to cars, and from human-driven vehicles to intelligent machines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make autonomy universal. Wayve’s mapless and hardware-agnostic AI platform integrates with global OEM partners, enabling continuous software evolution and unlocking advanced levels of automation from L2 plus through to L4 as our core AI model scales. In a race increasingly defined by intelligence and real-world learning, Wayve is taking a distinct approach, building a generalisable driving intelligence that can power any vehicle, anywhere. By combining embodied AI with scalable deployment, we are creating technology that can be shaped to each OEM brand and driver experience, accelerating the transition to a safer, more intelligent future of mobility.<br /></p><h2>How we work 💻 — Locations &amp; Flexible Working:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-time role based in our London office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our main hubs are in London, Sunnyvale, Yokohama, Herzliya, Vancouver and Leonberg. We operate a hybrid working model that combines in-person collaboration in our dedicated office spaces with focused time working remotely. This gives our teams the connection and energy of working together, alongside the flexibility to do their best work in a way that fits their lives.<br /></p><h2>🔍 The Interview Process:</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is clear and respectful of your time:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial call / recruiter screen</strong> (30 mins)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency Interviews</strong> (Release Management &amp; Cross Functional Collaboration)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep-dive technical interviews</strong> (Technical Assessment and Case Study)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interview:</strong> mission &amp; values alignment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ll always explain the format and work around your availability.<br /></p><h2>What’s in it for you (Location dependent):</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Salaries benchmarked against the market annually</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Meaningful equity, sharing in the ownership and long-term success of Wayve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ Relocation support and visa sponsorship where applicable</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Hybrid working, core hours and the chance to work hands-on in vehicle workshops and labs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 Learning and development budgets with support for training, conferences and growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Comprehensive benefits including health insurance, dental, enhanced maternity and paternity leave, retirement or pension where applicable, access to therapists, wellbeing partnerships, team socials and more</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">A quick, honest note before you apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wayve is not a mature, fully-structured place with the playbook already written. Much of how we work is still being written, and if you join, you’ll help write it. That suits people who want real ownership more than people who need a settled structure from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like the kind of problem you want to spend your time on, we’d really like to hear from you.<br /><br />At Wayve we're committed to creating a diverse, fair and respectful culture that is inclusive of everyone based on their unique skills and perspectives, and regardless of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding) or any other basis as protected by applicable law.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Careers at Wayve.</a> To learn more about what drives us, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Values at Wayve</a><br /><br />DISCLAIMER: We will not ask about marriage or pregnancy, care responsibilities or disabilities in any of our job adverts or interviews. However, we do look to capture information about care responsibilities, and disabilities among other diversity information as part of an optional DEI Monitoring form to help us identify areas of improvement in our hiring process and ensure that the process is inclusive and non-discriminatory.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wayve/release-manager-ai-models-london-united-kingdom-67141","tags":["AV Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792712418},{"slug":"principal-engineer-data-quality-platform-london-365915","company_name":"Talos Trading","title":"Principal Engineer, Data Quality Platform","description":"<h1>Institutional Fabric for the Digital Asset Market</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2018, Talos provides institutional-grade trading technology for the global digital asset market, powering many of the major players in the crypto ecosystem. Our mission is clear: to advance the mass adoption of digital assets by seamlessly connecting institutions to the digital asset ecosystem. We are committed to building the most innovative and trusted platform in the world, supporting the entire trading lifecycle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Talos, you’ll find an environment that champions kindness and respect, values diverse perspectives, and upholds inclusivity at every turn. We believe every member of our team brings invaluable insights and abilities that drive Talos forward. In our pursuit of excellence, we foster a culture of trust, integrity, collaboration, and mutual growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a tight-knit yet globally distributed team of highly experienced engineers and business leaders, with hubs in New York, London, Singapore, and Cyprus. You’ll be part of a hybrid-friendly environment where your unique talents and insights will play a crucial role in building something extraordinary.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong> Principal Engineer, Data Quality Platform</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll own data correctness across Talos. You'll lead the data quality engineering team, run BAU data operations, and own reference and security master data, along with the pipelines and platform that deliver it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our goal: the data we return to clients is always correct, and we find defects before a client does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join a small team with the mandate to work independently from product engineering and challenge it. Engineering teams make assumptions about how their systems behave. Your job is to test those assumptions and prove or disprove them with evidence.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead AI-first data quality engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Validate every client-facing endpoint continuously. The focus is our REST and WebSocket APIs. Cloud delivery (S3, Snowflake, Databricks) is also in scope. Assert correctness against independent sources of truth, across every environment and client entitlement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cover streaming as well as request/response. For WebSocket, that means:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">sequencing and gap detection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">snapshot-to-increment consistency</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">reconnect and replay correctness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">staleness of live subscriptions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">agreement between the streamed view and the REST view of the same state</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use adaptive detection, not static thresholds. Learn baselines per endpoint and per market, and let them adjust as "normal" changes. Hand-set limits get noisy, go stale, and teach people to ignore alerts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply LLM and agentic tooling to generate checks from API specs and schemas, keep them current as the product changes, and triage alerts before a human sees them. Know when a deterministic rule, invariant or cross-source reconciliation is the better tool.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test resilience and load. Design load, performance and failure-mode tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">When you find a fault, raise it with the owning team with enough evidence for them to act. Drive it to resolution, then add a check that would have caught it earlier.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure and publish endpoint and field coverage, time to detect, detected-before-client rate and false-positive rate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run data governance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a catalog of our data assets and APIs, covering lineage and downstream consumers. Maintain an understanding of assets, how they're used and what breaks when they change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own data governance tooling such as OpenMetadata.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own reference and security master data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the build-out of the next-generation security master platform, then run it day to day: new listings, symbol mapping across venues, and increment and contract specs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design processes for safe updates to security entries, with validation and rollback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expand coverage across the firm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, extend data quality coverage beyond client APIs to:</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">trade signals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">pre-trade analytics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">client post-trade analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PMS analytics</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Qualifications</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of leading data QA or data quality teams, preferably on market data or other high-throughput, real-time data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep understanding of streaming and API behaviour: throughput, WebSocket semantics, ordering, recovery and failure modes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience inventorying and testing a large API and data surface end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with data governance: cataloging, lineage, ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with performance and load testing of distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong engineering background. You design platforms, not scripts on a cron job, and you build on shared infrastructure rather than creating one-off tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience applying LLM and agentic tooling to engineering problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our stack: Flink, Doris, Dagster and Spark, plus OpenMetadata (or an equivalent such as Apache Atlas). Experience with comparable tools is just as relevant.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out these videos and links to learn more about Talos and our culture!</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spotlight Article: Talos Snapshot by DRW</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Podcast: 2023 episode with co-founders Anton &amp; Ethan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Website: Explore Talos: Products, Investors, Team &amp; More</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case Studies: Real world examples of client solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Awards: Talos Wins Hedgeweek Global Digital Assets Award 2024</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture: Award-winning, Forbes-listed, low-attrition team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Andreessen Horowitz re: Talos: "The company best suited to drive institutional adoption is one that understands traditional capital markets deeply and is forward-thinking enough to fully grasp the promise of crypto. Talos is that company."</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Benefits </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will also enjoy a comprehensive array of competitive benefits, regardless of your location, within our warm, welcoming, and ambitious company culture. Some of our benefits include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement plan contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited Vacation + a PTO bonus: Employees that take 15 days of vacation, with 5 days being consecutive, receive a $2000 USD bonus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Yearly discretionary cash bonus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee stock options plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical, dental, and vision insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave for 20 weeks, after 1 year of service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global offsites and team outings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-time stipend towards at-home office set-up for all employees</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A wellness credit of $50 accrued monthly, to go towards things like gym memberships, ski-passes, and work out classes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A lunch credit of $25 USD towards lunches for days in-office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Donation matching up to $100 USD annually</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Other in-office perks: Catered lunches on Tuesdays, snacks, and drinks</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://talos.com/company/#join-the-team"><u>other open positions</u></a> listed on our website!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer.  We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, sexual stereotypes, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.  Talos is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities in our recruiting process.  If you need any assistance or accommodations due to a disability, please let us know at ----- style="min-height:1.5em">© Talos Trading, ----- style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talos is proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer.  We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pre