&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the end-to-end strategy for Kaluza Agent Experience (KAE) within the European market—grounded in global product goals but sharpened by local client needs and agent behaviors. Driving core operational metrics (AHT, FCR, CSAT, AI adoption, onboarding)ensuring capabilities improve agent/customer outcomes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Journey Design &amp;amp; UX Consistency: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as guardian of agent UX across KAE to ensure coherence across the experience. Partnering with UX and domain teams to apply shared patterns consistently, reduce agent cognitive load, and maintain alignment and compliance with the design system as new automation and assistive/AI capabilities are introduced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Integrations &amp;amp; Client Onboarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive technical and product integrations with third-party platforms and oversee spinning up new KAE instances end-to-end for incoming clients from discovery through go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure Accessibility &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion EU accessibility regulations by design, translating regulatory and market-specific needs into actionable engineering requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage Clients &amp;amp; Drive Value:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the trusted expert for clients on agent experience, advocating for platform-first configuration over bespoke builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Delivery &amp;amp; Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain active involvement across the entire Product Development Life Cycle (PDLC)—from agent discovery sessions to feedback loops—and produce materials to support successful client adoption.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;(Note: Travel to client sites e.g., Brussels, is expected at roughly 1–3 trips a month initially, tapering to 1–2 times a quarter.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally, you’ll have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contact Centre &amp;amp; UX Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep experience owning end-to-end user journeys for high-frequency operational tools (e.g., agent desktops), with hands-on craft in user research, journey mapping, and usability testing with agents and supervisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EU Accessibility &amp;amp; Platform Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of EU accessibility standards alongside proven experience integrating products with complex third-party platforms and vendor ecosystems.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Delivery &amp;amp; Market Expansion:&lt;/strong&gt; Successful track record implementing or localizing a product for external enterprise clients, taking solutions from zero to live through discovery, configuration, and change management.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Informed Judgement &amp;amp; Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability using operational metrics (AHT, FCR, CSAT, agent effort) to defend product decisions, coupled with a platform-first mindset that prioritizes existing capabilities over custom code.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bilingual Capability:&lt;/strong&gt; Full professional bilingual fluency (written and spoken) in both English and French.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What will set you apart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experience leveraging AI tools, machine learning capabilities, or LLM integrations within product workflows to enhance platform intelligence and automation directly into customer service desktop environments.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience within SaaS platforms, the energy sector, or large-scale utility migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience to scale UI consistency across different product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience to scale UI consistency across different product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Five values guide how we work at Kaluza:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play to win:&lt;/strong&gt; Collective pride in decarbonising energy at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve the real problem:&lt;/strong&gt; Cutting through complexity to focus on real-world outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trust every day:&lt;/strong&gt; Consistency, transparency and doing what we say.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the outcome:&lt;/strong&gt; Full accountability, wins and setbacks, without ego.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go further together: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaboration, respect and different perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial &amp;amp; Insurance: &lt;/strong&gt;Discretionary bonus, Alan Mutuelle Health Insurance, x3 Life &amp;amp; Death insurance (Prévoyance) via Alan, and standard Sécurité Sociale contributions (pension, family allowance, unemployment insurance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Allowances:&lt;/strong&gt; 50% commuting expense reimbursement, €200 Home Working Allowance, and €150 Learning Fund&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off &amp;amp; Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; 25 days holiday + bank holidays + RTT days, Moments That Matter Leave, Compassionate Leave, two paid Volunteering Days, Flexible Working, and Career Break eligibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come as you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to meet people from all walks of life. The more inclusive we are, the better our work will be, and we recognise talent on merit and potential. If you’re excited about the role but don’t tick every box, we’d still love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;. Our Applicant Data Protection Policy is&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/applicant-data-protection-notice/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kaluza/product-manager-agent-experience-fluency-in-french-english-required-london-174817","tags":["Product"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792702534},{"slug":"director-of-platform-operations-bristol-london-258015","company_name":"Kaluza","title":"Director of Platform Operations","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job title:&lt;/strong&gt; Director of Platform Operations&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Bristol or London (Including hybrid)&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary: &lt;/strong&gt;£141,000 - £170,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Product &amp;amp; Tech Operations&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to:&lt;/strong&gt; VP Product &amp;amp; Tech Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is based in either Bristol or London and requires an existing right to work in the UK.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today&#39;s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future. Leveraging Data, AI, and real-time decision-making we turn energy complexity into growth opportunities for our partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable and affordable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Europe, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global leadership role accountable for how clients experience Kaluza day to day. Reporting to the VP Product &amp;amp; Tech Operations, you&#39;ll run three global functions and hold global accountability for client support and SLA performance across every client and region:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Support (incl. Incident &amp;amp; Problem Management)&lt;/strong&gt; - our client-facing service desk, owning triage and first-contact resolution, incident response and the client/product-team relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Platform Performance Assurance (KPPA)&lt;/strong&gt; - our neutral source of truth on platform performance, monitoring contractual SLAs and journey health per client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Product Specialists (KPS)&lt;/strong&gt; - Global retail-energy experts fixing broken journeys and operational gaps outside core platform coverage - driving an automation-by-default approach across all client brands&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead the practice / craft globally, set the strategy and standard for how each operates, and be the steady, credible presence clients and colleagues rely on - from a board-level service review to a live Sev1. Specifically, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Client Support, Incident &amp;amp; Problem Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own incident response end to end - severity, Major Incident command, root cause analysis, client communication and resolution within contractual SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage incoming support requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Problem Management, driving root-cause remediation and reducing the rate and duration of incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep support frictionless - shielding Product &amp;amp; Engineering from noise while closing the loop with clients, and making sure postmortems land as real systemic change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SLA &amp;amp; Performance Assurance (KPPA)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own global monitoring of contractual SLAs, KPIs and performance metrics as the agreed source of truth per client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the assurance loop - prevent, diagnose, treat - and coordinate performance reporting into Client Service Reviews and senior leadership, raising events when performance deviates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the line on data integrity (Datadog, Jira, Databricks) and embed Kaluza&#39;s Global Standard SLAs consistently across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial relationship, budget and roadmap with our key Operational tooling vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight and inputs on commercial conversations related to client reporting of performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Operational Resolution &amp;amp; Product Specialists (KPS)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the processes that fix broken journeys and coverage gaps across all of our client brands, including new clients as we grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance scheduled and ad-hoc work while keeping a safe, well-governed operational estate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed recurring manual interventions back to Product &amp;amp; Tech as signals for systemic fixes, and drive down manual effort through automation and AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across all three, you&#39;ll be genuinely AI-native - pushing AI into support, assurance and operations so each function does more with less - and you&#39;ll operate fluently at every altitude, staying neutral, evidence-led and a steady presence under pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideally you&#39;ll have/be:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An accomplished operations and support leader with a strong track record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder, not an executor - you define what good looks like, take full accountability, and go looking for what you need rather than waiting for a brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely AI-native - AI feels like leverage, and you actively push it into support, assurance and operational delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steady in ambiguity - nimble, sharp and decisive in a live incident, and a steady presence clients and colleagues rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced leading client support, service operations or service management at scale, ideally across multiple regions and enterprise clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in incident and problem management (severity and Major Incident command, postmortem culture, root-cause remediation) and in managing against contractual SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to understand, or quickly master, retail-energy operations and the operational reality of running processes around a platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will set you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with the data and tooling of assurance - SLAs, KPIs, observability (Datadog), Jira Service Management, and BI/warehouse tooling (Databricks/BigQuery) - enough to challenge the numbers, not just receive them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A credible partner to senior leadership and C-level clients, especially in a tense service review or live incident.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong people leader and coach across multiple disciplines, able to build a self-solving, high-performing culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to radical candour and customer centricity, with experience scaling a high-growth SaaS business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
