ox/account-executive-london-288357","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1792701617},{"slug":"senior-crm-executive-london-429801","company_name":"LemFi","title":"Senior CRM Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ambition has no passport.</strong> That belief is why <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lemfi.com/en-gb/careers">LemFi</a> exists. We're the financial engine for people the world wasn't built to serve, the millions who move countries to build something better and find the financial system hasn't caught up with them yet. We started with remittances: the money people send home to the people they love. Now we run multi-currency accounts, Savings, eSIMs and Credit. Because staying connected to home and building somewhere new are not two separate things. They never were.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>About the role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every product launch, promo and market entry at LemFi reaches customers through a campaign. As Senior CRM Executive, you'll build and ship them: email, push, in-app and SMS, across remittance, credit, savings and whatever we launch next. You take a brief and turn it into a live, tested, correctly targeted send - then tell us what it did.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You'll report to the Senior CRM Manager for Campaigns and work daily with Growth Managers, Product Marketing, Design and Compliance. This is a hands-on role with a high volume of sends and a high bar for getting each one right, because a wrong rate, a broken link or the wrong segment lands in a customer's pocket. Do it well and you'll be the person the rest of the business trusts to get their message out.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What you'll build and own</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and launch campaigns end to end in our marketing automation platform: segments, content, scheduling and send.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn campaign requests from across the business into clear builds, and push back when a brief doesn't hold up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">QA every send before it goes: targeting, personalisation, links, localisation and compliance sign-off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run A/B tests on subject lines, timing, offers and channels, and feed what wins into the next campaign.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the campaign calendar honest so customers aren't hit by five messages in one day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report on every campaign in numbers the team can act on: who received it, who converted, what it was worth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot what's repetitive in your own work and template or automate it.</p></li></ul><h3>Your experience</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1-3 years in CRM, email marketing or lifecycle, ideally in fintech, e-commerce or another high-frequency consumer product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on with a marketing automation platform (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Customer.io">Customer.io</a>, Braze, Iterable or similar) - you build the campaign yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Liquid and HTML for personalised, dynamic content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An eye for detail that catches the wrong segment or the broken link before the customer does.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable pulling your own numbers, with basic SQL or a BI tool such as Tableau, Looker, Amplitude or Mixpanel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bias to ship: you'd rather launch, measure and iterate than polish a brief.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable using AI tools to speed up copy variants, translations and QA checks.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lived experience or deep empathy with the life of our users - the millions who move countries to build something better.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Language skills in Italian, Portuguese, German, Mandarin, Wolof or Swahili.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running campaigns in a regulated or compliance-sensitive comms environment.</p></li></ul><h2><br />Why Join LemFi?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work here puts money back into families' pockets. That's the reward, and the weight of it. You'll take on some of the hardest problems in finance alongside people who do their best work when the stakes are real. We move fast and we expect a lot, because our customers can't afford for us to do otherwise. In return you get room to own real problems, global impact you can see, and a team that won't slow you down.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring grit and ownership and there's a place for them here. Ambition belongs here, come and show us yours.<br /><br />Follow us on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/lemfi/">LinkedIn</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/uselemfi/">Instagram</a> and if you haven't already, download the app on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/lemfi/id1533066809">App Store</a> or <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?hl=en&amp;id=com.lemonadeFinance.android">Google Play</a>. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Recruitment Agencies Notice</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">LemFi does not accept unsolicited CVs from recruitment agencies. We work only with agencies on our preferred supplier list, and only when we’ve asked them for their support. Any CVs sent to us outside this arrangement will not incur a fee.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lemfi/senior-crm-executive-london-429801","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792701617},{"slug":"technical-account-manager-emea-united-kingdom-414824","company_name":"Primer.io","title":"Technical Account Manager - EMEA","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An Introduction to Primer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Primer is the unified infrastructure for global payments. We give finance and payments teams the visibility and control to reduce complexity, improve performance, and capture more revenue - all from a single platform.<br /><br />Backed by Sofina, Peak XV Partners, ICONIQ, Tencent, Accel, and Balderton, we're building the payments layer the world's best companies rely on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://primer.io/the-primer-showcase">Watch our showcase &gt;</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.primer.io/blog/series-c">Read up on our $100m Series C</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://primer.io/careers">Learn more about our culture &gt;</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🔍 <strong>What will you be doing?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Payment performance &amp; risk mitigation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively monitor merchant integration and payment performance (authorisation rates, network tokenisation coverage, routing configuration) and flag risk before it becomes a problem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recommend and drive routing/NT/config changes, making the economic case (auth rate, cost) for why they matter.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integration debugging</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Root-cause complex technical issues hands-on, failures, SDK conflicts, webhook gaps, using logs, traces and API behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Loop in Primer engineering only when genuinely needed, rather than as a first resort.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical escalation ownership</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will act as an escalated contact during incidents that affect key merchants and require support from someone who has context on their particular payment stack. This sort of activity will be done in close contact with Support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">During and after incidents, you will be in touch with key merchants to deliver RCA’s, walk-through any impacts and offer recommendations to prevent future exposure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enablement &amp; solution design</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead technical deep-dives and solution design sessions when a merchant adopts a new PSP connector, payment method, or unreleased Primer product as a design partner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the expectation gap through rollout and feed structured, usable feedback back to Product and Engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proactive technical reviews</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run recurring technical integration reviews (e.g. quarterly) with each merchant's engineering/payments stakeholders, covering integration health, optimisation opportunities, and risk, independently of any commercial QBR run in-partnership with the AM.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regulatory &amp; compliance navigation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate changes in card scheme rules or regional regulation (e.g. BNPL rules, PCI requirements) into a concrete technical plan for each affected merchant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>👀 <strong>What we’d love to see:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep, hands-on technical ability:</strong> comfortable reading API logs and traces, debugging integration issues directly, and writing basic scripts/SQL to investigate an issue — a real technical peer to a merchant's engineers, not a relationship manager with technical vocabulary.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience in a technical, merchant/customer-facing role:</strong> Technical Account Manager, Solutions Engineer, Support Engineer, Customer Success Manager (technical focused), Implementation Specialist, in payments, fintech, or e-commerce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong understanding of APIs, webhooks, and SDKs:</strong> The ability to explain technical flows clearly to both engineers and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A proactive operating style:</strong> Comfortable identifying and surfacing risk before being asked, not just responding to tickets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Confidence and credibility presenting technical material:</strong> Comfortable presenting to senior technical stakeholders (VP Engineering, Head of Payments) at enterprise merchants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable owning ambiguity:</strong> Coordinating across Primer's engineering, product, and support teams without heavy oversight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Direct experience with payments infrastructure:</strong> network tokenisation, PSP connectors/routing, or card scheme mechanics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design-partner support experience:</strong> exposure to beta or early-access product rollouts across key merchants.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h3>What this role is explicitly not</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a renewals or commercial negotiation owner, that's the Account Manager.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a support/ticket-routing role, the bar is proactive technical ownership, not reactive Q&amp;A.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>✅ A typical interview process</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An initial intro call with a Talent Partner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interview with the Hiring Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge Stage - Contextualised to the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A final, values-alignment interview</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What's the culture like at Primer?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We're building a culture where people can do their best work and be proud of the impact they have. You'll be working with people who are mission-driven, smart, and reflective, and who are genuinely invested in building exceptional products and delivering success for our merchants.<br /><br />We work remotely, and have done since day one. We believe that building a successful, profitable company goes beyond proximity. We invest in our relationships through great remote working practices and thoughtfully designed face-to-face time, including workations, our annual company retreat, and access to co-working spaces across most major cities.<br /><br />The work is challenging. Scaleups are a challenge, and building category-defining products is a challenge. But there's a meaningful difference between a challenge and a struggle. At Primer, the right challenge comes with the right support: strong onboarding, a collaborative environment, and a team that is genuinely invested in your success. It's never something you face alone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌍 We are fully remote and globally distributed; and have been since day one<br />💰 Competitive share options<br />🌴 Flexible holiday, with 25 days minimum to be taken<br />🗣️ Co-working space access across major cities<br />📅 Workations &amp; Company Retreat<br />💻 The best equipment for your role<br />🏠 £500 towards your home office setup<br />🔎 Generous learning budget<br />🏥 Private Medical Insurance<br />📈 A broad set of additional perks and benefits (<em>depending on location)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Don’t meet every single requirement?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Primer, we're dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive, and authentic workplace. If you're excited about this role but your experience doesn't align perfectly with every qualification listed, we encourage you to apply. You may be the right candidate for this or other roles.<br /><br />Primer is committed to the equal treatment of all current and prospective employees and adopts a zero-tolerance approach to discrimination, regardless of age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, pregnancy and maternity, race or ethnicity, religion or belief, gender identity, marriage and civil partnership, or any other background or belief.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/primerio/technical-account-manager-emea-united-kingdom-414824","tags":["Merchant Experience"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792701616},{"slug":"commercial-london-45456","company_name":"Axle Careers","title":"Commercial","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1