n Europe.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>⭐️ Your role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relationships &amp; Presence</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and maintain trusted, long-term relationships</strong> with the organizations that represent employees and members across the sectors that matter to Alan (unions, federations, and the structures that convene them).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Map the ecosystem, prioritize interlocutors</strong>, and design the engagement strategy at confederal, federal and branch level.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Alan in federations, working groups, congrès and paritariste institutions</strong> where our sector’s future is discussed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the credible consistent Alan voice social partners recognise</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partnership with Alan's Enterprise &amp; Public Sector work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a partner to our teams</strong> serving large private employers and public sector clients, briefing them on the social partners context and how Alan’s offer speaks to their priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Introduce the right contacts</strong> at the right moment in the commercial cycle, turning Alan’s ecosystem relationships into concrete commercial leverage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Share Alan’s content </strong>with social partners to help them assess Alan on its merits and form their own view.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sector Engagement &amp; Anticipation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Follow the dialogue</strong> at branch level and across the paritariste ecosystem and turn that understanding into internal clarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Alan in the federations and working groups</strong> where our sector's future is discussed, contributing a constructive and recognizable voice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a sharp, early internal voice on where social dialogue is heading</strong> and on the implications for Alan's strategy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build &amp; Scale</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Knowledge base</strong>: Build and maintain a knowledge library on social partner positions, branch agreements, and paritariste institutions shared with Enterprise and Public Sector deal teams to increase win rates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Framework &amp; tools</strong>: Implement processes and AI tools to improve the quality and efficiency of our social partner engagement and documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration</strong>: Share best practices with the broader Enterprise &amp; Public Sector team and contribute proven methodologies to their scaled commercial operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Market intelligence</strong>: Provide competitive intelligence on how social partners and competitors position themselves in our key markets.</p></li></ul><h1><br /> ⭐ Is it you we’re looking for?</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ll be a great fit for the Union Relations Lead role at Alan if you:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have at least 8 years of total experience in social partner relations</strong>: in a union organization, a branch federation, a paritariste institution, or in an external affairs role at a mutelle, IP or insurer</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have legitimate credibility at federation level:</strong> ability to engage f