ce across portfolios.</p></li><li><p>Write runbooks so that operational knowledge is shared, not held by one person.</p></li></ul><h2>The impact you will have</h2><ul><li><p>Customers receive optimization proposals and simulations that are correct and delivered on time.</p></li><li><p>Issues are caught before customers see them, not after.</p></li><li><p>The time the ML team spends on operational work goes down measurably, because recurring steps are automated.</p></li><li><p>Customer Success can trust automated optimization and simulation results without checking them by hand.</p></li></ul><h2>Your experience and skills</h2><ul><li><p>Recently completed Master's degree in Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p>Solid Python skills, including pandas and NumPy, and comfort working with SQL.</p></li><li><p>Good understanding of statistics and basic machine learning concepts such as regression, model evaluation and overfitting.</p></li><li><p>A careful, structured way of working: you check results before you share them and you document what you do.</p></li><li><p>Ability to explain technical findings clearly to non-technical colleagues.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English, spoken and written, is a must.</p></li></ul><h2>Bonus points</h2><ul><li><p>Experience with optimization methods, for example constrained or non-convex optimization.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Marketing Mix Modeling, attribution or digital advertising metrics.</p></li><li><p>Experience with data pipelines, scheduled jobs or monitoring tools.</p></li><li><p>Experience with Git, Docker and cloud environments.</p></li><li><p>Fluent in German or Italian.</p></li></ul><h2>Your future work life</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Your work directly influences how enterprise marketers allocate their budgets.</p></li><li><p><strong>Responsibility:</strong> You own the quality of a defined part of our automation from day one, with a personal 