&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/globalizationpartners/field-account-executive-emea-421503","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792702535},{"slug":"senior-engineer-product-intelligence-materials-engineering-chemistry-thin-film-design-418449","company_name":"Asm","title":"Senior Engineer Product Intelligence (Materials Engineering – Chemistry & Thin Film Design)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step into a career with ASM, where cutting edge technology meets collaborative culture. &lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For over 55 years ASM has been ahead of what’s next, at the forefront of innovation and what’s technologically possible. With more than 4,500 ASMers representing 70 nationalities, our people and our advanced semiconductor devices are playing a crucial role in trends such as 5G, cloud computing, AI, and autonomous driving.  But&amp;nbsp;we’re more than just a tech company. We value diversity, inclusion and sustainability as we strive to make a positive impact on the world.&amp;nbsp; Our development programs help support your growth, shaping your future and pushing the boundaries of innovation to unleash potential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Engineer Product Intelligence (Materials Engineering – Chemistry &amp;amp; Thin Film Design) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek a Senior AI/ML Engineer to develop practical, science-grounded ML solutions for materials science and semiconductor applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and support AI models and workflows for relevant chemical systems for thin film development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model &amp;amp; embedded known physics &amp;amp; mechanisms to ensure accurate model output and turnaround time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use of SoTA GenAI frameworks for materials science and ML tools deliver applications that acceleration R&amp;amp;D workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data pipelines to extract required data from multi-modal data sources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with software &amp;amp; data science engineers to deliver reproducible pipelines, dashboards, APIs and decision-support tools for R&amp;amp;D and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers define modelling standards and communicate across AI/ML, chemistry, materials and semiconductor teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD or MSc with strong expertise in CS, Data Science, Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry, Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building ML models, tools and frameworks for materials science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years’ experience in applying AI/ML or computational methods (MLIPs, DFT, MD, kMC, etc.) to complex scientific or engineering problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience on atomistic to feature scale AI tools &amp;amp; frameworks – generative models, deterministic models, Stochastic models, active learning/reinforcement learning Python, PyTorch/TensorFlow/JAX/scikit-learn&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate physical, chemical and engineering challenges into practical AI/ML workflows for materials engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI/ML experience in semiconductor materials engineering or in relevant chemistry/materials system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who will thrive in this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate bridges advanced AI/ML engineering, materials engineering/process R&amp;amp;D, and eager to solve problems that make an impact to the users&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply today to be part of what’s next.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make the tech that enables the chips in devices which improve lives around the world. We do this with an eye to the future, pushing the boundaries of what’s possible through cutting-edge innovation, and driving the next wave of technological breakthroughs that shape how we live, work, and connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;To learn more about ASM, find us at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.asm.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;asm.com&lt;/a&gt; and&amp;nbsp;on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/asm/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/ASMOfficialCompany&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/asmofficialcompany/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram,&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/ASMofficialco&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;X&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/c/ASM_Official&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;ASM is an equal opportunity employer and considers qualified applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, age, nationality, social or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, gender, gender identify or expression, marital status, pregnancy, political affiliation, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/asm/senior-engineer-product-intelligence-materials-engineering-chemistry-thin-film-design-418449","tags":["SU3.Platform Common Modules"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792702533},{"slug":"international-expansion-netherlands-379837","company_name":"Axle Careers","title":"International Expansion","description":"<h2>About Us </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Axle Energy, we’re building the infrastructure that will underpin the decarbonised energy system. Our software moves energy usage to times when electricity is cheap and green, by controlling vehicle charging, heating systems, inverters and home batteries. We control hundreds of thousands of energy assets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building in a legacy industry and moving gigawatt-hours of electrons in the real world, but we operate at lightning speed, and we’re growing the team to meet customer demand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proud to be supported by world-leading investors, including Energize Capital and Accel. Read more about what we’re building <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.axle.energy/blog/analysis/power-of-the-home"><strong>here</strong></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We’re looking for a commercially sharp, highly autonomous operator to drive Axle’s commercial success in the Dutch market.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axle has quickly become the leader in our operational markets, and we’re now looking to expand our reach internationally. Our goal is to become the go-to platform for energy flexibility globally, and we’re hiring the person to make that happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role will assess Axle’s participation in Dutch markets and business models from first principles: diving deep into regulations, modelling revenue-per-asset, and trialling new propositions at pace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You speak Dutch and fluent English. Other European languages will also be an asset.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you will be doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning new customer acquisition end-to-end, from first conversation through to commercial close, setting our partners up to generate meaningful revenue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High-level strategy development, defining and executing Axle’s international expansion plans, and assessing the commercial value of Dutch markets and business models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diving deep into policy and regulations, understanding how market access works and what needs doing to achieve it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developing the zero-to-one of the business through partnerships with key stakeholders. You’ll be jumping on the phone (and eventually, getting on the ground) with grid operators, utilities/retailers and potential clients to create and disprove hypotheses as quickly as possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a conduit between partners and engineering teams creating fast, structured feedback loops that help translate field insights into meaningful product enhancements.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As such, we are looking for a “full-stack operator” who can process highly technical information, ramp up commercial value, and accelerate us into new markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might have previous experience in one or more of the activities above, but we are more interested in your growth potential than your domain-specific expertise. We are looking for people who have built things, developed new relationships, and helped get big projects over the line in complex environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to repeatedly deliver first-of-a-kind projects across the world, become a domain expert, and work at the bleeding edge of global electrification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What’s in it for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a 12 month fixed-term contract. Compensation is highly competitive and dependent on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with a deliberately flat structure and aim to keep pay equitable across the company, with a 1:1 median ratio between founder and team compensation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual retreats to strengthen team connection &amp; shared purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be based in the Netherlands. To maximise collaboration, we ask that you spend ~1 week per month working from our London office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to directly shape the future of energy markets and accelerate the transition to a low-carbon world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are <em>extremely</em> keen to build a diverse team, and we’re particularly eager to hear from candidates who don't fit the traditional role stereotypes. If you’re motivated by our mission, please do reach out, even if you feel you might not ‘check all the boxes’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Interview process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take-home exercise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview (in-person)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, references, and welcome to the team!</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/axle-careers/international-expansion-netherlands-379837","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1792701617},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-payments-amsterdam-298606","company_name":"Airwallex","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Payments","description":"<h2><strong>About Airwallex</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is the AI-native financial operating system for a real-time, intelligent economy. More than 675,000 businesses, including McLaren Racing, Qantas, SHEIN, and TikTok, use us, directly or through our platform partners, to run their financial operations or build and monetize financial products of their own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in Melbourne in 2015 to build the infrastructure global commerce runs on. We're the regulated backbone behind global payments: not by accident, but by design. A decade plus, 85+ licenses, and a financial infrastructure spanning North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're co-headquartered in San Francisco and Singapore, with more than 2,700 people across 27 offices. We hire builders with founder-level energy, people who move fast with good judgment, dig in with real curiosity, and make calls from first principles rather than waiting to be told what to do. Read our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.airwallex.com/en-us/operating-principles"> <u>operating principles</u></a> to see it in full.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h3>How you'll make impact</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll define the technical direction for Airwallex’s Payments Platform, lead architecture decisions and build highly reliable, high-volume distributed systems that directly affect merchant experience and business outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll design and build scalable backend services, REST APIs, event-driven systems and integration components within a microservices architecture, connecting with our React frontend. You’ll drive complex initiatives across payment gateways, acquiring, issuing, card networks and local payment methods, while partnering with product, business, infrastructure and external engineering teams to turn merchant needs into technical solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll raise the engineering bar through architectural reviews, thoughtful approaches to technical debt, strong design practices, code quality, testing, observability, reliability and mentorship.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What we're looking for</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essentials</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">10+ years of software engineering experience, including Staff-level technical leadership or equivalent ownership of complex backend systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience designing and operating high-volume distributed systems, preferably in payments, fintech, commerce or financial infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recent hands-on experience with Java or Kotlin and Spring or Spring Boot.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert experience building REST APIs, backend microservices, Kafka-based event streams and distributed data stores such as Cassandra, Hazelcast, Oracle Coherence or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with cloud platforms such as GCP or AWS, plus Docker and Kubernetes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong familiarity with observability and operational tooling such as New Relic, StatsD, ELK, Datadog, Prometheus or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven ability to lead projects from concept to production, with a focus on quality, testing, reliability and maintainability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills and the ability to influence across engineering, product and business stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building payment gateways, acquiring platforms, issuing platforms or payment acceptance infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating major card networks such as Visa and Mastercard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with local payment methods such as iDEAL, Klarna, Trustly or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with authorisation, capture, refunds, chargebacks, settlement, reconciliation, fraud, risk or PCI/compliance workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience mentoring senior engineers and leading cross-team technical initiatives.</p></li></ul><h3>You'll thrive here if</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable owning the roadmap yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the outcome and you don’t wait for permission to fix what’s broken.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable with ambiguity. Give you a problem, not a prescription, and you’ll run with it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate clearly and directly across cultures, and you’re thoughtful about how context shifts meaning across borders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable operating across time zones with a globally distributed team, including colleagues based in APAC and EMEA.</p></li></ul><h3>Learn more about your team</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payments Platform at Airwallex builds the infrastructure that turns global payment complexity into reliable, scalable payment experiences, helping businesses accept and process money across markets with less friction. The challenge is balancing performance, reliability, local complexity, and commercial outcomes in the same system, where small improvements can materially affect conversion and failures are immediately visible. You'll do well here if you're thoughtful, pragmatic, and motivated by making complex problems feel simple to customers. If you want to build the platform that makes payments work seamlessly for businesses around the world, this is the team at the center of that mission.</p><h2><strong>Applicant Safety Policy: Fraud and Third-Party Recruiters</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To protect you from recruitment scams, please be aware that Airwallex will not ask for bank details, sensitive ID numbers (i.e. passport), or any form of payment during the application or interview process. All official communication will come from an @</em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://airwallex.com"><em>airwallex.com</em></a><em> email address. Please apply only through </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://careers.airwallex.com"><em><u>careers.airwallex.com</u></em></a><em> or our official LinkedIn page.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Airwallex does not accept unsolicited resumes from search firms/recruiters.  Airwallex will not pay any fees to search firms/recruiters if a candidate is submitted by a search firm/recruiter unless an agreement has been entered into with respect to specific open position(s).  Search firms/recruiters submitting resumes to Airwallex on an unsolicited basis shall be deemed to accept this condition, regardless of any other provision to the contrary.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We value diversity and anyone seeking employment at Airwallex is considered based on merit, qualifications, competence and talent. We don’t regard color, religion, race, national origin, sexual orientation, ancestry, citizenship, sex, marital or family status, disability, gender, or any other legally protected status when making our hiring decisions. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/airwallex/staff-software-engineer-payments-amsterdam-298606","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"NL - Amsterdam","created_at":1792701616},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-payments-platform-amsterdam-175739","company_name":"Airwallex","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Payments Platform","description":"<h2><strong>About Airwallex</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is the AI-native financial operating system for a real-time, intelligent economy. More than 675,000 businesses, including McLaren Racing, Qantas, SHEIN, and TikTok, use us, directly or through our platform partners, to run their financial operations or build and monetize financial products of their own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in Melbourne in 2015 to build the infrastructure global commerce runs on. We're the regulated backbone behind global payments: not by accident, but by design. A decade plus, 85+ licenses, and a financial infrastructure spanning North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're co-headquartered in San Francisco and Singapore, with more than 2,700 people across 27 offices. We hire builders with founder-level energy, people who move fast with good judgment, dig in with real curiosity, and make calls from first principles rather than waiting to be told what to do. Read our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" hr