evraagstukken? Dan past deze rol bij je.</p><p>Als Embedded Software Designer werk je binnen multidisciplinaire ontwikkelomgevingen aan innovatieve projecten met hoge kwaliteitsnormen. Je bent betrokken bij het volledige ontwikkelproces: van requirements en architectuur tot implementatie en testing. Je werkt samen met ervaren engineers en krijgt volop ruimte om jouw technische kennis verder uit te bouwen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p>Als Embedded Software Designer ben je verantwoordelijk voor het ontwerpen, bouwen en verbeteren van embedded softwareoplossingen. Je stelt technische architecturen op, ontwikkelt software in C en/of C++, en test de werking van systemen. Daarnaast integreer je verschillende softwaremodules en zorg je voor duidelijke documentatie.</p><p>Je werkt aan projecten binnen Embedded Linux, RTOS of OS-less omgevingen en schakelt regelmatig met collega’s uit andere disciplines.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Hoe je impact maakt</strong></h2><p>Je bent een belangrijke schakel binnen het ontwikkelteam en zorgt ervoor dat softwareoplossingen betrouwbaar, efficiënt en toekomstbestendig zijn. Door jouw inzet verlopen projecten soepel en worden technische uitdagingen succesvol opgelost. Je draagt bij aan innovatieve producten en de groei van het team.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat je van ons krijgt</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Salaris: €3.750 - €5.500 bruto p/m, afhankelijk van ervaring</p></li><li><p>Goede begeleiding en een duidelijk inwerktraject</p></li><li><p>Werken in een professioneel en technisch sterk team</p></li><li><p>Hybride werken met goede thuiswerkfaciliteiten</p></li><li><p>Pensioenregeling en goede verzekeringen</p></li><li><p>Mobiliteitsregeling: NS Businesscard, reiskostenvergoeding of auto van de zaak</p></li><li><p>Veel ruimte voor opleiding en persoonlijke ontwikkeling</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat het jou oplevert</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Veel afwisseling in uitdagende technische projecten</p></li><li><p>Werken met moderne technologieën en systemen</p></li><li><p>Snel groeien in kennis en verantwoordelijkheid</p></li><li><p>Samenwerken in een hecht team van specialisten</p></li><li><p>Een rol waarin je direct impact maakt</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Takenverdeling</strong></h2><p>25% Implementatie</p><p>25% Architectuur &amp; Design</p><p>20% Requirements Engineering</p><p>15% Integratie</p><p>15% Documentatie</p> <br> <h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Hard skills</h3><ul><li><p>Hbo- of Wo-werk- en denkniveau</p></li><li><p>Afgeronde opleiding richting Technische Informatica of vergelijkbaar</p></li><li><p>Minimaal 5 jaar ervaring in softwareontwikkeling</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met C++ en/of C</p></li><li><p>Kennis van Embedded Linux, RTOS of OS-less systemen</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met Agile, TDD, OOAD of vergelijkbare methodieken</p></li><li><p>Kennis van communicatiebussen zoals SPI, UART, I2C en CAN</p></li><li><p>Je bent woonachtig in de regio of bereid om binnen een straal van circa 60 minuten te reizen.</p></li><li><p>Je spreekt en schrijft uitstekend Nederlands en Engels</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="heading-quartary electric-purple mb-10">Nice to have</h3><ul><li><p>Ervaring met het coachen van junior collega’s </p></li><li><p>Ervaring met Jira, Confluence, Git of QT</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Soft skills</h3><ul><li><p>Teamspeler</p></li><li><p>Analytisch sterk</p></li><li><p>Proactief</p></li><li><p>Communicatief vaardig</p></li><li><p>Leergierig</p></li><li><p>Oplossingsgericht</p></li><li><p>Nauwkeurig</p></li><li><p>Gedreven</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gradematch/embedded-software-designer-eindhoven-21636","tags":["Software Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"software-test-engineer-eindhoven-229483","company_name":"GradeMatch","title":"Software Test Engineer","description":"<h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>De uitdaging</strong></h2><p class="isSelectedEnd">Wij zoeken per direct een Software Test Engineer voor ons zusterbedrijf Veynex in de regio Limburg / Brabant. Haal jij voldoening uit het waarborgen van softwarekwaliteit en het continu verbeteren van testprocessen? Dan past deze rol bij je.</p><p>Als Software Test Engineer werk je samen met product owners, domeinexperts en ontwikkelteams aan het opstellen van heldere en effectieve testplannen. Je zorgt ervoor dat software op alle niveaus van de stack grondig wordt getest en zet actief in op testautomatisering. Je bent betrokken bij het volledige testproces en draagt bij aan het verbeteren van softwarekwaliteit binnen multidisciplinaire ontwikkelomgevingen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>Wat ga je doen?</h2><p class="isSelectedEnd">Als Software Test Engineer ben je verantwoordelijk voor het ontwerpen, uitvoeren en verbeteren van testprocessen. Je stelt testplannen op, scherpt requirements aan waar nodig en zorgt ervoor dat tests efficiënt worden uitgevoerd.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">Je gebruikt scripts en geautomatiseerde testtools om software te testen, valideert testresultaten en rapporteert bevindingen aan stakeholders. Daarnaast ontwikkel je verificatieplannen, kwaliteitsborgingsprocedures en teststrategieën. Door continu te zoeken naar verbeteringen in processen en automatisering help je het team om softwarekwaliteit sprint na sprint te verhogen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>Hoe je impact maakt</h2><p class="isSelectedEnd">Je bent een cruciale schakel in het leveren van betrouwbare en hoogwaardige software. Door jouw nauwkeurigheid worden fouten vroegtijdig opgespoord en opgelost, waardoor producten robuuster, gebruiksvriendelijker en toekomstbestendiger worden. Je draagt direct bij aan de kwaliteit van softwareproducten én aan de verdere professionalisering van het ontwikkelproces.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>Wat je van ons krijgt</h2><ul><li><p>Salaris: €2.350 – €4.500 bruto p/m, afhankelijk van ervaring en fit met de functie</p></li><li><p>Flexibele werkweek van 32 tot 40 uur</p></li><li><p>Goede pensioenregeling</p></li><li><p>Verzekeringen bij arbeidsongeschiktheid</p></li><li><p>Hybride werken met goede thuiswerkfaciliteiten</p></li><li><p>Mobiliteitsregeling: NS Businesscard, reiskostenvergoeding of auto van de zaak</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h2>Wat het jou oplevert</h2><ul><li><p>Veel ruimte voor opleiding en persoonlijke ontwikkeling</p></li><li><p>Werken binnen een professionele en technisch uitdagende omgeving</p></li><li><p>Veel afwisseling in uitdagende softwareprojecten</p></li><li><p>Werken met moderne testtools en automatiseringsoplossingen</p></li><li><p>Snel groeien in kennis en verantwoordelijkheid</p></li><li><p>Samenwerken in multidisciplinaire Agile-teams</p></li><li><p>Direct impact maken op de kwaliteit van innovatieve softwareproducten</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2>Taakverdeling</h2><p class="isSelectedEnd">40% Ontwerpen, ontwikkelen, onderhouden &amp; valideren van testoplossingen</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">20% Uitvoeren van geautomatiseerde en handmatige testscripts</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">15% Valideren en rapporteren van testresultaten</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">15% Ontwikkelen van software verificatieplannen, teststrategieën en kwaliteitsborgingsprocedures</p><p>10% Testprocedures documenteren en onderhouden</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h3>Hard skills</h3><ul><li><p>Hbo- of Wo-werk- en denkniveau</p></li><li><p>Afgeronde opleiding richting Technische Informatica of vergelijkbaar</p></li><li><p>Minimaal 1 jaar relevante werkervaring als Software Test Engineer, bij voorkeur in SAFe, Agile of DevOps omgeving.</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met testtools en testframeworks zoals Selenium, Cypress en Cucumber</p></li><li><p>Kennis van testmethodieken zoals CAT, TMAP en ISTQB</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met Continuous Integration en Continuous Delivery (CI/CD)</p></li><li><p>Kennis van werkmethodieken zoals DevOps, Agile/Scrum en/of Kanban</p></li><li><p>Je beheerst de Nederlandse en Engelse taal uitstekend (mondeling en schriftelijk)</p></li><li><p>Je bent woonachtig in de regio of bereid om binnen een straal van circa 60 minuten te reizen</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul><li><p>Ervaring met Python</p></li><li><p>Affiniteit met elektronica</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met Jira, Confluence, Git en/of Qt</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3>Soft skills</h3><ul><li><p>Teamspeler</p></li><li><p>Proactief</p></li><li><p>Doorzetter</p></li><li><p>Communicatief</p></li><li><p>Analytisch</p></li><li><p>Nauwkeurig</p></li><li><p>Enthousiast</p></li><li><p>Probleemoplosser</p></li><li><p>Leergierig</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gradematch/software-test-engineer-eindhoven-229483","tags":["Software Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Eindhoven, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1792669911}],"links":{"first":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=1","last":null,"prev":null,"next":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=2"},"meta":{"current_page":1,"current_page_url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api?page=1","from":1,"path":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/api/job-board-api","per_page":300,"to":300,"terms":"This is a free public API for jobs, please do not abuse. I would appreciate linking back to the site. By using the API, you agree to the terms of service present on Arbeitnow.com","info":"Jobs are updated every hour and order by the `created_at` timestamp. Use `?page=` to paginate. Read more information here: https://www.arbeitnow.com/blog/job-board-api"}}

{"data":[{"slug":"customer-success-key-account-management-vollzeit-100-remote-berlin-318206","company_name":"Lemontaps","title":"Customer Success & Key Account Management (Vollzeit) - 100% remote","description":"<p>Hey! 👋</p><p>Du liebst Herausforderungen und packst gerne selbst an? Du magst es Verantwortung zu tragen und bei einem schnell wachstenden Startup einen Bereich von klein auf selbst mitaufzubauen?</p><p>Dann könnte diese Stelle genau das Richtige für dich sein!</p><h2>Aufgaben</h2><p>Als Customer Success Manager:in bist du in unserem Team die Ansprechperson für unsere Kunden. Deine Aufgabe ist es, unsere Kunden in allen Belangen zu beraten, zu unterstützen und ganz wichtig – glücklich zu machen.</p><p>Gemeinsam mit dem Kunden sorgst du dafür, dass das Erlebnis mit der digitalen Visitenkarten-Software ein voller Erfolg wird.</p><p>Du..</p><ul><li><p>führst Onboardings unseren Kunden (KMUs) durch</p></li><li><p>hälst regelmäßige Checkups Calls und versuchst dadurch die Active Usage Rate zu erhöhen und Churn zu vermeiden</p></li><li><p>hilfst Upselling-Potentiale bei Kunden zu identifizieren</p></li><li><p>identifizierst neue potenzielle Use Cases auf Basis des Kunden Feedbacks</p></li><li><p>fungierst als Ansprechpartner und Schnittstelle zwischen Kunde und unserem Produktteam und trägst damit einen wesentlichen Teil zur Weiterentwicklung unseres Produkts bei</p></li><li><p>baust die Success Stories unserer Kunden weiter aus</p></li><li><p>konzeptionierst Einführungsunterlagen und Schulungsmaterialien für unsere Kunden</p></li></ul><p>Zur Info: Vorerst wirst du die einzige Customer Success Managerin / der einzige Customer Success Manager sein. Es gibt jedoch bereits ein paar etablierte Prozesse, sodass du nicht bei null starten musst, sondern auf bestehende Strukturen aufbauen kannst. Es besteht also die Möglichkeit, dass du in ein paar Monaten weitere Personen einlernen kannst und den Bereich ausbauen kannst.</p><h2>Qualifikation</h2><ul><li><p>Erfahrung im Customer Success (2 Jahre mindestens) bei einer B2B SaaS Lösung</p></li><li><p>Flexibilität, Organisationstalent sowie eine hohe Hands-On-Mentalität</p></li><li><p>Gute Kommunikationsskills</p></li><li><p>Sehr gute Deutsch- und Englischkenntnisse</p></li><li><p>Starke Analytische- und Organisationsskills machen dich aus</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits</h2><p>Die Möglichkeit den Bereich aufzubauen, mitzugestalten und vom ersten Tag Verantwortung zu übernehmen</p><ul><li><p>Flexible Arbeitszeiten, angenehmes Arbeitsumfeld in einem kleinen, leistungsstarken Team</p></li><li><p>Fully remote möglich</p></li><li><p>Du kannst zwischen unserem Büro in Berlin, Home Office und Remote-Arbeit wechseln.</p></li><li><p>Firmeneigene Geräte und Arbeitsmittel werden bezahlt, ausgesucht nach deiner Präferenz (Laptop, Bildschirm, ...)</p></li><li><p>Regelmäßige Team Events in ganz Deutschland</p></li><li><p>STEILE Lernkurve durch Gründer:innen, Partner:innen, unseren großen Kundenstamm und mehr</p></li><li><p>Make a big difference: Sorge dafür das Lemontaps ein erstklassiges Produkt mit begeisterten Kunden ist</p></li><li><p>Arbeite in einem Unternehmen, in dem wir Vielfalt schätzen und uns dafür einsetzen, ein inklusives Umfeld für alle Mitarbeiter zu schaffen und zu erhalten.</p></li><li><p>Sei Teil eines schnell wachsenden Teams in einem vielversprechenden Markt.</p></li></ul><p>Wir freuen uns Dich kennenzulernen.</p><p>Anna und Raji :)</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/lemontaps/customer-success-key-account-management-vollzeit-100-remote-berlin-318206","tags":["Customer Service"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792681298},{"slug":"senior-ehs-advisor-finsterwalde-136543","company_name":"Kirbygroupengineering","title":"Senior EHS Advisor | Finsterwalde","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Permanent position available with a considerable portfolio of works for the next 5+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To build your career by assisting in the delivery of ‘leading edge’ engineering projects.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To work with a vibrant, agile and multi-functional team in delivering projects on time, safely, to budget and to the required quality standards.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To benefit from Kirby’s Career Development Programmes that will enhance your leadership capability.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To work with the best.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent package on offer with room for negotiations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kirby Group Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an international multi-disciplinary engineering services contractor and leading provider of high-value engineering services to a number of ‘blue chip’ companies. Operating across Ireland, the UK, Europe and South Africa, Kirby has become the engineering service provider of choice in growth segments such as pharmaceuticals, data centres and power transmission and distribution. Our culture is innovative, collaborative and performance focused. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to grow and develop in a company committed to developing talent and rewarding performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The role of the Senior EHS Advisor is to provide Environment, Health and Safety guidance working with the project team. You will implement and maintain the Kirby management system for the project.&amp;nbsp; The role is to coordinate all EHS Matters within various Project Management Teams and to report constructively all EHS matters to Project Manager. Under the direction of the EHS Manager, the EHS Advisor will be responsible for providing support to the Project Managers, supervisors and workers. This position will provide leadership and coordination of the day-to-day EHS requirements of the assigned project(s).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Functions of the Senior EHS Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide advice, guidance, support and instruction in all EHS matters to management, safety representatives and employees (including where applicable to sub-contractors, suppliers and visitors to sites).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership through good example. Be proactive in all matters concerning the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify training needs, report requirements to project team and carry out training as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit and inspect projects, agree and prepare achievable corrective and preventive action plans towards compliance to and continual improvement of the EHS on the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on business EHS risks, KPIs and trends accurately with data and recommend constructive actions towards continuous improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure incidents are reported and investigations are carried out in a thorough and professional manner in order to identify root causes and corrective and preventive action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that Site EHS Plans, RAMS and other associated site documents are updated and compliant with statutory and other requirements and that they are reviewed on a continuous basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EHS Advisor Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reports to EHS Manager, Site Managers/Supervisors and Project Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is conversant with the contents of the Kirby safety statement, environment manual, risk assessments, aspects &amp;amp; impacts, legislation and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides advice, guidance, instruction and training in all EHS matters to management, safety representatives and employees (including where applicable to sub-contractors, suppliers and visitors to sites).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carries out internal audits and site inspections in conjunction with Site Management, recommends corrective actions, improvements and document findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares in conjunction with site management team a project specific EHS Plan, induction and Risk Assessment Method Statements (RAMS). These shall be compiled and agreed prior to work commencing and ongoing through lookaheads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures that the project specific EHS Plan, induction and RAMS are up to date, reviewed periodically and communicated to all relevant persons (including clients, Main Contractor, other contractors, visitors and others who may be affected by that work).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visits each new project, sets up the necessary site safety files (Series 500 &amp;amp; 600), registers, abstracts of regulations, posters, SEOR program, etc., and ensures that site establishment complies with the legislation, client regulations and company regulations as a minimum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviews Contractor Appointments and ensures that correct appointment is carried out and that only competent contractors are used on projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduces and implements effective measures aimed at the prevention of incidents at work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reports on incidents and/or dangerous occurrences should they occur to the EHS Manager, Project Manager and Site Managers as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reports on areas of concern to the relevant party for correction. Persistent and serious areas of concern are to be reported immediately to line management as per (1) above. Retains evidence of communications with relevant parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carries out incident investigation in conjunction with site management, establishes cause of incident or dangerous occurrence and recommends method for future avoidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audits the company site safety file, (Series 500 &amp;amp; 600), makes sure that hazards/risks are regularly assessed, that control measures are implemented, that inspections are carried out and that all incidents are reported, investigated and closed out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepares Monthly KPI Report for their projects, issues monthly return of Site Visit Schedule, SEORs, KPIs, violations to the EHS Manager and the Business Unit Manager. Issues new SDS to EHS Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides training and information to the workforce using appropriate training aids and media as required. Issues records of training to HR to update the training matrix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attends the regional EHS Coordination Meeting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attends the EHS meeting with the Business Unit Manager, as required (1 per region).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attends internal and external site meetings as required – safety meetings, coordination meetings etc...&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implements and promotes the company Incentive Scheme on all projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arranges distribution and maintenance of fully stocked first aid boxes on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors P.P.E usage and advises site management on type of protective equipment required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issues non-conformances, commendations and disciplinary warnings both written and verbal if required or instructed to do so.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Necessary requirement of the EHS Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ Years’ Experience in similar industry. Knowledge of Electrical, Mechanical and CSA preferably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diploma to NFQ 8 in Occupational H&amp;amp;S. Certificate to NFQ 6 Environmental Management. Safe Pass, (CSCS (UK)), Train the Trainer, First Aid, Training Instructor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal ISO14000 and ISO45000 system auditor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Construction Regulations and CDM roles, with experience working with sub-contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with EHS Management Systems, safety schemes and tendering e.g. ISOs, Achilles, SSiPs etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, through presentations, reports, written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with Kirby / client / main contractor Safety and Project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well within strict deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be able to prepare Audits and EHS reports, to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to date with Legislation, Standards, Guidance, Advice and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive in identifying positive and negative acts, ability to follow through with realistic corrective and preventive actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and coordinate incident investigations and utilise root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IOSH Member or Equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on this role, or other Construction / Engineering opportunities across Ireland, the UK, Europe, or South Africa please review our careers page (&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.kirbygroup.com/vacancies/&quot;&gt;Vacancies - Kirby Group Careers&lt;/a&gt;) or contact the Talent Acquisition Team at Kirby Group in confidence on +353 (0)1 454 0411.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates, regardless of race, gender, disability, religion, sexual orientation, or age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/kirbygroupengineering/senior-ehs-advisor-finsterwalde-136543","tags":["EHS K206"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792680934},{"slug":"engineering-manager-berlin-berlin-381548","company_name":"Superchat","title":"Engineering Manager (m/f/d)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Superchat, we&#39;re rebuilding how businesses talk to their customers. The phone call, the contact form, the support ticket: all of it is being replaced by messaging and AI. We&#39;re building the platform that runs underneath.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020, Superchat has become the platform of choice for &lt;strong&gt;10,000+ businesses worldwide&lt;/strong&gt;, from globally recognized brands like Allianz, Auto1, Enpal, Danone, and GASAG to the small businesses, dental practices, and one-person startups that need to look bigger than they are. Today, &lt;strong&gt;millions of messages flow through Superchat every single day&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We started as a unified inbox: one place for every channel a customer might pick, WhatsApp, email, SMS, Instagram. Then ChatGPT happened, and the second chapter began: AI agents that respond across chat, email, and voice at the quality of the best human teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re &lt;strong&gt;100 people&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;profitable&lt;/strong&gt;, and have raised &lt;strong&gt;€18M in funding&lt;/strong&gt; (last round 4.5 years ago, we&#39;ve been growing on our own money since). Headquartered in Berlin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a backend-leaning Tech Lead to lead a team of 3-4 engineers and own the tech for a part of Superchat’s product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role: You’ll spend roughly half your time designing and building software and the other half enabling your team to perform at its best. Work directly on architecture, development and important projects while creating the clarity, feedback and environment your engineers need to deliver an excellent product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Want&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong, current backend engineer.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You bring 3+ years of experience as a Senior or Staff Engineer and remain deeply involved in software development. You are comfortable owning, designing and building crucial parts of production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced with the JVM ecosystem.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You have substantial experience with Java or another JVM language. Kotlin and AWS experience are a plus, since our backend runs on Kotlin/Quarkus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to lead people.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You have at least 2 years of experience in a leadership role, whether as a Tech Lead, Engineering Manager, or through leading projects and owning architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong at delivery.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You know how to turn product goals into reality. You are used to work in fast-paced startups and are a driver to increase velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-minded.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You care about solving the customers problem. You engage with product decisions, challenge assumptions constructivly and find pragmatic solutions to build things in a lean way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are able to explain complex technical things in details to Engineers and in an understandable way to non-technical stakeholders. You create alignment and motivate people&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excited about AI-assisted development.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are already using AI in your development workflow and are eager to explore how it can improve engineering speed, quality and the way teams work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Don’t Want&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure people manager.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You no longer want to work directly on software. This role requires meaningful, ongoing involvement in architecture, implementation, code review, and technical problem-solving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hero engineer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You want to make every important technical decision yourself or become the bottleneck for the team. Your job is to raise the effectiveness of the whole team, not to be the only person who can solve difficult problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure delivery manager.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You treat engineering as a ticketing operation focused only on timelines and task tracking instead of product quality, technical health, and team growth. We need engineering leaders, not project coordinators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-only operator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You prefer fully remote work and don’t want to actively build relationships and culture in person with the team. We believe strong engineering leadership requires regular in-person collaboration and presence in Berlin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Day To Day&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend approximately 50% of your time contributing directly to architecture, development, code reviews, and important technical projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of 3-4 engineers and take responsibility for its effectiveness, technical quality, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with your Product Manager to understand customer problems, shape solutions, scope projects, and set priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear technical direction while enabling engineers to own decisions and develop their judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular 1:1s, give actionable feedback, and support each engineer’s development and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remove blockers, manage dependencies, and help the team identify delivery risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering practices and explore effective uses of AI throughout the software-development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to hiring through technical interviews, structured feedback, and candidate conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Director of Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Your manager and partner on people development, calibration, processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports: &lt;/strong&gt;Engineers in your team; you own their development, performance and growth&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Manager:&lt;/strong&gt; PMs own what and why; you own how (delivery) and who (people)&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CTO and CPO: &lt;/strong&gt;We are a lean organization with a flat hierarchy. You will regulary disccuss the direction of architecture with the CTO and product with the CPO&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Why People Choose Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission that matters. &lt;/strong&gt;Real impact on small businesses, not abstract metrics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funded with conviction. &lt;/strong&gt;$18M raised and profitable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern stack. &lt;/strong&gt;Kotlin/Quarkus, AWS, TypeScript/React/Next.js, and LangGraph for AI-powered features&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Squad-based organization. &lt;/strong&gt;Each squad owns its domain end-to-end with real ownership and autonomy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Two clear career tracks&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; We support both individual contributor growth (up to Staff level) and Management Paths with explicit reversibility between both and Tech Lead being the first level of management that is still quite hands-on&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-led structure. &lt;/strong&gt;PMs report directly to the CPO, keeping product strategy focused, consistent, and clearly prioritized&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid by design. &lt;/strong&gt;Our Berlin office in Prenzlauer Berg is the center of gravity, with two work-from-home days as the standard setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct feedback culture. &lt;/strong&gt;Honest, direct, and kind feedback is part of how we work together - in 1:1s, retrospectives, and everyday collaboration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Choose between an Urban Sports Club/John Reed membership or a public transport/Dance subscription&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal development budget of €500 for conferences, courses, books, career coaching, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An inclusive and exciting startup culture that enables fast professional and personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Beautiful office in the heart of Berlin (Prenzlauer Allee 242) with free snacks, drinks, and top-notch equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want to build a community, not just a company.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s important to us to create an environment where people genuinely enjoy spending time together - whether that’s through HYROX training, golfing, beer pong tournaments, running clubs, Warhammer, weekend activities, or whatever kind of community you’d like to help build here!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for people with passion, grit, and integrity. You&#39;re encouraged to apply even if your experience doesn&#39;t precisely match the description. At Superchat, we welcome diverse perspectives and people who think rigorously.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocating to Berlin? We support you with practical relocation help. You&#39;ll feel home in no time.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We look forward to your application! 🙂&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;With your application you agree to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/f601741cb4f24d418411aa0ff86c3787?pvs=21&quot;&gt;privacy policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://i.imgur.com/Uicf3C7.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/superchat/engineering-manager-berlin-berlin-381548","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin, Berlin","created_at":1792680934},{"slug":"solutions-engineer-munich-331674","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Solutions Engineer","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a technical pre-sales team at a B2B software company focused on digital transformation for industrial research and development. You will connect deep chemistry and materials science expertise with enterprise R&amp;D workflows, helping prospective customers understand the value of modern data platforms.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own technical pre-sales engagements from initial demonstrations through value cases, technical evaluations, and pilot execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tailored demonstrations, workshops, and pilots that reflect each prospect's research and development workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with account executives and customer stakeholders to support value-based selling and new business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead technical evaluations and presentations, explaining how digital tools can improve R&amp;D data management and innovation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentor and coordinate junior team members supporting technical evaluations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write scripts and configure platform integrations to support prospect engagements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel approximately 25% to 50% for customer meetings, presentations, and workshops.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Four to seven years of relevant experience, including at least four years in digitalization, change management, or R&amp;D leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An advanced degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, or materials science, with a focus on machine learning or computational methods.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong chemistry or materials science expertise and an understanding of enterprise R&amp;D workflows and laboratory informatics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and demonstrating technical platforms for enterprise customers, ideally alongside R&amp;D digitalization or organizational change initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A value-based sales approach, strong communication skills, and the ability to take ownership in a fast-paced pre-sales environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Python scripting skills are useful. Management consulting experience with a science background is also relevant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English and, for European locations, C1 or higher proficiency in the local language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness and ability to travel 25% to 50%, and authorization to work in the United States, United Kingdom, or Germany. Visa sponsorship is not available.</p></li></ul><h3>Compensation &amp; Benefits</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Base salary: $120,000 to $150,000 USD annually.</p><h3>Location</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid, based in Munich, Germany. London or New York may also be considered.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/true-talent-solutions-partners/solutions-engineer-munich-331674","tags":["Client Roles"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792680016},{"slug":"client-delivery-lead-accounting-experience-preferred-berlin-373377","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Client Delivery Lead (Accounting Experience preferred) (w/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Help us use technology to make a big green dent in the universe!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://kraken.tech/"><u>Kraken</u></a> powers some of the most innovative global developments in energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the technology that redefines utilities and unlocks a new energy system of the future. By optimising renewable generation, building a more intelligent grid, and empowering utilities to deliver an exceptional customer experience, our operating system is transforming the industry worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s an incredibly exciting time to work in energy. Join us on our mission to improve the lives of ONE BILLION humans within the decade and shape a cleaner, better future for everyone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kraken Customer</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we do: build the most AI-driven, innovative, forward-thinking platform for energy management. From optimizing resources to delivering cost-effective, exceptional customer experiences through advanced Customer Information Systems (CIS), billing, meter data management, CRM, and AI-driven communications, Kraken is powering the next wave of innovation in the energy industry.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Why we do it: future energy will not look like energy as we know it today. We need to not just think about our future, but build for it. Now.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have been licensing Kraken for over 4 years now, transforming businesses by not only moving their customer base to our Kraken platform but also changing their operating model &amp; ways of working. Throughout this time our team has been at the forefront of industry leading migrations whilst setting a new standard for what business transformation can look like. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏠 Where you'll fit in:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be joining the client delivery team with Kraken working to support European clients through their technology transformation journeys, supporting long term migration projects.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> The Client Delivery Lead has direct responsibility managing a tech domain (billing, finance, comms..) for our client projects. This is either migrating onto our Kraken platform or managing long term technology requirements. They need to work in partnership with the technology and operational teams at Kraken as well as the client to deliver results for our client’s project or business needs. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The<strong> Client Delivery Lead</strong> has to really understand how Kraken works, understand problems or requests raised by the client and refine solutions in the best way to leverage existing and new capability. They will bring technology, people and processes together to innovate improvements for our clients. You will also support the client in adapting to ways of working that are aligned to Kraken’s development style. You will work closely with Kraken’s product managers and developers to request development needs and act as a link to the client.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 What you'll own:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be managing the relationship with client counterparts (often product owners and business owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the first point of contact for tech development and the escalation and resolution point with customers for specific domain/product issues</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being the knowledge base of how Kraken works and how we deliver Kraken Platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Triaging incoming requests and communicating client priorities internally. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Summarising and articulating client needs, considerations, timelines internally to enable the ongoing development of the Kraken <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="http://platform.supporting/">platform.</a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting the engineering team to deliver product features</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenging the client to think differently about tech development, having full belief in the continuous iteration and deployment approach we have.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on, individual contributor position. The role is European based and your projects could be run from any country, travel is expected as part of this role.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a flat and agile organisation and plan to remain this way. We are looking for open minded individuals who are comfortable with ambiguity and an ever changing environment. To thrive here you must be a self-starter and willing to roll your sleeves up to solve any problem, constantly flexing outside of your typical job role to drive progress for our clients and organisation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You must be  committed to the Kraken way of delivering tech based on simplicity, client benefit and efficiency while bringing stakeholders through a journey of change. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You must be willing to challenge beliefs, have the ability to see through multiple viewpoints and, if needed, reach beyond your remit to support the client. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building a Kraken for everyone, a universal platform where there is greater benefit in sharing development to enable the green energy transition. Pioneers in this space, we are excited about how Kraken can change the lives of our customers and convinced that Kraken is the best answer, not only for efficiency but as a tool to tackle the climate crisis. If you believe this too then Kraken Tech is the right place for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 What you'll bring to the party:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this position you will be laser focused on satisfying our customer’s needs. We are looking for people with strong problem solving skills and a super positive solutions oriented mindset. If you have a taste for raising up to challenges and a winner mindset, this position is the right fit for you! (“Every problem has a solution, facing new challenges is exciting because that’s what makes us better every day and the bigger the challenge, the bigger the feeling of success”)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong client delivery and/or product ownership experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agile delivery experience </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of product management and customer journeys</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of technology and associated trends</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communications, collaboration and presentation skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong influencing skills and ability to challenge traditional ways of thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of working with significant complex delivery pipelines for clients</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Patience and initiative - our clients are undergoing huge transformations that take time and require our understanding </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time management and a get-stuff-done attitude</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consulting experience is a plus </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English + German</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous experience in accounting and billing or payments is nice to have for this position</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If this sounds like you then we'd love to hear from you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Are you ready for a career with us? We want to ensure you have the right tools and environment to unleash your potential. If you have any accommodation requests, please contact us at ----- We’ll do our best to tailor the experience to your needs so you can feel comfortable, confident and be at your best!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Studies have shown that some groups of people, like women, are less likely to apply to a role unless they meet 100% of the job requirements. Whoever you are, if you like one of our jobs, we encourage you to apply as you might just be the candidate we’re looking for! At Kraken, we're creating a team of genuine, honest, empathetic people. Our people are our strongest asset and the unique skills and perspectives people bring to the team are the driving force of our success. As an equal opportunity employer, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute. We consider all applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, national origin, age, sex, gender id