gen für dich.</p></li><li><p><strong>Technik:</strong> Ein Instandhaltungs-Team übernimmt die Handwerker-Koordination.</p></li><li><p><strong>Backoffice:</strong> Ein Buchhaltungs-Team hält die Zahlen und Abrechnungen sauber.</p></li><li><p><strong>AI:</strong> Unsere Software automatisiert die Dokumentation und das Daily Business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Deine Mission</strong></h3><ul><li><p><strong>Beirats-Management:</strong> Du pflegst die Beziehungen zu den Beiräten und führst deine Gemeinschaften souverän durch das Jahr.</p></li><li><p><strong>Versammlungsleitung:</strong> Du moderierst hybride und digitale Eigentümerversammlungen mit unserer hauseigenen Software.</p></li><li><p><strong>Innovation:</strong> Du bist die Schnittstelle zum Produkt-Team und hilfst uns, die Software so zu bauen, dass sie Verwaltern das Leben rettet.</p></li><li><p><strong>Wachstum (Optional):</strong> Du hast Lust, neue Kunden zu begeistern? Wir honorieren das mit attraktiven Prämien.</p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><strong>Erfahrung:</strong> Du bist Profi in der WEG-Verwaltung und kennst die Fallstricke der Branche.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Zertifizierung:</strong> Du bist „Zertifizierter Verwalter“ (§ 26a WEG) oder hast eine vergleichbare Qualifikation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Ownership:</strong> Du hast keine Lust mehr auf „Dienst nach Vorschrift“, sondern willst Prozesse aktiv neu denken.</p></li><li><p><strong>Kommunikation:</strong> Du trittst sicher auf und überzeugst Beiräte durch Kompetenz und Verbindlichkeit.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Was du bei Ralph bekommst</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Echte Freiheit:</strong> Wir sind <strong>"Remote-first"</strong>. Egal ob Hamburg, Berlin oder ein Coffee-Shop – du arbeitest, von wo du willst.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Sicherheit:</strong> Unbefristeter Vertrag in einem stabilen, VC-finanzierten PropTech mit 10.000 Einheiten im Rücken.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Entwicklung:</strong> Wir fördern deine Spezialisierung zum <strong>Klimaverwalter</strong>.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Extras:</strong> Attraktives Fixum plus erfolgsabhängiger Bonus, Urban Sports Club Mitgliedschaft und regelmäßige Team-Offsites.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Modernes Setup:</strong> High-End Hardware (MacBook) und unsere eigene AI-Plattform, die dir den Rücken frei hält.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/ralph-management-gmbh/senior-weg-verwalterin-100-remote-oder-hamburg-hamburg-office-88213","tags":["Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Homeoffice","created_at":1792669909},{"slug":"agentic-platform-engineer-gn-at-ai-venture-berlin-409481","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"Agentic Platform Engineer (gn) @ AI Venture, Berlin","description":"<p><em>This is an Atlantic portfolio venture.<br></em></p><p><strong>About the Venture</strong></p><p>AI models have moved faster than most companies’ ability to put them to work. The capabilities are there; knowing how to combine them effectively is still catching up.</p><p>Frontier labs naturally put their own models first. Companies often follow suit, asking one general-purpose model to handle ten very different jobs. We believe there is far more to unlock in the models that already exist, even before the next generation arrives. That is the opportunity we are building around.</p><p>We bring closed providers and open-weight models together behind a single API. Our engine breaks requests into their component parts, routes each to the right model within a cost budget, fine-tunes on customer data and checks the result against agreed quality standards. With no proprietary model to promote, we can choose the right combination for the task.</p><p>Lower costs matter because of what they make possible: giving a small team the freedom to build something that would previously have required a much larger one.</p><p>Our founder brings considerable drive, a hands-on approach and a strong sense of urgency to building the company. Backed by Atlantic at pre-seed, we are growing the engineering team to bring the product into production, with people already waiting to use it.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p>As one of our first platform engineers, you will build the foundations that every product feature depends on: the gateway and router, usage and billing systems, customer key management and the European infrastructure underneath.</p><p>Much of that platform is still taking shape. Working directly with the founder, CTO and founding AI engineer, you will help turn early architectural decisions into systems that remain reliable as the product grows.</p><p>You will take capabilities from design through to production, thinking through their APIs, failure modes, deployment, observability and ongoing operation. In a team this small, building and running the system belong together. You will also work alongside our founding AI engineer on evals, embeddings and open-weight model serving, bringing platform engineering depth to the ML side of the product.</p><p>Agentic engineering is central to how we work. You will operate in an agentic way by default, using coding agents as a core part of how you design, build, test and ship software. You'll develop the harnesses and workflows that allow you to delegate and parallelise work effectively, increasing what a small engineering team can deliver. This requires strong coding fundamentals and the judgement to review, challenge and take responsibility for everything that reaches production.</p><p>There is a lot to build and an ambitious timeline ahead. We work with intensity, move quickly from decisions to execution and value people who take initiative and see things through.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You’ll Work On</strong></p><p>Your first area of ownership will depend on your strengths and our priorities. From there, you will contribute across the platform as it develops.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Gateway and routing:</strong> build a consistent API across model providers, with reliable streaming, fallbacks and safe handling of retries and provider errors.</p></li><li><p><strong>Agentic engineering workflows:</strong> build and refine the harnesses, tooling and workflows that enable coding agents to work effectively across the development lifecycle, from implementation and testing to debugging and deployment.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cost optimisation:</strong> develop caching, history compression and model selection, measuring savings while keeping estimated costs distinct from actual spend.</p></li><li><p><strong>Usage and billing:</strong> build accurate accounting for model calls, usage reports, plan entitlements and invoice reconciliation.</p></li><li><p><strong>Agent infrastructure and integrations:</strong> support tool calls, cost limits, human approvals and runs that can recover safely from interruptions, alongside connectors for services such as Gmail, Slack and calendars.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tenancy and secrets:</strong> maintain workspace isolation, secure authentication and encrypted customer key management.</p></li><li><p><strong>European infrastructure and model serving:</strong> build and operate our cloud infrastructure, including the GPU capacity used to serve open-weight models.</p></li><li><p><strong>Production reliability:</strong> make systems observable, migrations reversible and releases safe, with tests that protect data integrity and logs that keep customer content and secrets private.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>The platform will evolve quickly. You will need to move comfortably between improving what exists and learning enough about a new problem to build the next piece well.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Our Stack</strong></p><p>Our backend is built in Python, with a TypeScript frontend in a shared monorepo.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Backend:</strong> Python, FastAPI, Pydantic and LiteLLM.</p></li><li><p><strong>Data and queues:</strong> Postgres with row-level security and pgvector, Redis and arq.</p></li><li><p><strong>Frontend:</strong> <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="http://Next.js">Next.js</a>, React and TypeScript.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cloud and infrastructure:</strong> Scaleway, Terraform and Kubernetes for GPU workloads.</p></li><li><p><strong>Auth and secrets:</strong> Zitadel, Secret Manager and KMS.</p></li><li><p><strong>Observability and testing:</strong> OpenTelemetry, Langfuse, Sentry, pytest and testcontainers, alongside frontend testing tools.</p></li></ul><p>You should be comfortable with the core backend technologies and ready to learn the rest as the work requires.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About You</strong></p><p>You enjoy the craft of engineering and the responsibility of seeing your work used in production. Faced with an unclear problem, you can identify what matters, make sensible trade-offs and carry a solution through to release without someone planning every step. You naturally look for ways to multiply your output through agentic workflows, rather than approaching every engineering task as something to execute manually.</p><p>We are looking for:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Experience building and operating production systems:</strong> several years of backend engineering with real users, typically three to six, and meaningful ownership of what you shipped.</p></li><li><p><strong>Strong Python fundamentals:</strong> confidence with async code, typing and testing. TypeScript experience is a plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>Agentic engineering as a default way of working:</strong> you have hands-on experience using coding agents as a core part of your engineering workflow. You know how to break down problems, delegate and parallelise tasks, provide the right context and build effective agentic workflows. Crucially, you have the technical depth to review, debug and take ownership of the resulting code.</p></li><li><p><strong>Platform engineering depth:</strong> practical experience with Postgres, Redis, queues, networking and Terraform. Kubernetes experience is useful, particularly for our GPU infrastructure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Sound engineering judgement:</strong> clear APIs, tenant isolation, data integrity, partial failure and safe rollouts. You can explain both your decisions and what you chose to leave out.</p></li><li><p><strong>A working understanding of ML systems:</strong> familiarity with LLMs, embeddings, evals, model serving and fine-tuning. Experience with LLM APIs, streaming and token costs is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p><strong>A disciplined approach to measurement:</strong> you benchmark changes, question assumptions and use evidence to understand whether an improvement holds up.</p></li><li><p><strong>Initiative and drive:</strong> you enjoy getting deep into a problem, finding a way forward and putting in the work to make it happen.</p></li><li><p>This is an experienced individual-contributor role, with ownership of the capabilities you build and close collaboration across the founding team.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English is required; German is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Why Join</strong></p><p>At this stage, platform engineering decisions have a direct influence on the product and how quickly the team can build it. You will work close to the founder and CTO, with room to shape the systems you own and see the results of your work first-hand.</p><p>The challenge spans AI infrastructure, distributed systems, security and cost efficiency. You will build across those boundaries, take real responsibility early and receive a meaningful equity package in the company you help develop.</p><p>We are competing with teams that have more people, more funding and an earlier start. Our approach depends on technical depth, focused decisions and the drive to turn them into working software. We believe agentic engineering can fundamentally change what a small, technically strong team is capable of building, and we're looking for people who want to push that approach forward. For someone who enjoys a demanding build, close collaboration and visible impact, there is a lot to get involved in.</p><p>This is a full-time role, based in our Berlin office five days a week, starting as soon as possible.</p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/agentic-platform-engineer-gn-at-ai-venture-berlin-409481","tags":[],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1792669908},{"slug":"technical-co-founder-ai-efficiency-at-ai-venture-berlin-172572","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"Technical Co-Founder (AI Efficiency) @ AI Venture, Berlin","description":"<p><em>This is an Atlantic portfolio venture.<br></em></p><p><strong>About the Venture</strong></p><p>AI models have moved faster than most companies’ ability to put them to work. The capabilities are there; knowing how to combine them effectively is still catching up.</p><p>Frontier labs naturally put their own models first. Companies often follow suit, asking one general-purpose model to handle ten very different jobs. We believe there is far more to unlock in the models that already exist.</p><p>We bring closed providers and open-weight models together behind a single API. Our engine breaks requests into their component parts, routes each to the right model within a cost budget, fine-tunes on customer data and checks the results against agreed quality standards. With no proprietary model to promote, we can choose the best combination for each task.</p><p>Lower costs matter because of what they make possible: giving a small team the freedom to build something that would previously have required a much larger one.</p><p>Our founder was selected for Slush 20 Under 20, awarded by Anthropic, Slush, Index Ventures and Sifted. We closed our pre-seed round in two weeks and already have people waiting to use the product. We're now looking for a technical co-founder to help turn this opportunity into a company.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p>As Technical Co-Founder, you will lead the development of our AI efficiency engine, working alongside the founder to turn a compelling technical opportunity into a product.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>At the heart of the role is a deceptively simple question: <strong>how can we make AI models deliver the same or better results at a fraction of the cost?</strong></p><p>You will explore approaches to model routing, fine-tuning, caching and inference optimisation, combining scientific curiosity with the ability to turn promising ideas into measurable improvements.</p><p>This is a role for someone who enjoys difficult technical problems, rigorous experimentation and challenging existing approaches. You won't be expected to build every part of the platform yourself. Working alongside our founding AI engineer and backend platform engineer, you will set the technical direction and focus your expertise where it creates the greatest impact.</p><p>Agentic engineering is central to how we work. We're looking for someone who already operates this way, using coding agents and developing the workflows and harnesses that allow a small team to move exceptionally quickly without compromising technical quality.</p><p>Above all, this is a co-founder role. We're looking for someone who wants to take genuine ownership, work with relentless intensity and help build a company from its earliest stages.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Drive AI cost efficiency:</strong> develop approaches to reducing inference costs through model selection, routing, caching, fine-tuning, quantization and other optimisation techniques.</p></li><li><p><strong>Experiment and benchmark:</strong> design rigorous evaluations to understand the trade-offs between cost, quality and latency, turning technical insights into measurable improvements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Shape the efficiency engine:</strong> determine how closed and open-weight models can be combined and optimised to deliver the best outcomes for different tasks.</p></li><li><p><strong>Set technical direction:</strong> identify promising opportunities, make key architectural decisions and guide the founding engineers in bringing them to production.</p></li><li><p><strong>Push agentic engineering forward:</strong> use coding agents as a core part of your work and develop the harnesses and workflows that allow a small team to operate with exceptional leverage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Build the company:</strong> work closely with the founder on technical strategy, attract exceptional talent and help shape the product and business.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>About You</strong></p><p>You bring deep technical curiosity, scientific rigour and an entrepreneurial mindset. You enjoy getting into the details, testing hypotheses and finding approaches others might overlook.<br></p><p>We're particularly interested in people who bring:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Deep expertise in AI efficiency:</strong> meaningful experience optimising the cost or performance of LLMs or other AI systems, with concrete results to show for it. Experience in inference optimisation, routing, fine-tuning or related techniques is particularly relevant.</p></li><li><p><strong>Strong technical foundations:</strong> a solid understanding of modern AI models, rigorous experimentation and the ability to translate research into practical improvements.</p></li><li><p><strong>An agentic approach to engineering:</strong> you actively use coding agents, know how to orchestrate them effectively and are excited by what small, highly leveraged teams can achieve.</p></li><li><p><strong>A co-founder mindset:</strong> you're resourceful, ambitious and comfortable with uncertainty. You take initiative, move quickly and want to build something from the ground up.</p></li><li><p><strong>Technical leadership potential:</strong> you have the judgement to make difficult technical decisions and guide others. Previous CTO or engineering management experience is not required.</p></li></ul><p>We're more interested in exceptional depth in AI efficiency and the ambition to build a company than a conventional CTO background.</p><p>Fluent English is required; German is a plus.<br></p><p><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience with open-weight models, GPU inference or model serving.</p></li><li><p>A strong research or open-source track record in AI or machine learning.</p></li><li><p>Experience taking AI systems into production or working in an early-stage startup.<br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Why Join</strong></p><p>With the pre-seed round closed and early momentum behind us, you'll join at a point where there is considerable room to shape what comes next. You'll work alongside the founder, set the technical direction and receive meaningful co-founder equity in the company you help create.<br></p><p>We're competing with teams that have more people, more funding and an earlier start. Our conviction is that exceptional technical depth, focused decisions and an agentic approach to engineering can give a small team a meaningful advantage.<br></p><p>For someone who wants to apply their expertise in AI efficiency to an ambitious technical challenge, and take the leap from specialist to co-founder, this is an opportunity to build something of their own.<br></p><p>This is a full-time commitment, based in our Berlin office five days a week, starting as soon as possible.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/technical-co-founder-ai-efficiency-at-ai-venture-berlin-172572","tags":["Founder & Entrepreneurs in Residence"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1792669908},{"slug":"it-administrator-system-engineer-monchengladbach-325371","company_name":"Hall Tabakwaren e.K","title":"IT-Administrator / System Engineer (m/w/d)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Kommen Sie ins Team – gestalten Sie unsere Personalarbeit aktiv mit</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><em>Hall Tabakwaren</em> ist bundesweit in aller Munde.</strong> 1903 als Ladengeschäft für Zigarren, Rauchtabak und Zigaretten gegründet, sind wir heute einer der führenden Tabakwarengroßhändler in Deutschland. In unserem in 5. Generation inhabergeführten Familienunternehmen sorgen über 750 Mitarbeiterinnen und Mitarbeiter in 11 Niederlassungen mit 330 firmeneigenen Fahrzeugen und 30.000 <em>Cigarettenautomaten</em> dafür, dass Menschen im gesamten Bundesgebiet schnell, sicher und zuverlässig zu ihrer Lieblingsmarke kommen. Mit unserer Erfahrung, unserer Leidenschaft und unserem Engagement – auch für unsere rund 4.300 Einzelhandelskunden – erwirtschaften wir jährlich mehr als 1 Milliarde Euro Umsatz. Und wir wachsen weiter, gerne mit dir als</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>IT-Administrator (m/w/d)</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>in Mönchengladbach</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Ihre Aufgaben</strong></p><ul><li><p>Betreuung, Administration und Optimierung unserer IT-Infrastruktur (Server, Clients, Netzwerk und Speicherlösungen)</p></li><li><p>Verwaltung und Weiterentwicklung der <strong>VMware</strong>-Virtualisierungsumgebung</p></li><li><p>Steuerung und Wartung unserer <strong>NetApp</strong>-Speichersysteme</p></li><li><p>Sicherstellung der Netzwerksicherheit und Firewall-Administration mittels <strong>OPNsense</strong></p></li><li><p>Administration der <strong>Windows Server</strong>-Landschaft (Server 2016 – 2025) sowie Betreuung der Windows-Clients</p></li><li><p>Verwaltung und Betreuung von <strong>Exchange On-Premises</strong> sowie <strong>Microsoft 365</strong> Cloud-Umgebungen (Hybrid-Setup)</p></li><li><p>Betreuung und Wartung von <strong>MS SQL Server</strong>-Datenbanken</p></li><li><p>Automatisierung von administrativen Aufgaben und Prozessen mittels <strong>PowerShell-Skripting</strong></p></li><li><p>Administration und Konfiguration von <strong>UniFi-Telefonanlagen</strong> (UniFi Talk / VoIP) und Netzwerkkomponenten</p></li><li><p>Zentrales Management und Deployment von <strong>IGEL ThinClients</strong></p></li><li><p>Analyse und Behebung von Störungen im 2nd-Level-Support sowie Unterstützung der Anwender</p></li><li><p>Mitwirkung an IT-Projekten zur Modernisierung und Erweiterung der Systemlandschaft</p></li></ul> <br> <p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Ihr Profil</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </p><ul><li><p>Erfolgreich abgeschlossene Ausbildung im IT-Bereich (z. B. Fachinformatiker für Systemintegration), ein vergleichbares Studium oder eine entsprechende Qualifikation</p></li><li><p><strong>Mehrjährige nachgewiesene Berufserfahrung</strong> in der IT-Systemadministration</p></li><li><p>Fundierte praktische Kenntnisse in <strong>mehreren der folgenden Bereiche</strong>:</p><ul><li><p>Virtualisierung mit <strong>VMware</strong></p></li><li><p>Storage-Lösungen von <strong>NetApp</strong></p></li><li><p>Firewall- und Netzwerkadministration mit <strong>OPNsense</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Windows Server</strong> (Versionen 2016 bis 2025) sowie Windows Desktop-Betriebssysteme</p></li><li><p><strong>Exchange On-Premises</strong> und <strong>Microsoft 365</strong> / Cloud-Services</p></li><li><p>Administration von <strong>MS SQL Servern</strong></p></li><li><p>Automatisierung / Skripting mit <strong>PowerShell</strong></p></li><li><p>Verwaltung von <strong>UniFi-Telefonanlagen / VoIP</strong></p></li><li><p>Client-Management mit <strong>IGEL ThinClients</strong></p></li></ul></li><li><p>Hohes Qualitäts- und Sicherheitsbewusstsein</p></li><li><p>Selbstständige, strukturierte und lösungsorientierte Arbeitsweise</p></li><li><p>Sehr gute Deutschkenntnisse in Wort und Schrift</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Das bieten wir Ihnen</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">++ Flache Hierarchien ++ Kurze Entscheidungswege ++ Attraktives Gehalt ++ Viel Eigenverantwortung ++ Festanstellung mit unbefristeten Arbeitsvertag ++ Dienstwagen mit privater Nutzung ++ Flexible Arbeitszeitgestaltung innerhalb bestimmter Bandbreiten ++</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">Klingt nach einer Aufgabe, die zu Ihnen passt? Dann freuen wir uns darauf, Sie kennenzulernen.</p><p class="MsoNormal">Bewerben Sie sich jetzt – inklusive Gehaltsvorstellung und frühestmöglichen Eintrittstermins – per Post oder E-Mail und werden Sie Teil unseres Teams.</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Hall Tabakwaren e. K.</strong></p><p>Herr Domink Mathieu</p><p class="MsoNormal">Bismarckstr. 22</p><p class="MsoNormal">41061 Mönchengladbach</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/hall-tabakwaren-ek/it-administrator-system-engineer-monchengladbach-325371","tags":["Innendienst"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Mönchengladbach, Nordrhein-Westfalen, Deutschland","created_at":1792669906},{"slug":"head-senior-director-of-sales-central-europe-wetzlar-123895","company_name":"Cyclomedia Technology","title":"Head / Senior Director of Sales – Central Europe","description":"<p><strong>About Cyclomedia</strong></p><p><br>At Cyclomedia, our mission is to digitise the outside world with precision. Our geospatial technology turns street-level and aerial imagery into data and insights that cities, municipalities, utilities, telecom operators and infrastructure owners use to plan and run their operations more safely, efficiently and sustainably.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Backed by private equity investor Volpi Capital, we operate across the Netherlands, Germany, Belgium, Poland and the United States. Our customers range from Kommunen, Länder and federal authorities to Stadtwerke, utilities and telecom infrastructure companies.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Our culture is driven by curiosity and innovation, guided by impact and purpose, and built on collaboration, trust, transparency and accountability. We believe diverse perspectives drive innovation, and we are committed to building a team that reflects different backgrounds, identities and experiences. We welcome applications from everyone.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Job Summary</strong></p><p><br>Germany is one of Cyclomedia's most important markets and a key pillar of our growth strategy. As Head / Senior Director of Sales, Central Europe, you will lead the next phase of our growth across DACH and Poland as a hands-on sales leader who owns the pipeline, the team and the plan.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You will build on a strong foundation: an established sales team and a base of strong reference customers. Your mandate is to take this to the next level by building a predictable, scalable sales engine with full visibility across pipeline, accounts and forecast.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Around 75% of your time goes into hands-on sales leadership, and around 25% into business development and growth strategy. You will be a member of the commercial leadership team, alongside the regional VPs and the VP Marketing.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Job Duties<br></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>Pipeline and forecast</em></p><ul><li><p>Lead the weekly pipeline review across every rep, deal and stage.</p></li><li><p>Drive qualification rigour from first contact to close, ensuring forecasts are built on well-qualified opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Deliver a reliable monthly and quarterly forecast with clear insight into drivers and variance.</p></li><li><p>Be a hands-on CRM user and champion high standards of data quality and accuracy across the team.</p></li><li><p>Identify deals that need momentum early, create urgency and engage personally where it adds the most value.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><em>Team leadership</em></p><ul><li><p>Set clear, measurable expectations for every seller, supported by structured 1:1s, deal reviews and coaching.</p></li><li><p>Develop team performance through coaching, enablement and effective talent management.</p></li><li><p>Lead the team through growth and change with a style that inspires people to follow.</p></li><li><p>Maintain transparent, proactive communication with senior leadership, raising topics early and always with a recommended next step.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><em>Customers and key accounts</em></p><ul><li><p>Personally own key accounts and strategic deals as a player-coach.</p></li><li><p>Build senior relationships across Kommunen, Länder and Bund, Stadtwerke and utilities, and infrastructure and telecom accounts.</p></li><li><p>Lead or steer public tenders (RFQ / RFP, Vergaberecht, framework agreements) together with pre-sales.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><em>Growth strategy and business development</em></p><ul><li><p>Build and own the growth plan for Germany, DACH and Poland: where the next 12–24 months of revenue will come from, by vertical, segment and channel.</p></li><li><p>Translate the plan into quarterly targets, headcount needs and channel priorities, and keep it current as a live commitment.</p></li><li><p>Align public-sector buying cycles with the company's annual planning cadence.</p></li><li><p>Identify white space in the existing customer base and the wider market.</p></li><li><p>Bring structured market intelligence to the commercial leadership team, always with a recommendation.</p></li><li><p>Orchestrate pre-sales, marketing and product through influence and collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><strong>Job Requirements:</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>10+ years in B2B sales, including 4+ years leading sales teams against revenue targets; around 15 years of overall experience is a useful guide.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>A hands-on operating style: you personally run the forecast, the weekly cadence, the pipeline and key accounts.</p></li><li><p>Public-sector exposure: familiarity with tender mechanics, procurement rules and public-sector buying timelines.</p></li><li><p>Experience in data or technology solution sales, ideally geospatial or adjacent technology, or data-driven solutions with a long, considered buying cycle.</p></li><li><p>Experience in a larger, structured corporate environment, combined with the motivation to apply that discipline in a company where your impact is direct and visible.</p></li><li><p>Leadership people follow: you set high standards, coach people to meet them and make sound people decisions.</p></li><li><p>Fluent German and fluent English.<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><em>Nice to have</em></p><ul><li><p>Experience selling across several verticals such as government, utilities / Stadtwerke, telecom and infrastructure.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with Vermessung / Kataster and municipal planning buyers.</p></li><li><p>A regional growth plan you built and executed with measurable accountability.</p></li><li><p>Experience running several sales motions at once: direct enterprise, public sector, channel / partner and inbound.</p></li><li><p>Hands-on knowledge of public procurement, including RFPs, tenders and multi-year framework agreements.</p></li><li><p>Experience aligning public-sector sales cycles with the planning cadence of an investor-backed growth business.</p></li><li><p>Polish language skills.</p></li><li><p>Based in the Wetzlar / Frankfurt region<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>Benefits<br></strong></p><ul><li><p>Real ownership: a clear growth mandate, genuine freedom to shape the plan, and a seat on the commercial leadership team.</p></li><li><p>A strong starting point: an experienced team and solid reference customers.</p></li><li><p>Competitive package: attractive base salary plus performance-related variable pay.</p></li><li><p>Company car.</p></li><li><p>28 days of annual leave, plus public holidays.</p></li><li><p>Supplementary health insurance: treatment by senior physicians and a private room, fully paid by Cyclomedia.</p></li><li><p>Company pension (Direktversicherung) with an employer contribution.</p></li><li><p>Learning and development: team coaching, online courses and individual training.</p></li><li><p>Team events: hiking, karaoke, treasure hunts and wine tastings are all part of how we get together.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p>Ready to lead the growth of one of our most important markets? Apply now and help us bring Cyclomedia's geospatial insights to the organisations shaping Central Europe.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cyclomedia-technology/head-senior-director-o