2B Food Ingredients Distribution m/f/d","description":"<h2>About Our Client</h2><p>Our client is a leading international ingredients distributor connecting customers and suppliers across multiple markets. </p><p>Products are valued added Ingredients from leading suppliers.</p><p>As the organisation continues to expand its international footprint, it is seeking a commercially driven and strategically minded Head of Marketing  to strengthen market positioning, accelerate business development initiatives, and elevate the company's brand globally.</p><p>This is a highly visible leadership role combining strategic marketing, brand management, business development support, supplier engagement, and customer experience across multiple international markets.</p><h2>The Opportunity</h2><p>As Head of Marketing , you will own and drive the global marketing agenda. Working closely with commercial leaders, local country organisations, suppliers, and external partners, you will identify opportunities, develop compelling value propositions, and execute impactful marketing programmes that strengthen customer and supplier engagement.</p><p>You will play a key role in shaping the company's market positioning, accelerating category business development, and building a consistent international brand that supports ambitious expansion plans.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><h3>Strategic Marketing & Business Development</h3><ul><li><p>Develop and execute the international marketing strategy aligned with commercial and business development objectives.</p></li><li><p>Lead category business development initiatives across business units and markets, leveraging synergies throughout the organisation.</p></li><li><p>Identify market trends, customer needs, competitive developments, and emerging business opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Translate market intelligence into actionable business development initiatives and commercial programmes.</p></li><li><p>Partner closely with sales and business development teams to drive customer acquisition and market penetration.</p></li><li><p>Develop compelling value propositions, sales tools, customer presentations, and marketing collateral.</p></li><li><p>Establish, share, and implement best-practice marketing approaches across countries and business platforms.</p></li></ul><h3>Supplier Marketing & Strategic Partnerships</h3><ul><li><p>Build and execute joint marketing programmes with strategic supplier partners.</p></li><li><p>Develop supplier branding, communication concepts, and co-marketing initiatives.</p></li><li><p>Strengthen supplier relationships through impactful marketing activation and category development support.</p></li></ul><h3>Brand Leadership & Corporate Communications</h3><ul><li><p>Own and further develop the corporate brand strategy, positioning, and identity.</p></li><li><p>Ensure consistent brand execution across all markets, communication channels, and customer touchpoints.</p></li><li><p>Lead corporate communications, internal communications, and employer branding activities.</p></li><li><p>Manage external agencies, designers, and communication partners.</p></li><li><p>Continuously enhance the company's digital presence, including websites, social media, and digital communication channels.</p></li></ul><h3>Events & Customer Engagement</h3><ul><li><p>Lead the global event strategy, including trade fairs, customer seminars, supplier conferences, webinars, and internal events.</p></li><li><p>Create engaging customer and supplier experiences that strengthen relationships and generate commercial opportunities.</p></li><li><p>Maximise event ROI through effective planning, execution, lead generation, and follow-up programmes.</p></li><li><p>Support local organisations in executing high-impact regional marketing initiatives.</p></li></ul><h2>Candidate Profile</h2><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li><p>Minimum 10 years of progressive experience in B2B marketing, business development, commercial leadership, or business development-focused marketing roles.</p></li><li><p>Demonstrated track record of developing and executing strategic marketing programmes that deliver measurable commercial results.</p></li><li><p>Strong experience within Food Ingredients, Flavours, Nutrition, Specialty Chemicals, Life Sciences, or adjacent B2B industries.</p></li><li><p>Experience within ingredient distribution, specialty distribution, or B2B trading environments is highly desirable.</p></li><li><p>International experience across multiple markets and cultures is strongly preferred.</p></li></ul><h3>Skills & Competencies</h3><ul><li><p>Strong commercial acumen and strategic thinking capabilities.</p></li><li><p>Proven ability to translate technical product features into compelling customer value propositions.</p></li><li><p>Excellent stakeholder management and influencing skills across all organisational levels.</p></li><li><p>Strong project management and execution capabilities.</p></li><li><p>Data-driven decision-maker with highly developed analytical skills.</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial, hands-on, and results-oriented leadership style.</p></li><li><p>Outstanding communication, presentation, and relationship-building skills.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English is essential. Additional European languages are advantageous.</p></li></ul><h3>Education</h3><ul><li><p>Degree in Food Technology, Marketing, Business, Economics, or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p>Additional marketing qualifications or postgraduate education would be advantageous.</p></li></ul><h2>Why This Opportunity?</h2><ul><li><p>Shape and lead the global marketing and business development agenda of a leading international ingredients platform.</p></li><li><p>Direct exposure to senior leadership and strategic decision-making.</p></li><li><p>Significant influence on commercial business development, branding, customer engagement, and market development.</p></li><li><p>International scope with extensive supplier and customer interaction.</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial culture offering high visibility, autonomy, and impact.</p></li></ul><p>If you are a commercially minded B2B marketing leader with a passion for business development, branding, and international market development, we would welcome a confidential conversation.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/gfic/head-of-marketing-b2b-food-ingredients-distribution-london-481941","tags":["Remote","Management","Team Leader"],"job_types":["Permanent employment","manager"],"location":"London","created_at":1792709251},{"slug":"product-director-466269","company_name":"Zone & Co","title":"Product Director","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Zone &amp;amp; Company Software Consulting LLC (“Zone”) is the ERP-native AI platform for financial operations, purpose-built for organizations running on Oracle NetSuite. We are redefining how finance teams operate by delivering an AI-powered system that automates, connects, and scales financial workflows directly within the ERP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the AI operating system for finance teams in NetSuite, Zone enables more than 4,500 customers worldwide to run smarter, faster, and with greater accuracy. Our platform spans the full financial lifecycle, including Quote-to-Cash, Procure-to-Pay, Treasury, Payroll Management, and Record-to-Report, eliminating manual processes and unlocking real-time financial intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By embedding intelligence directly into NetSuite, Zone helps finance teams move beyond reactive work to proactive, strategic impact. Learn more at&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.zoneandco.com&quot;&gt; www.zoneandco.com&lt;/a&gt; or follow us on LinkedIn:&lt;a href=&quot;http://linkedin.com/company/zoneandco&quot;&gt; linkedin.com/company/zoneandco&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone &amp;amp; Co. is seeking a Director of Procure-to-Pay Product Suite to define, build, and scale our flagship platform. As the strategic leader of this product area, you will set the vision, drive innovation, and lead a high-performing team to deliver transformative solutions for global businesses. This is a unique opportunity for a product executive with a proven track record or exceptional potential to shape the future of enterprise financial operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is changing what technology can do. We want someone who knows the problem space to see where it is heading, and who builds with AI to get there first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate a bold, actionable product vision and strategy for the Procure-to-Pay suite, aligned with Zone &amp;amp; Co.’s overall business goals and market opportunities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and empower a high-performing team of product managers, fostering a culture of innovation, accountability, and customer focus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and scale the product roadmap, ensuring seamless integration of procurement and payment workflows that drive measurable value for customers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer feedback, market trends, and competitive insights into data-driven product decisions and prioritization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion design excellence by delivering intuitive, user-centric solutions that elevate the customer experience and differentiate our offerings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering, sales, marketing, and executive leadership to align vision and execution, from ideation to launch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a visible product leader—representing the Procure to Pay suite in customer conversations, internal leadership forums, and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;job-requirements-title&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;x12ofw9d&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, Computer Science, Product Management, or a related field; an advanced degree is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in product management, with deep expertise in Accounts Payable (AP) automation and Procure-to-Pay (P2P) solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of end-to-end AP workflows, including the day-to-day needs of AP teams and the strategic priorities of CFOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building AI-powered products and successfully bringing them to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and initiative, with the ability to drive outcomes end to end, act proactively, and identify and address challenges early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment, adapt quickly, and adjust priorities based on customer feedback, data, and market insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgment, with the ability to balance customer needs, business objectives, and market opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading and developing product teams, with excellent communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with peers and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is £100,000 – £108,000 GBP + bonus + equity. Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including, but not limited to, the candidate’s skills, qualifications, experience, and education, as well as market and business considerations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zone, we provide the platform; you provide the grit. We operate as a high-velocity, fully remote, global team where autonomy isn&#39;t just a perk, it’s the standard. We’re looking for self-driven professionals eager to navigate the complexities of a unique SaaS environment and take full command of their professional evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We ditch micro-management for high-trust flexibility, ensuring you have the space to innovate and scale. Our benefits are built to fuel this lifestyle, supporting your life beyond the screen so you can focus on making a global impact. Explore our offerings at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.zoneandco.com/careers&quot;&gt;https://www.zoneandco.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Our Global Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zone &amp;amp; Co is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to building a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace. We thrive on unique perspectives and strongly encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Here, your identity is valued, and your talent is the only limit to your growth. All qualified applicants will receive consideration regardless of race, color, religion, sex, orientation, age, disability, or any other protected factor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Terms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;United States&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment with Zone is &lt;strong&gt;“At-Will”&lt;/strong&gt;, meaning either party may terminate the relationship at any time, with or without cause or notice, in accordance with applicable law. This job description does not constitute an employment contract or guarantee of continued employment. Duties and responsibilities may evolve as the company grows and may change at any time with or without notice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-US Jurisdictions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is offered as a Fixed-Term or Permanent Contract based on your country of residence.&amp;nbsp; Employment is subject to a written contract which outlines specific notice periods, probationary terms, and statutory entitlements.&lt;/p&gt;
