 calendar, manage budgeting and PO processes, and look after team operations, from onboarding and the Learning &amp; Development programme to offsites and events.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also spend time embedded with teams such as Content, Product Marketing or Social Media to set up their operations or support a major launch. Throughout, you'll use Asana and AI to remove admin friction and improve how all Marketing teams work together. It's a hands-on, cross-functional role for someone who wants to support a large team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marketing experience is a plus. Admin or operational experience is essential.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong><br /><br /><strong>Marketing team coordination and calendar management; </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up and own a marketing calendar for all internal and external milestones, from reporting to campaign milestones and events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage day-to-day team admin and support VP Marketing: meeting coordination and bookings, room/resource scheduling, food and catering orders for team events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate logistics for offsites and workshops end to end: venue sourcing, catering, travel where needed, run-of-day schedule</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the onboarding documentation and process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and iterate the Learning &amp; Development programme — scheduling sessions, tracking attendance, gathering feedback</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Asana as the operational backbone across the team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimise processes and team operations with AI; </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with AI leads and wider marketing team to identify and prioritise cross-functional AI tools, skills and agents that reduce manual work across Marketing (briefing, reporting, budget tracking, onboarding)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own workflow automation for repeatable operational tasks (PO/invoice tracking, budget reconciliation, status reporting) using AI-assisted tools where they save meaningful time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the link between Marketing and the AI/upskilling programme: surface where the team is spending time on repetitive work, and bring back relevant tools, prompts or agents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support rollout of new AI-enabled processes — documentation, quick training, troubleshooting first use</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Budget, PO and invoice administration; </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a point of contact between Marketing and Accounting/Procurify for POs and invoices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track budgets and support monthly reconciliations across the whole org</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain clear, current budget trackers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI to optimise this process and remove friction</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tooling audits; </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run periodic audits of agencies and tools in use across marketing: what's licensed, what's actually used, overlap and gaps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Marketing Operations team to recommend consolidation or decommissioning where tools are duplicated or underused</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we look for:</strong><br /></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable owning team logistics and