er leading minds from the travel, fintech, and SaaS industries, representing over 70 countries. If you're excited about having a real impact and shaping how millions of people experience work, we'd love you on the team.<br /><br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.perk.com">www.perk.com</a> to learn more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4899a966-8724-4480-958f-7271e5dc2807/f3e1915d-e346-4987-a1fb-9c447e8786c0" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Suitcase is Perk's design system, supporting 25+ designers and the engineers who build with them across web and mobile. Our ambition is for it to be a complete, consumer-grade, accessible and distributable system, so Perk feels like one consistent product on every surface our customers use, including AI agents and assistants. As a Senior Design Systems Designer you'll own the craft and visual direction of Suitcase, and work with front-end engineers, content designers and product designers to make high quality design the default standard. You will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the direction for Suitcase with design and engineering leadership, turn the vision into a roadmap with named resources, and report progress against it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the visual language, token architecture, and foundations of Suitcase: typography, colour, space, motion, and interaction states.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with content design and localisation on content tokens, so components carry their language requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, document, and refine components with complete states, variants, platform coverage and usage guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write component specs that AI prototyping tools can read, so generated prototypes use real Suitcase components and tokens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring components to WCAG 2.2 AA, and make conformance part of how new components are built and reviewed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define adoption, component health, accessibility, and Figma-to-code parity measures with engineering, and report against them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the contribution governance model, with defined routes for components between an experimental layer and the core system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion Suitcase across Builders, explain the reasoning behind decisions, and coach designers and engineers on using and contributing to the system.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll need</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product design experience, including time spent designing and scaling design systems for a fast-growing product on web and mobile.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep grasp of typography, colour, layout, motion, and micro-interactions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Judgement on when the system needs a new component and when an existing one should be used.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and maintaining token systems, including naming, theming, documentation, and Figma-to-code workflows, and working knowledge of HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience designing components for WCAG 2.2 AA standards, including keyboard and screen-reader behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience prototyping with AI tools and with Storybook, Code Connect and MCP tooling, and an understanding of how they connect design systems to code and AI tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to take non-designers from the problem to the decision to the outcome and build adoption by persuasion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear opinion of what good looks like, and the ability to make trade-off decisions and defend them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using customer insight from research, support and sales as well as team data, and taking ownership of business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear voice in shaping roadmap, sequencing and scope, and the ability to push back, including when the system is being bypassed, without damaging the relationship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience integrating or consolidating design systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with content and localisation considerations in components.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Perk</strong><br />AI is embedded in how we work across every function. The tools you'll use day-to-day are AI-enabled so you can move faster and spend more time on the work that matters. In practice, that means using AI to research and prioritise accounts, draft and refine outreach, handle customer interactions more effectively, synthesise information, and cut through shadow work - the invisible tasks that pull people away from the work only they can do - so you can focus on relationships and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Perk, we take an IRL-first approach to work, where our team works together in-person 3 days a week. As such, this role requires you to be based within commuting distance of our hubs. We fundamentally believe in the value of meeting in real life to improve connectivity, productivity, creativity and ultimately making us a great place to work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For certain roles, we can help with relocation from anywhere in the world, English is the official language at the office. Please submit your resume in English if you choose to apply. Do not forget to submit an updated portfolio and/or resume.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk is a global company with a diverse customer base, and we want to make sure the people behind our product reflect that. We’re an equal opportunity employer, which means you’re welcome at Perk regardless of how you look, where you’re from, or anything else that makes you, well, you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All official communication from Perk will always come from email addresses ending in @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://perk.com">perk.com</a> or @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://externalperk.com">externalperk.com</a>, our verified social media channels, or recruiters listed on our official LinkedIn page. We will never ask you to pay for equipment, training, or fees, request sensitive personal information such as bank details early in the process, or communicate through unofficial apps like WhatsApp, Telegram, or Signal. If you receive a message claiming to be from Perk that seems suspicious, please do not respond. Forward it to <u>security [at] perk .com</u>, and we will confirm whether it is legitimate.<br /><br />#LI-Hybrid</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/perk/senior-design-systems-designer-london-35547","tags":["Design"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792690816},{"slug":"account-executive-manchester-332667","company_name":"Cytix","title":"Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an Account Executive to close new-logo business for Cytix in a market where most of the people you're calling haven't heard of us yet. <br />You'll be selling a product, not a service, into CISOs, security engineers and AppSec leads, which means the pitch has to work on its own merits rather than on brand recognition. This is a full-cycle closing role: you'll run discovery, demo and negotiation yourself, with support from the CRO on the harder deals while you build that muscle.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll carry mid-market opportunities to start, working alongside SDR-sourced pipeline as well as your own prospecting, with a clear path to Senior Account Executive as your quota, deal complexity and independence grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run full-cycle new-logo opportunities from qualified meeting through discovery, demo and close, sourced by SDR, Marketing and your own prospecting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generate some of your own pipeline alongside SDR support, prospecting into a clearly defined ideal customer profile.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run structured discovery calls solo, identifying pain and priorities for your primary buyer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close mid-market deals with negotiation support from the CRO as you build experience with more complex procurement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain your own weekly pipeline and forecast, developing commit accuracy over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work SDR and Customer Success handoffs as directed, keeping CRM records clean and up to date.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3–5 years' full-cycle closing experience in B2B SaaS, or a strong track record in an adjacent commercial role (for example SDR) ready to step up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record at or near 100% of quota (around £500k–£750k) in at least one of the last two years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real consultative selling instinct:</strong> you'd rather understand a prospect's problem than run a script at them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable prospecting and selling into accounts with little existing awareness of Cytix, energised by the challenge of a cold or lightly-worked start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Visible drive and competitiveness, and a willingness to take on unfamiliar deal types or buyer personas when asked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuinely bright and inquisitive</strong>: good follow-up questions come naturally to you, and you're genuinely curious about the product and the security market, including how software gets built and secured.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drawn to a business where new challenges show up daily; you want to take ownership of them and lean in, rather than needing everything mapped out in advance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable taking yourself out of your comfort zone when a deal or a buyer is unfamiliar territory.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll get</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off that works for you: Unlimited holiday policy, including a guaranteed 33 days plus your birthday off</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible hybrid working: Work in a way that helps you do your best work, while staying connected with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A stake in what we’re building: Eligible employees can participate in our EMI share option scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthcare that goes further: After one year’s service, access private healthcare through Vitality, including dental, optical, hearing and therapy cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">More ways to get around: Access our company car salary-sacrifice scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support for growing families: Enhanced maternity and paternity leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Cytix</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software never stops changing. Teams ship new code every day, through tickets, pull requests, releases, and increasingly with AI in the mix, but the way security keeps up with all that change hasn't really moved on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's the problem we're solving. Cytix helps organisations understand which software changes actually matter, what should happen next, and how to prove the right call was made. Security understood, in other words.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a small team with big plans, so every person we hire genuinely shapes what Cytix becomes. That's why we're upfront about our five values: we interview for all of them, and they matter to us more than a perfect CV. They're things you do, not things you are, so have a read and see if they sound like you.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make the first move</strong>. When the goal is clear but the path isn't, you get moving rather than waiting for perfect instructions. If you're blocked, you make a sensible call, say what you're assuming, and explain how you'd course-correct. We'd rather you act and be slightly wrong than sit still.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Find the smarter path.</strong> You ask why before how. You dig into what the real problem is instead of just building what the spec says, and you're happy to question 'that's how it's always been done' when the reason behind it has gone stale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>See it through. </strong>When something's yours, it lands. No loose ends, no surprises for whoever picks it up next. You keep people posted when things change, and if something falls between roles, you catch it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the bar.</strong> You do the best job possible in the time you've got, whether that's a day or a month. Sometimes that means deep craft; sometimes the smartest move is quick and scrappy. It's about good judgement, and we hold each other to it without blame or politics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to win.</strong> You care about the mission but don't take yourself too seriously. You say 'I' when things go wrong and 'we' when they go right, trust teammates to do things their own way, and bring a bit of humour when the pressure's on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: £50K – £70K • OTE - uncapped 50/50</p><ul><li>Account Executive • Estimate Base Salary £50K – £70K • OTE - uncapped 50/50</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cytix/account-executive-manchester-332667","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792690814},{"slug":"sales-evergreen-moorgate-419707","company_name":"Checkatrade","title":"Sales Evergreen","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Powering Great Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started as the place to find a trusted trade. Now, as we shape the future of home improvement, we're building the tech to transform that landscape for everyone - better products, smarter data, AI where it actually helps - so trades can spend less time on admin and consumers can find someone they trust, first time. That's Powering Great Work, and it's why every team here exists:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔧 Trades spend less time on admin and more on winning work 