duct or even a name. The studio's work spans wherever a market and the data or infrastructure underneath it are broken enough to justify building the fix from scratch.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000"> </span></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#000000">About The General Data Corporation</span></strong></h2><p><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://generaldata.io/"><span style="color:#1155CC">General Data</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> is the infrastructure for licensing proprietary data: The platform runs the whole deal from request to delivery, with privacy checks, rights evidence and contracts built in. The vision is to become the system of record between AI and the world’s private data, the data that has never been published but that the next generation of AI depends on. On one side are enterprises, AI labs and robotics teams that need real-world data, and on the other are companies whose operations generate it. General Data is the data infrastructure for the modern economy, connecting every party so that data can be licensed safely, transparently and at scale.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2><strong><span style="color:#000000">Why this is a unique opportunity</span></strong></h2><p><span style="color:#121317">AI has absorbed the public internet, and its next gains will come from private, real-world data, yet today these deals still run on email, WhatsApp and brokers, with no visibility into what was checked, who holds the rights, or whether personal data was removed. Labs are already paying for this data, and regulation like GDPR and the EU Data Act makes a trusted, verifiable layer a necessity. </span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">General Data is VC-backed and looking for its technical co-founder. Together with Founder &amp; CEO </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/louaiallani/?isSelfProfile=false"><span style="color:#121317">Louai Allani</span></a></u><span style="col