g, diagnostics, data acquisition and analysis that support engineering and field activities.</p><p>- Documentation & Continuous Improvement: Maintain clear software and interface documentation and improve existing code as Traila products mature from development into deployed systems.</p><p> </p><p><strong>What you bring</strong></p><p>- Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Automation, Mechatronics or a related discipline, or equivalent practical technical experience.</p><p>- Hands-on professional software-development experience in an industrial, automation, automotive, machinery or comparable technical environment.</p><p>- Proven professional railway software experience, including products released and maintained in service.</p><p>- Strong practical programming skills in C++, C#, Python or a comparable industrial software stack; you do not need to be an expert in every language listed.</p><p>- Experience developing software that interacts with real hardware, devices or physical systems.</p><p>- Experience taking software beyond prototypes into tested, maintainable and deployable industrial use.</p><p>- Practical railway software lifecycle experience aligned with EN 50716:2023, including requirements traceability, configuration management and verification/validation appropriate to the required software integrity level; relevant EN 50128 / EN 50657 predecessor experience is also valuable.</p><p>- Practical embedded or industrial cybersecurity experience, including secure credentials and access, signed software updates and rollback, and handling vulnerabilities in released products.</p><p>- Strong debugging and troubleshooting skills across software, communication and hardware interfaces.</p><p>- Experience with Git and structured software-development workflows.</p><p>- A practical ownership mindset: comfortable working directly with prototypes, test equipment and deployed systems and driving technical problems through to resolution