strong>Praxisaufgabe:</strong> Gemeinsame Bearbeitung einer realistischen Recruiting- und People-Herausforderung.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kennenlernen des Teams:</strong> Gespräche vor Ort in Zürich, um herauszufinden, ob wir gut zueinander passen.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Unsere Werte</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bei Rivia setzen wir auf Spitzenleistung, kontinuierliches Lernen und den Erfolg unserer Kund:innen und unseres Teams.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mit vollem Einsatz gewinnen:</strong> Herausforderungen mit Entschlossenheit, Ausdauer und Tatkraft angehen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Veränderung annehmen:</strong> Wandel als Chance zur Verbesserung sehen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Warum eigentlich nicht?:</strong> Annahmen hinterfragen und neugierig bleiben.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lücken erkennen:</strong> Probleme frühzeitig identifizieren und lösen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Gemeinsam Verantwortung übernehmen:</strong> Zusammen für Ergebnisse einstehen und einander unterstützen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lösungen mit Mehrwert schaffen:</strong> Sinnvolle Ergebnisse erzielen, die wirklich etwas bewirken.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/rivia/sr-talent-people-partner-zurich-36947","tags":["People"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792518043},{"slug":"senior-integration-engineer-erp-oracle-zurich-458781","company_name":"BLP Digital AG","title":"(Senior) Integration Engineer, ERP (Oracle)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join BLP and help make the world’s business processes autonomous! </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our agentic platform helps finance and operations teams worldwide remove manual work from their core business processes, so work runs end-to-end with greater control and significant productivity gains. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, over 550 enterprise customers use BLP across 1,300+ deployed projects. In the processes we automate, customers achieve productivity improvements of 5 to 10 times. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To date, BLP remains majority employee-owned, with Goldman Sachs holding a minority stake as a growth investor. Our success is driven by deep expertise in technology and business processes, a superior product with strong product-market fit, reflected in an expanding customer base that includes Fortune 500 companies. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP is one of Switzerland's fastest-growing SaaS scale-ups; we are now entering our next phase of growth. From our headquarters on Zürich's Bahnhofstrasse, we're expanding globally, with a growing presence across Europe and North America. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Join us and help make autonomous operations the new standard. </em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">BLP only works when it talks to our customers’ ERP systems. As an Integration Engineer, you build and own those connections and keep live integrations running for enterprise customers. Every new ERP system is a new problem to solve. You’ll lead our Oracle integrations across Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, NetSuite and JD Edwards, while also contributing to other integrations.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you’ll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own our integrations with Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, NetSuite and JD Edwards and ensure their market fit, usability and reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and implement interfaces for diverse protocols: REST, SOAP, direct DB access and file transfers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore new ERP systems and determine the best way to connect them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build new ERP integrations, often in close collaboration with pilot customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own existing integrations end to end, including issue resolution, and document them so teammates can pick them up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable technical project managers to consult on, install and configure mature integrations.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on integration experience with Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, NetSuite or JD Edwards EnterpriseOne, ideally more than one. You have built or maintained interfaces yourself, not only used the system as a functional consultant or key user.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with the native interfaces of at least one of these:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP:</strong> REST and SOAP web services, File-Based Data Import (FBDI) through the ERP Integration Service, and data extraction with BI Publisher or BI Cloud Connector (BICC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>NetSuite:</strong> SuiteTalk REST and SOAP web services, SuiteQL, SuiteScript 2.x (e.g., RESTlets, Map/Reduce scripts), and Token-Based Authentication or OAuth 2.0.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>JD Edwards EnterpriseOne:</strong> AIS Server and Orchestrator, Business Services (BSSV), and Z-file interface tables (e.g., F0411Z1) with their batch processors.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A good understanding of purchase-to-pay data in Oracle ERPs: suppliers, purchase orders, receipts and supplier invoice matching.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid programming skills in at least one backend language. We build our integrations in Go. If you come from Java, C#, Python or similar and are keen to pick up Go, that works for us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A degree in computer science or a related field, or equivalent experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, self-reliant way of working, and ideally experience in a client-facing role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English. German is a plus, as most of our customers are in the DACH region.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with both cloud (Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, NetSuite) and on-premise (JD Edwards) environments, and the constraints of each (e.g., no direct database access in Fusion, governance limits in NetSuite).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience with SQL, common data formats (JSON, XML, CSV) and transports (REST/SOAP APIs, SFTP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with modern engineering practices: Git, code reviews, automated testing and CI/CD.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integration experience with other ERPs, such as SAP, Microsoft Dynamics or Infor.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Integration Engineer or Senior Integration Engineer</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>We hire at both levels. </u></strong>Four things decide where you start: years of experience, breadth of experience, coaching experience and scope.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integration Engineer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Years:</strong> 2+ years of hands-on integration work, including Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP, NetSuite or JD Edwards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Breadth:</strong> in-depth experience with one Oracle ERP and its interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><