 van PLC- en SCADA-systemen</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="heading-quartary electric-purple mb-10" style="text-align:start;">Nice to have</h3><ul><li><p>Kennis van industriële besturingssystemen en -netwerken</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met het opstellen van technische en functionele specificaties</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met inbedrijfstelling bij industriële klanten op locatie</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Soft skills</h3><ul><li><p>Zelfstandig en oplossingsgericht</p></li><li><p>Goede communicatieve vaardigheden richting klant en team</p></li><li><p>Praktisch en hands-on ingesteld</p></li><li><p>Leergierig en flexibel inzetbaar op wisselende projecten<br></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gradematch/automation-engineer-weert-293161","tags":["Industrial Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Weert, Limburg, Nederland","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"plc-software-engineer-helmond-114608","company_name":"GradeMatch","title":"PLC Software Engineer","description":"<h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>De uitdaging</strong></h2><p>Wij zoeken per direct een PLC Software Engineer voor onze klant in de regio Echt. Onze klant ontwikkelt en bouwt hoogwaardige verpakkingsmachines voor de voedingsmiddelenindustrie en levert klantspecifieke oplossingen voor de eindverpakking van zowel flexibele als vormvaste producten aan klanten over de hele wereld.</p><p>De machines worden aangestuurd via hightech besturingssystemen die volledig in-house door software engineers worden geprogrammeerd. Het gaat om uiteenlopende machines met complexe, meervoudige (master-slave) bewegingen. Als PLC Software Engineer ontwikkel en onderhoud jij de PLC- en HMI-software voor deze verpakkingslijnen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p>Als <strong>PLC Software Engineer</strong> ontwikkel en onderhoud jij de PLC- en HMI-software voor deze verpakkingslijnen, met uiteenlopende machines met complexe, meervoudige (master-slave) bewegingen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Je werkzaamheden bestaan onder andere uit:</p><ul><li><p>Ontwikkelen en onderhouden van PLC- en HMI-software voor machines met complexe, meervoudige bewegingen</p></li><li><p>Testen van de software, machines in bedrijf stellen en storingen en technische knelpunten oplossen</p></li><li><p>Zorgen voor heldere technische documentatie van de ontwikkelde besturingssoftware</p></li><li><p>Nauw samenwerken met hardware engineers, projectleiders en collega-softwareontwikkelaars binnen het projectteam</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Hoe je impact maakt</strong></h2><p>Als PLC Software Engineer zorg jij dat complexe machines betrouwbaar en efficiënt draaien. Door robuuste besturingssoftware te bouwen, draag je direct bij aan de kwaliteit en continuïteit van de machines die wereldwijd bij klanten in bedrijf zijn.<br></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat je van ons krijgt</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Salaris: €3.600 – €5.250 bruto per maand (bij 40 uur)</p></li><li><p>Een afwisselende functie binnen een hightech, internationaal georiënteerde omgeving</p></li><li><p>Ruimte voor persoonlijke ontwikkeling en het volgen van vakgerichte opleidingen</p></li><li><p>Reiskostenvergoeding of mobiliteitsoplossing in overleg</p></li><li><p>Een informele werksfeer met korte lijnen en betrokken collega's</p></li><li><p>Volop ruimte voor initiatief en eigen inbreng in projecten<br></p></li></ul><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat het jou oplevert</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Werken aan technisch uitdagende, complexe machines</p></li><li><p>Verdieping in PLC- en HMI-software voor hightech productielijnen</p></li><li><p>Korte lijnen en veel eigen verantwoordelijkheid</p></li><li><p>Samenwerken in een hecht, multidisciplinair projectteam</p></li><li><p>Zicht op je software in machines die wereldwijd worden ingezet</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Takenverdeling</strong></h2><p><strong>35%</strong> Ontwikkelen en onderhouden van PLC- en HMI-software<br><strong>30%</strong> Testen en inbedrijfstellen van machines<br><strong>15%</strong> Documentatie van besturingssoftware<br><strong>20%</strong> Samenwerking binnen het projectteam</p><p><br></p> <br> <h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Hard skills</h3><ul><li><p>HBO-opleiding in Elektrotechniek, Werktuigbouwkunde, Mechatronica of vergelijkbaar</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met het ontwikkelen en programmeren van PLC- en HMI-software</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="heading-quartary electric-purple mb-10" style="text-align:start;">Nice to have</h3><ul><li><p>Affiniteit met machines met complexe, meervoudige (master-slave) bewegingen</p></li><li><p>Sterk analytisch en oplossingsgericht vermogen</p></li><li><p>Ervaring binnen de machinebouw of verpakkingsindustrie</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Soft skills</h3><ul><li><p>Nauwkeurig en resultaatgericht</p></li><li><p>Zelfstandig, met oog voor samenwerking in het team</p></li><li><p>Praktisch en hands-on ingesteld</p></li><li><p>Leergierig en gedreven om door te ontwikkelen<br></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gradematch/plc-software-engineer-helmond-114608","tags":["Industrial Engineering"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Helmond, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"lead-software-engineer-plc-industry-helmond-351592","company_name":"GradeMatch","title":"Lead Software Engineer PLC & Industry","description":"<h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>De uitdaging</strong></h2><p>Complexe machines vragen om software die vanaf het eerste ontwerp klopt. PLC-besturing, motion, robotica, hardware en mechanica moeten naadloos samenwerken. En bij machines die nog niet eerder zijn gebouwd, ligt de oplossing niet vooraf klaar.</p><p>Als Lead Software Engineer PLC &amp; Industrial Automation neem jij de technische leiding over de softwareontwikkeling binnen complexe hightech machinebouw. Je vertaalt functionele eisen en klantwensen naar een robuuste besturingsoplossing en bewaakt de technische keuzes van ontwerp en architectuur tot commissioning en ingebruikname.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong></h2><p>Je bent technisch verantwoordelijk voor de software binnen multidisciplinaire machinebouwprojecten. Je vertaalt klantwensen en systeemeisen naar een softwarearchitectuur en bepaalt hoe de besturing wordt opgebouwd:</p><ul><li><p>Ontwerpen van softwarearchitectuur voor complexe machines</p></li><li><p>Ontwikkelen van PLC-software en oplossingen voor motion en robotica</p></li><li><p>Vertalen van requirements naar technische oplossingen</p></li><li><p>Inhoudelijk aansturen en begeleiden van software engineers</p></li><li><p>Afstemmen met system, mechanical en electrical engineering</p></li><li><p>Bewaken van technische keuzes, kwaliteit en voortgang</p></li><li><p>Testen, debuggen en commissionen van machines</p></li><li><p>Technische afstemming met klanten tijdens het project</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Hoe je impact maakt</strong></h2><p>Jouw keuzes bepalen hoe een machine wordt aangestuurd en hoe betrouwbaar deze uiteindelijk presteert. Je kijkt verder dan alleen de PLC-code en overziet de samenhang tussen software, motion, robotica, hardware en mechanica.<br>Je bent technisch aanspreekpunt voor engineers en klanten, neemt andere software engineers mee in technische keuzes en zorgt dat oplossingen niet alleen werken, maar ook robuust, onderhoudbaar en herbruikbaar zijn. Daarmee heb je direct invloed op zowel de machine als de manier waarop software binnen toekomstige projecten wordt ontwikkeld.<br></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat je van ons krijgt</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Salaris van €4.000 – €7.500 bruto per maand</p></li><li><p>27 vakantiedagen + 13 ADV-dagen</p></li><li><p>Jaarlijkse winstuitkering</p></li><li><p>Goede pensioenregeling</p></li><li><p>Reiskostenvergoeding</p></li><li><p>Veel ruimte voor opleidingen en technische ontwikkeling<br></p></li></ul><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Wat het jou oplevert</strong></h2><p>Je krijgt een rol waarin je niet alleen software bouwt, maar bepaalt hoe de besturing van een nieuwe machine technisch wordt opgezet:</p><ul><li><p>Bepaal de softwarearchitectuur voor nieuwe hightech machines</p></li><li><p>Combineer PLC-besturing met motion en robotica</p></li><li><p>Bespreek technische oplossingen en keuzes rechtstreeks met klanten</p></li><li><p>Geef inhoudelijk richting aan andere software engineers</p></li><li><p>Volg jouw ontwerp van eerste requirements tot commissioning</p></li><li><p>Bouw standaarden en softwarecomponenten die in volgende machines opnieuw worden gebruikt</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h2 class="ct-headline heading-secondary electric-purple"><strong>Takenverdeling</strong></h2><p><strong>30%</strong> Softwarearchitectuur &amp; technisch ontwerp<br><strong>25%</strong> PLC, motion &amp; robotica ontwikkelen<br><strong>20%</strong> Technische afstemming met klanten &amp; engineering<br><strong>15%</strong> Software engineers inhoudelijk aansturen<br><strong>10%</strong> Testen, debugging &amp; commissioning</p> <br> <h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Hard skills</h3><ul><li><p>Hbo- of wo-diploma in een relevante technische richting</p></li><li><p>Minimaal 5 jaar software-engineeringervaring</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met PLC-programmering (Siemens, Beckhoff en/of Allen-Bradley)</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met softwarearchitectuur voor PLC- en machinebesturing</p></li><li><p>Kennis van motion control en/of robotica</p></li><li><p>Kennis van objectgeoriënteerd programmeren (OOP)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="heading-quartary electric-purple mb-10" style="text-align:start;">Nice to have</h3><ul><li><p>Ervaring met hightech machinebouw</p></li><li><p>Ervaring binnen semicon of analytical systems</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met meerdere PLC-platformen</p></li><li><p>Ervaring met commissioning en debugging</p></li><li><p>Kennis van Agile/Scrum en het V-model</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="ct-headline electric-purple heading-quartary">Soft skills</h3><ul><li><p>Technisch leiderschap</p></li><li><p>Analytisch sterk</p></li><li><p>Communicatief sterk</p></li><li><p>Besluitvaardig</p></li><li><p>Klantgericht</p></li><li><p>Teamgericht<br></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/gradematch/lead-software-engineer-plc-industry-helmond-351592","tags":["Industrial Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Helmond, Noord-Brabant, Nederland","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"lead-analytics-engineer-rotterdam-137108","company_name":"AIHR","title":"Lead Analytics Engineer","description":"<p><span style="color:#121317">Do you love turning messy business questions into data people can trust? Can you connect the customer journey from the first marketing touch through sales conversion, revenue, retention, and product usage and explain the numbers equally clearly to an engineer, a CMO, and a CFO? AIHR is looking for a Lead Agentic Analytics Engineer to become the hands-on functional lead of our two-person Data &amp; Analytics team. You will own the translation of cross-functional business questions into trusted metrics, governed semantic models, and decision-ready agentic analytics; set the analytical direction; and build the most critical models yourself. You are transforming raw data into governed products that drive decision-making for our business partners.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About AIHR</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.aihr.com/"><span style="color:#1999e3">Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR)</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> has become the global market leader in online training for HR professionals. We support customers in more than 140 countries, including organizations such as Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. Our goal is to continuously upskill and empower one million HR professionals.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Today, we are an international team of more than 100 people representing over 30 nationalities. We are driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow, while staying friendly, enthusiastic, and committed to helping each other succeed.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Working at AIHR means taking real responsibility, improving how we operate, and getting the freedom to develop in new areas and shape your role as the company grows.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000"><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Role and Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">AIHR's Data &amp; Analytics team is part of Business Operations. You will work alongside Vahid, our Senior Data Engineer, and report to Leo, our VP of Business Operations. Our ingestion and warehouse foundation is largely established: data from systems such as HubSpot and our own LMS moves through ETL pipelines into Snowflake. Through special Projects, we are building governed semantic layers on top so the business can self-serve trusted analytics through Power BI, Metabase, and AI tools.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Your role owns the step that matters most: translating a business question into a clear definition, a well-designed model, and conversational/agentic analytics that your leadership trusts. You will set the analytical architecture, dbt standards, and roadmap, while Vahid focuses on ingestion, warehouse reliability, and engineering implementation. You will both build: you will personally deliver the most critical business models, review implementations, and ensure the outputs are usable by the business.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This role has no direct reports. Your colleague, Vahid, remains managed by the VP of Business Operations, while you have clear functional decision rights over metric definitions, semantic-model design, analytical quality, dbt standards, and technical priorities. It is designed for someone who wants to lead through expertise while remaining close to the work.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What You'll Own</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own and execute a rolling one-year Data &amp; Analytics roadmap, balancing urgent business needs with foundational work. Guide Vahid through clear priorities, design reviews, code review, and reusable modeling patterns.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead discovery across Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, Product, and Finance to uncover the decision behind a request and translate it into agreed metric definitions, governed semantic layers, and data models that connect the full customer lifecycle.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Set the analytical architecture and dbt standards; design, build, test, and document the most critical governed models yourself using SQL and dbt.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own the full-funnel measurement framework—from marketing reach, demand generation, attribution, and customer acquisition cost through lead and pipeline conversion, sales cycle, bookings, and revenue to onboarding, product adoption, expansion, renewal, churn, and customer lifetime value. Keep core recurring-revenue definitions finance-grade and reconciled while showing how upstream activity drives downstream customer outcomes.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own the logic and quality behind executive dashboards and self-service analytics across Power BI, Metabase, and AI-enabled interfaces. Present the results to senior leaders, explain every assumption, and respond constructively to challenge.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Partner closely with Vahid on warehouse and pipeline requirements, resolve conflicting numbers at the source, and raise the technical quality of the team. Apply AI where it improves development speed or data access, while using sound judgment around privacy, governance, validation, and trust.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">A Typical Week</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This is a hands-on lead role. The exact balance will shift with business priorities, but you should expect roughly half your time to remain close to the data—building, reviewing, and investigating—and the rest to be split across discovery, functional leadership, and decision support.<br></span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Design or improve a dbt model that connects data across HubSpot, our LMS, billing, or other source systems; write the SQL, tests, documentation, and metric logic needed to put it into production.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Run discovery sessions with leaders in Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, Product, or Finance to clarify the decision they need to make, challenge the requested metric, and agree on the definition.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work side by side with Vahid on source-data requirements, architecture choices, and implementation; review code and unblock delivery without handing off all of the technical work.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Investigate a commercial or customer-lifecycle question, improve an executive or functional dashboard, and present the conclusion—including assumptions and limitations—to the relevant leadership team.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Reprioritize the Data &amp; Analytics roadmap, resolve competing requests, and invest in the semantic layer, governance, and reusable modeling foundations that reduce future ad hoc work.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What Success Looks Like</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Within your first three months, you have established a clear operating model with Vahid, mapped ownership of the most important metrics, agreed the Data &amp; Analytics roadmap, and resolved at least one material conflicting-number problem.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Within six months, AIHR has a governed customer-lifecycle domain in dbt and an executive view connecting acquisition and pipeline to revenue, retention, and product usage, and has launched the first MVP of our agentic analytics platform to drive self-serve adoption. The underlying definitions are documented, reconciled where relevant, and trusted across Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, Product, and Finance.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Within twelve months, two or three priority business domains are governed end to end, leadership can trace performance from acquisition through lifetime value using consistent numbers, self-service adoption is growing, and Vahid can independently implement the modeling patterns and quality standards you established.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Throughout, you remain hands-on in SQL, dbt, Snowflake, and analytics while setting direction, coaching through the work, and earning leadership's trust in both the numbers and the roadmap.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">We offer</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high-impact role as the functional lead of a small Data &amp; Analytics team, with end-to-end ownership of the semantic layer behind company-wide decisions.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive, benchmarked compensation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Substantial autonomy to shape your day-to-day work, with regular growth conversations and support for your career goals.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Flexible working hours and work-from-home arrangements after onboarding.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">26 paid holidays per year, plus one extra day for each of your first five years at AIHR.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">The option to exchange any two public holidays for two days of your choice.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A work-from-anywhere policy that lets you work abroad for up to 20 days per calendar year.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A pension plan, four Trust Days for ad hoc recovery, and access to the OpenUp mental health platform.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A personal development budget, training opportunities, and the books you need to keep learning.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">All public-transport expenses covered through an NS Business Card, plus a MacBook and the equipment you need.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A beautiful office opposite Rotterdam Central Station, a satellite office in Amsterdam, daily chef-prepared lunch, regular drinks, team activities, and free access to the office gym.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Get a taste of working at AIHR in our </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://aihr.recruitee.com/benefits-guide"><span style="color:#1999e3">AIHR Benefits Guide</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000">.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Apply for the Job</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you excited to become our Lead Analytics Engineer? We would love to hear from you. We are aiming for a start date in December 2026 or January 2027.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">P.S. If this role excites you but you do not meet every point, we still encourage you to apply. We care about the evidence behind your experience and your potential to grow—not a perfect checklist.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">You are a hands-on technical leader: commercially sharp, calm under challenge, and confident enough to defend your numbers in any room. You also have the patience to build data foundations properly and raise the quality of the work around you.<br></span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You bring 5+ years of experience across analytics engineering, BI, data engineering, or business-facing analytics roles, including substantial recent hands-on analytics engineering and evidence of leading work beyond your own delivery.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have a proven track record of building semantic layers or governed dimensional models end-to-end—from business discovery and metric definition to production models and adoption—not only dashboards.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have expert SQL and data modeling skills, strong production experience with dbt, and hands-on experience with Snowflake or a comparable warehouse, along with a BI tool such as Power BI, Looker, Omni, or Metabase.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You bring strong financial acumen, but your analytical experience extends across the full customer lifecycle. You can connect marketing acquisition and attribution, sales pipeline and conversion, revenue and unit economics, customer retention and expansion, and product adoption into one coherent model. You understand how bookings, billings, recognized revenue, cash, ARR, and NRR differ without treating financial reporting as the whole analytical problem.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You have worked in a B2B SaaS, subscription, fintech, or marketplace business and have modeled several stages of the funnel spanning marketing or growth, sales, customer success and retention, and product usage—rather than specializing in only one function.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You explain complex logic in plain language, push back constructively on senior stakeholders, and build trust without becoming defensive—even when you discover that your own number or assumption needs to change.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You take pride in driving the analytical roadmap and architectural vision, leading technical work through architecture and code review, and mentoring experienced colleagues without relying on formal authority. You want the majority of your role to remain hands-on.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You balance pragmatic execution with rigorous analysis, adapting precision levels to fit business needs and operational constraints.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You are used to leveraging a broad range of AI tools to boost your productivity and know how to configure them to produce output that lives up to our quality standards and best practices</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Nice to Have</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Earlier experience in RevOps, Growth, FP&amp;A, product analytics, or commercial analytics, ideally combined with experience in a fast-growing scale-up.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with HubSpot, marketing automation and attribution data, subscription or billing data, LMS or product-usage event data, Personio, or building semantic layers for AI-enabled and conversational analytics.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aihr/lead-analytics-engineer-rotterdam-137108","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Manager","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"senior-sales-operations-salesops-manager-rotterdam-326112","company_name":"AIHR","title":"Senior Sales Operations (SalesOps) Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Do you like making it easier for a Sales team to do its best work? Do you enjoy owning the details that keep deals moving, while also spotting where the process could work better? And do you get satisfaction from turning repetitive work into a simpler, smarter way of working?</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">AIHR is looking for a </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Senior Sales Operations Manager</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> to join our Revenue Operations team. You’ll help support more than </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">€10 million in annual deal value</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, working closely with Sales leadership while owning the operational processes that move deals from opportunity to collected revenue.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About AIHR</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://www.aihr.com/"><span style="color:#1999e3">Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR)</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000"> has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spread across 140+ countries, amongst which companies like Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are an international team of 90+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility and getting countless opportunities to develop yourself in new areas and potential to craft your own role.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Role and Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As our Senior Sales Operations Manager, your job is to make it easier for Sales to do great work. This is a hands-on role with a broad view of the commercial journey. You’ll work on how Sales operates, support leadership with better insight, and own processes such as the Deal Desk, vendor registration, invoicing, collections, and order-to-cash.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We see those responsibilities as connected. Being close to the day-to-day work gives you the context to see where time is being lost, where a process no longer works, and where the same problem keeps coming back. We want someone who is comfortable doing the work themselves, but who does not simply accept unnecessary manual work because “that’s how we do it.”</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">This role is a combination of keeping things moving today and making sure they work better tomorrow.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Your responsibilities include:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Improving how Sales works.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You use data, feedback, and your understanding of the day-to-day work to identify where things can be better. That could mean redesigning a workflow, improving reporting, clarifying ownership, creating a better operating rhythm, or removing manual steps that no longer add value.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Helping Sales leadership improve performance.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You look beyond individual requests and help spot patterns across the Sales organization. Where are deals slowing down? What does the data tell us about why? Are we missing information in HubSpot that would help Sales, Marketing, or leadership make better decisions? You turn those observations into practical recommendations and are comfortable challenging existing ways of working when the data points somewhere else.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Owning and improving the Deal Desk.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> When a deal needs something outside the standard process, you help move it forward. This can include approvals, documentation, commercial questions, vendor or supplier registration, procurement portals, questionnaires, and coordination across internal and external stakeholders. You take care of the immediate need, while also looking for patterns that could make the next request simpler.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Owning order-to-cash and collections.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You take responsibility for turning booked revenue into collected cash. Collections is a meaningful and hands-on part of the role: monitoring outstanding invoices, following up with customers, picking up the phone when that is the best way to resolve an issue, and working with Sales, Finance, procurement teams, and other stakeholders to clear payment blockers. You also look at the process behind the work — reducing overdue balances, improving follow-up, and finding ways to make order-to-cash more effective over time.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Working AI-first.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You actively use AI and automation where they can make the work more efficient or improve the quality of the outcome. That might mean analyzing patterns in Sales data, speeding up vendor registration, improving a recurring workflow, or removing repetitive administrative work. As part of RevOps, you are expected to try new approaches, keep what works, and share useful ways of working with the wider team.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Connecting the dots across teams.</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Many commercial processes cross Sales, Finance, Customer Experience, Marketing, Operations, and other parts of the business. You help create clarity around ownership, bring the right people together, and make sure decisions turn into action.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">You’ll work with tools including </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">HubSpot, Gong, Atlassian, QuotaPath, Zapier, Google Workspace</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, and a growing set of AI tools and internal AI workflows. We do not expect you to arrive as an expert in every system. We do expect you to be comfortable learning how they fit together and questioning whether we are using them in the best way.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Success in this role is not simply an empty queue or a dashboard that looks good. It is reliable day-to-day execution combined with steady improvement in how Sales operates.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">On a typical day</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Monday morning, you start by getting a view of the commercial week ahead. You check active deals in HubSpot, outstanding operational requests, the payments inbox, and anything else that needs attention.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">During the RevOps stand-up with the RevOps team, you talk through priorities. An Account Executive is working on an enterprise opportunity where the customer's procurement team needs AIHR registered as a vendor. Several invoices need follow-up. You have also noticed a group of deals spending longer than expected in one stage of the pipeline.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">The vendor registration comes first. You use one of our existing AI workflows to help complete the documentation, gather any missing information internally, and get the process moving. While doing that, you notice that part of the information the workflow relies on is out of date. Rather than working around it, you fix the source and make sure the next registration is easier.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Later, you turn to the stalled opportunities. You dig into the data, speak with the Sales team, and find that Account Executives are not consistently recording meeting outcomes. That makes it difficult to understand why certain MQLs progress while others do not.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">The answer may not be “Sales needs to update HubSpot more.” You look at why the information is not being captured in the first place and whether the workflow can be made easier for reps while still giving Marketing and leadership the information they need. You believe it’s easier to change a process than to change human behaviors.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After lunch with colleagues in the office, you spend time on collections. Some invoices need a straightforward reminder. Others need more persistence. You follow up with customers, get on the phone where needed, and work through issues involving purchase orders, invoicing details, procurement processes, or internal ownership.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">This work is part of the role, not something sitting outside it. And because you are doing it yourself, you see first-hand which issues are one-offs and which ones point to something we should fix.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On another day, you sit down with Sales leadership to look at commercial performance. You are not there simply to report what happened. You help interpret what is behind the numbers and what we might do differently.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You also regularly connect with </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Neal, Head of CX &amp; Operations</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, and colleagues across Business Operations. Some weeks you will spend more time on live operational work; other weeks give you more room to improve reporting, build an automation in Zapier, clean up a process in HubSpot, or work on a broader RevOps project.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">That balance is part of the role.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">By Friday, a good week means the work got done: customers were followed up, deals moved forward, Sales had the support they needed, and something in the way we operate is now a little clearer or easier than it was before.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">We offer</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high-impact role working closely with Sales leadership and the wider Business Operations organization;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">The opportunity to own important commercial processes while also improving how our Sales organization works;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Managing a growing deal volume of </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">€10M+ per year</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> across the commercial funnel;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive, benchmarked compensation;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">The opportunity to shape your own day-to-day work;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Regular growth talks and support to reach your career goals;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Flexible working hours &amp; working from home arrangements;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Access to AI tools including </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">the latest AI models</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> so you can automate repetitive work and improve how you operate day to day;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A beautiful office right across Rotterdam Central Station (Milleniumtower) and a satellite office in Amsterdam;</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">26 paid holidays per year + 1 extra day for the first 5 years you work at AIHR</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Exchange any 2 public holiday days for 2 other days of your choice;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Work from anywhere policy, where you can work abroad for 20 days in a calendar year;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Pension plan;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">4 Trust days per year (ad-hoc recovery days to take whenever you're overwhelmed, exhausted, or need to deal with something personal);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Access to OpenUp mental health platform;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Personal development budget, training, and we pay for the books you read;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">All public transport expenses covered (NS Business Card);</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">MacBook + all other equipment you need to do your work;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Daily lunch prepared by a chef, regular drinks, and fun team activities;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Free access to the office gym.</span></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">Get a taste of the AIHR experience and check out our </span><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://aihr.recruitee.com/benefits-guide"><span style="color:#1999e3">AIHR Benefits Guide</span></a></u><span style="color:#000000">!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Apply for the job</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Are you excited to become our Senior Sales Operations (SalesOps) Manager? Then we'd love to hear from you! We are looking to hire for this role as soon as we find an eligible candidate.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><em><span style="color:#000000">P.S. </span></em></strong><em><span style="color:#000000">Research shows that while men apply to jobs when they meet an average of 60% of the criteria, women tend to apply only when they meet 100% of them. So if you think you have what it takes, but don't necessarily meet every single point above, please still apply. We'd love to consider you and see if you could be a great fit.</span></em><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you are</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are looking for someone who combines strong operational execution with commercial awareness.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You are comfortable getting into the details and doing repetitive work when it needs to be done. At the same time, you tend to notice when the same issue keeps appearing and start thinking about how to remove it rather than simply processing it faster.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You are likely a strong fit if you:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Have solid experience in </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, Commercial Operations, or an end-to-end order-to-cash role</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> within a B2B environment, including hands-on exposure to collections;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Understand how B2B Sales processes work and can use data, operational signals, and feedback from Sales to identify where things could improve;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Are comfortable owning processes such as the </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Deal Desk, vendor registration, invoicing, collections, and order-to-cash</span></strong><span style="color:#000000">, even if you have not owned every one of them previously;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Are confident working with CRM data, spreadsheets, reporting, and operational tools. Experience with platforms such as </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">HubSpot, Gong, Atlassian, QuotaPath, Zapier, or Google Workspace</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> is useful, but curiosity and the ability to learn matter more than knowing our exact stack;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Communicate clearly across Sales, Finance, Operations, Marketing, and leadership, and are comfortable raising a different point of view when you believe there is a better way forward.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><span style="color:#000000">You do not need to match every point perfectly. What matters most is that you can combine ownership, attention to detail, analytical thinking, and the judgment to know when to execute the process and when to change it.</span></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/aihr/senior-sales-operations-salesops-manager-rotterdam-326112","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"senior-partnership-manager-rotterdam-319221","company_name":"AIHR","title":"Senior Partnership Manager","description":"<p><em><span style="color:#000000">Do you look at a partner program that works and immediately see what it could become at three times the size? Are you the kind of person who owns your number and a running book of business, while designing the channels that will carry the next phase of growth? Do you want a mandate that is yours: rethink how we work with resellers, open up consultancies and universities, and work out where tech partnerships fit? And do you like variety, where growing an existing commercial partner one day and presenting a new partner model to leadership the next is just part of the job?</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">AIHR is looking for a </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">Senior Partnership Manager</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> to grow our commercial partner book and build the partner programs that take us into the next phase of growth within our Sales Department. </span><em><span style="color:#000000">This is not a marketing position.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About AIHR</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR) has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spanning 140+ countries, including companies such as Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are an international team of 100+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility. For a senior hire, that means real ownership: the room to shape a commercial channel, direct access to leadership, and the potential to craft your own role as the program grows.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Role and Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As Senior Partnership Manager, you come in with the ambition to triple the AIHR partnership program. Today that program is a global portfolio of 130+ commercial partners driving primarily single-seat e-commerce sales, plus a reseller channel that brings in B2B business. Both work, and both have far more potential than we currently capture. Your job is to optimize what we have, evolve it into a set of structured commercial partner programs, and work out which new channels deserve investment.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">This is a quota-carrying role with a build mandate. You manage a running book of business with our existing commercial partners and stay their main point of contact. On top of that, you design and launch larger partner programs with resellers, HR consultancies, system integrators, and universities. We have a strong belief that these partners, HR implementation consultants in particular, are well placed to position our courses with their clients, and that this can become a major revenue stream for AIHR.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Your work is built from three connected workstreams:</span></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Grow the existing partner channel:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> run the existing book, grow partner revenue, and identify the commercial opportunities that drive meaningful additional business.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Build the extended partner programs:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> restructure the reseller program so it generates more predictable, repeatable B2B revenue, and extend it to consultancies, system integrators, and universities.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Define the tech partnership go-to-market:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> research which commercial models fit AIHR, propose the strategy, then test, validate, and build out what works.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You’ll report to the Team Lead for Channel &amp; Strategic Partnerships, work closely with Marketing, Sales, and Product to get your partners what they need, and act as the partnership network’s advocate across the wider commercial team. You will regularly present proposals and results to AIHR leadership.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">On a typical day</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On a typical Monday morning, you start with your pipeline. Your existing partner book is quick to review: a few conversations need a nudge, two QBRs are coming up. The larger partnerships take more thought. Other companies in our industry have built significant revenue through resellers, consultancies, and universities, but these deals have a longer sales cycle, so you always keep several opportunities moving at the same time. Today that means a value-added reseller in the middle of a negotiation, a prospective university that wants to add AIHR’s courses to its 2027 academic year, and a consultancy that signed last month and now needs to get moving.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">After lunch you speak with the managing partner of a German niche consultancy that does a lot of HR implementation work. Her clients keep running into the same problem: the new system goes live, and the HR team lacks the skills to get the most out of it. You talk through how capability building could become part of her offering, with AIHR as the partner behind it. She is interested, and you agree to work out a commercial proposal together. Next you work on an enablement session for consultants, covering what they need to know about our courses, how they bring AIHR into a client conversation, what a first joint win could look like, and you brief Marketing on the materials their consultants will need.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">The next morning is for outreach. You build a sourcing list of potential partners in a segment you want to open up, and you contact them yourself. AIHR has a very good name in the HR industry, and that usually helps open doors. Later that week you run a QBR with one of your strongest commercial partners. You review their numbers together, agree on two concrete actions, and set a date to check back in. You identify where there is room to grow the relationship and push for more where performance has stalled. You also notice that a large part of their customer base works in corporate HR teams, so you bring in a colleague from Sales to explore a B2B opportunity through the same relationship.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">On Thursday you are back with the value-added reseller. They want to bundle our courses with their own services. It is a model we haven’t proven yet. There is no standard agreement to pull off the shelf, so you work with our Sales Engineer to design the deal while you negotiate it: what they sell, how they are rewarded, how revenue is generated, and what would tell you both it is working. You treat it as a pilot and agree on a first version you can learn from. Some of these experiments will not work out. The ones that do become the programs you build the channel on, and you will be the person who figured them out.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You close out the week updating your forecast and walking your manager through where the existing book, pipeline, and new programs stand. Friday afternoon wraps with a quick team catch-up and, if you're in the Rotterdam office, our regular Friday drinks.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your Target</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">This is a quota-carrying role. Your number is built from the revenue of the partner book you run and the new partner programs you launch. In your first year, that means growing revenue across the existing partner portfolio, a restructured reseller program, the first signed partners among consultancies, system integrators, and universities, and a tech partnership go-to-market strategy that has been proposed, tested, and started generating commercial opportunities.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">We offer</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Competitive, benchmarked compensation, including a commission plan tied to your target</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A beautiful office r