#EFF6FF"> </span>application<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>procedure<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>at<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>Benchmark.<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> <br><br></span><em>Acquisition<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>is<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>not<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>appreciated.<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>No<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>rights<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>or<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>obligations<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>can<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>be<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>derived<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>from<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>the<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>introduction<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>of<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>candidates<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>without<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>an<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>assignment,<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>from<span style="background-color:#EFF6FF"> </span>HR.<br></em></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="color:#2f5496">Apply today and help us build the next generation of high-performance technology solutions at Benchmark.</span></strong></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/benchmark/software-integration-engineer-c-linux-almelo-39224","tags":["Design Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Almelo, Overijssel, Nederland","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"medior-c-software-engineer-utrecht-382349","company_name":"Vitestro","title":"Medior C++ Software Engineer","description":"<p style="text-align:start;"><strong>About Vitestro</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">Founded in 2017 in Utrecht, Vitestro is pioneering the future of blood collection with the<strong> Aletta® Autonomous Robotic Phlebotomy Device™&nbsp;(ARPD™)</strong>. This groundbreaking medical device combines advanced multi-modal imaging (near-infrared, ultrasound, and Doppler ultrasound) with robotics and AI to perform the entire diagnostic blood draw procedure autonomously.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">By addressing critical healthcare staffing shortages and improving patient experience, Vitestro is transforming one of the most common and essential medical procedures. With more than 130 team members and growing rapidly, we are scaling our impact. As we placed our first devices with customers, we are now expanding our team to ensure successful implementation and long-term reliability.</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:start;">At Vitestro, we are committed to continuous innovation and improvement.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">As a Medior C++ Engineer, you will take ownership of software components within our hardware-integrated systems. You will design, implement, and improve robust C++ software that interacts with multiple subsystems, and real-time environments. You will collaborate closely with hardware engineers, systems engineers, and other software developers to ensure system reliability, maintainability, and performance.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0"><strong>First months at Vitestro</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">In your first months, you get to know Vitestro's software architecture, hardware-integrated systems, and development processes. You build an understanding of how our software interacts with different subsystems and start contributing to the design, implementation, and improvement of software components in modern C++ (C++17/20).</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Working closely with hardware engineers, systems engineers, and other software developers, you become familiar with our state-machine-based logic, DDS communication protocols, and Linux and real-time environments. You contribute to debugging, automated testing, and code reviews while building the knowledge needed to take ownership of software components.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">After your first month you will be able to contribute to the velocity of the team by working on new features in the scope of the motion team. You will be able to solve complex integration issues coming from production and the field.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0"><strong>This is what success looks like</strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">After 12 months, you have taken ownership of software components within our hardware-integrated systems. You confidently design, implement, and maintain robust C++ software that interacts with multiple subsystems and real-time environments.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">You actively contribute to improving the existing software architecture, ensuring maintainability, scalability, and performance. You design and maintain structured state-machine-based logic, integrate evolving hardware components into the software stack, and contribute to system-level design discussions and technical decisions.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">You work effectively with hardware engineers, systems engineers, and other software developers to debug complex issues across software and hardware boundaries. You have contributed to improving testability and automated verification strategies, actively participate in code reviews, and help raise software quality standards.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">After your first year, you will own significant nontrivial features and parts of the code-base of the team. You will be a key knowledge holder of the implementation of the motion software unit as well as accuracy calibrations and verifications. You actively engage in building the roadmap for the coming years together with other engineers.</p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0"><strong>What You'll Bring:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Master's degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related technical field.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">4–7 years of experience developing C++ software in a professional environment.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Proven experience designing and maintaining production-level software systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Strong proficiency in modern C++ (C++17/20).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience structuring code for maintainability and scalability.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience with automated testing.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience working in Linux environments.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Strong debugging skills in complex systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Proficiency with Git and collaborative workflows.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0"><strong>Nice to Have:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience designing and implementing state machines.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience with hardware–software integration.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Familiarity with DDS or similar pub/sub communication frameworks.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Experience working in real-time or near real-time systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Python scripting experience.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW26816889 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW26816889 BCX0">Exposure to robotics or industrial communication protocols (EtherCAT, CANopen).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;">Competitive salary including pension plan</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">25 days of annual leave based on a full-time position</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Hybrid work model</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Working together in a high-skilled team with our home base in Utrecht</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Frequent out-of-work activities with our team, and annual company weekend away</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Annual training budget of €2000,-</p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;">Opportunity to be key shaper of a new global industry niche: autonomous medical robotics</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;">We offer an environment where you can make a lot of impact, as you are joining a growing scale-up in MedTech. Our team of driven and talented colleagues enjoys solving the challenges in developing, manufacturing, and completing our breakthrough medical device. While working in an open culture, we strive for excellence in all domains. We believe in taking courage and like to challenge each other. We learn and teach, regardless of age, nationality or gender.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vitestro/medior-c-software-engineer-utrecht-382349","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Utrecht, Utrecht, Netherlands","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"senior-quality-systems-officer-utrecht-167763","company_name":"Vitestro","title":"Senior Quality Systems Officer","description":"<p class="MsoNormal"><strong>About Vitestro</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">Founded in 2017 in Utrecht, Vitestro is pioneering the future of blood collection with the<strong> Aletta® Autonomous Robotic Phlebotomy Device™&nbsp;(ARPD™)</strong>. This groundbreaking medical device combines advanced multi-modal imaging (near-infrared, ultrasound, and Doppler ultrasound) with robotics and AI to perform the entire diagnostic blood draw procedure autonomously.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">By addressing critical healthcare staffing shortages and improving patient experience, Vitestro is transforming one of the most common and essential medical procedures. With more than 130 team members and growing rapidly, we are scaling our impact. As we placed our first devices with customers, we are now expanding our team to ensure successful implementation and long-term reliability.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal">At Vitestro, we are committed to continuous innovation and improvement. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">As our Senior QS officer, you focus on the continuous improvement of our quality systems and support the company through the change control process. You review existing quality processes, identify where they can be improved or made more compliant, and help develop practical solutions to make those improvements happen.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">You also guide colleagues through change control. Rather than executing every change yourself, you ensure people understand and follow the process, ask the right questions, consider the relevant implications, obtain the necessary approvals, and ensure that changes are  completed Correctly and on time.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This role requires a strong analytical and systematic mindset combined with a pragmatic approach to quality. You should be comfortable identifying problems, but more importantly, finding workable solutions and alternatives. You understand the requirements of working in a regulated environment without approaching quality as simply enforcing rules. You are able to adapt, think creatively and help the organisation find compliant ways forward.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>First months at Vitestro </strong></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">In your first months, you get to know Vitestro’s quality systems, processes, and the teams working with them. You build a thorough understanding of our Change Control process and start supporting colleagues through changes, helping them consider the right questions and ensuring changes are complete, appropriately approved, and progressing on time. As you become familiar with how we work, you identify opportunities to improve the compliance and efficiency of the Change Control process and develop a clear plan for implementing those improvements.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>This is what success looks like: </strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">After 12 months, you are a trusted partner for colleagues working with our quality systems and Change Control process. You confidently support the organization in executing changes, ensuring they are well considered, appropriately approved, and completed on time. You have improved the Change Control process to strengthen both compliance and efficiency, and have identified and implemented improvements across other areas of the QMS. You combine strong analytical thinking with a pragmatic and creative approach. You don’t just identify where something could be improved; you translate those insights into practical solutions and, when one approach doesn’t work, find alternative ways forward.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="Paragraph SCXW54022507 BCX8"><strong>What You’ll Bring:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW54022507 BCX8"><li><p>Strong analytical thinking and the ability to assess existing processes, identify where issues occur and determine how they can be improved.</p></li><li><p>Experience working in a regulated environment.</p></li><li><p>Relevant professional experience that provides an understanding of how quality systems and processes work.</p></li><li><p>A systematic, process-oriented way of working.</p></li><li><p>The ability to identify and develop solutions to quality and process problems.</p></li><li><p>A pragmatic and adaptable mindset, with the ability to think beyond rigid or established approaches while respecting regulatory requirements.</p></li><li><p>The ability to guide colleagues through processes by asking questions, highlighting considerations and ensuring required steps are completed.</p></li><li><p>Bachelor’s degree or higher in engineering, applied sciences, biomedical engineering, or similar technical field</p></li><li><p>Minimum 3 to 5 years experience in Quality Assurance / Quality Systems for medical devices.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Nice to have:</strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW15081406 BCX8"><li><p>Experience across multiple organisations or environments, providing exposure to different ways of working.</p></li><li><p>Medical-device experience can be relevant but is not required.</p></li><li><p>Experience with MDSAP </p><p class="Paragraph SCXW15081406 BCX8" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p>At Vitestro, ownership is not a slogan - it is an expectation. We trust people to take responsibility, make decisions, and drive work forward.</p><p>We believe breakthroughs happen when talented people combine dedication, accountability, and teamwork. That means:</p><ul><li><p>We take initiative rather than wait for direction.</p></li><li><p>We focus on execution and delivering results.</p></li><li><p>We proactively remove blockers and help each other succeed.</p></li><li><p>We challenge ideas, not people.</p></li><li><p>We continuously learn, improve, and raise the bar.</p></li><li><p>We celebrate team success over individual heroics.</p></li></ul><p>We move fast, but we do so thoughtfully. We care deeply about quality because the technology we build ultimately impacts patients and healthcare professionals.</p><p>If you are looking for an environment where you can make a significant contribution, take ownership of meaningful work, and be surrounded by highly motivated colleagues, we'd love to meet you.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What we offer</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><p>Competitive salary including pension plan&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>25 days of annual leave based on a full-time position&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Hybrid work model&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Working together in a high-skilled team with our home base in Utrecht&nbsp;</p></li><li><p class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">Frequent out-of-work activities with our team, and annual company weekend away.</p></li><li><p>Training budget&nbsp;</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Opportunity to be key shaper of a new global industry niche: autonomous medical robotics&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;"><strong><em>We’re big fans of working from the office – this is where team spirit comes alive. At the same time, we offer flexibility, allowing up to two (out of 5) days of working from home for those who prefer it.</em></strong><span style="background-color:#C6C6C6">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;"><strong>Are you excited?</strong>&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">We totally understand that and so are we! By joining us, you can play an active role in changing the future of health care. Excited to join our revolution? Then we’d love to hear from you!&nbsp;</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW61117212 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;"><em>If you think you've got what it takes, but you don't meet all the requirements - we still recommend you apply. We would love to learn about your interest and experience and consider if you can be a good fit for Vitestro. Nobody is a perfect fit, and we welcome applications with imperfections. We offer a learning environment where we grow together!</em>&nbsp;</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vitestro/senior-quality-systems-officer-utrecht-167763","tags":["QA / RA"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Utrecht, Utrecht, Netherlands","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"stagiaire-business-development-amsterdam-354918","company_name":"SKYTREE","title":"Stagiair(e) Business Development","description":"<p><strong>Wij zijn Skytree</strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Skytree maakt de overgang mogelijk naar een wereld met schonere lucht voor iedereen. Dat doen we door slimme technologie te ontwikkelen en uit te rollen die CO₂ uit de atmosfeer afvangt, zodat deze kan worden hergebruikt of opgeslagen — om klimaatverandering tegen te gaan en de maatschappij en het bedrijfsleven wereldwijd verder te helpen.<br><br>Skytree is voortgekomen uit de European Space Agency (ESA). We zijn een internationaal team van bijzonder getalenteerde wetenschappers, ingenieurs en business professionals, ondersteund door een ervaren managementteam. Onze werkcultuur kenmerkt zich door een dynamische en slimme benadering van ondernemen, een open en begripvolle houding naar anderen, en de drive om de grenzen van het mogelijke te </span>verleggen.<br><br>Nu<span style="color:#000000"> we ons project portfolio in Nederland verder uitbreiden, zijn we op zoek naar een gedreven en leergierige stagiair(e) voor ons Project Development-team in Amsterdam.<br><br>Klaar om jouw stempel te drukken op de CO₂-transitie? Lees dan verder!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>De rol</strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Skytree ontwikkelt actief DAC-projecten in de Nederlandse glastuinbouw — een markt met veel potentieel op het gebied van duurzame energie en een groeiende vraag naar circulaire CO₂.<br><br>Als stagiair(e) Business Development voor Nederland ondersteun je het team bij het identificeren en ontwikkelen van deze kansen — van het eerste contact tot een project partnerschap. Dit is een praktische, commerciële rol: je brengt klanten in kaart, benadert prospects en helpt de pijplijn op te bouwen die de technologie van Skytree in de praktijk brengt.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><img style="width:1511px" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/o6v729f1du/Skytree_Values_2025_03.jpg"></figure><p><strong>Jouw impact</strong></p><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Marktontwikkeling &amp; kansen in kaart brengen</span></em></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ondersteunen van marktonderzoek en het in kaart brengen van kansen in Nederland, en het kwalificeren van potentiële projectpartners en afnemers.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">In kaart brengen van nieuwe commerciële kansen.</span></p></li></ul><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Ondersteuning bij projectontwikkeling</span></em></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Meewerken aan projectvoorstellen, businesscases en haalbaarheidsanalyses voor DAC-installaties.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Klantbezoeken en presenteren van ons product.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Bijhouden en actualiseren van de strategische project pijplijn van Skytree over de verschillende projectfases (stage gates).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Samenwerken met de teams business finance, productontwikkeling en commercie om projecten van idee tot realisatie te brengen.</span></p></li></ul><p><em><span style="color:#000000">Commercial intelligence</span></em></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Volgen van de ontwikkelingen in Nederland.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ondersteunen bij het voorbereiden van commerciële presentaties, pitchmateriaal en partnerbriefings.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Bijdragen aan het groeiende netwerk van Skytree in Nederland door relevante contacten te identificeren en te benaderen.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p><strong>Wat we zoeken</strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een masterstudent of recent afgestudeerde in Bedrijfskunde, Economie, Duurzaamheid, Energie of een verwant vakgebied.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Sterke analytische en onderzoeksvaardigheden — je zet marktdata om in bruikbare inzichten.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Uitstekende schriftelijke en mondelinge communicatievaardigheden in het Nederlands en Engels.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een ondernemende houding en oprechte interesse in klimaattechnologie en de energietransitie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je voelt je thuis in een dynamisch, internationaal team.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ervaring in commercie, consultancy of projectontwikkeling is een plus.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Beschikbaarheid per november voor minimaal 6 maanden.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Vragen?<br></strong>Nieuwsgierig, maar heb je nog aanvullende vragen? Neem dan contact op met <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/skytree/stagiaire-business-development-amsterdam-354918","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1792669911},{"slug":"iam-platform-engineer-keycloak-java-den-haag-146365","company_name":"Centraal Bureau voor de Statistiek","title":"IAM Platform Engineer - Keycloak & Java","description":"<p><em><span style="font-size:1.2em">Heb jij visie op identity platformen, werk je graag aan moderne authenticatieoplossingen en krijg je techniek én samenwerking in beweging? </span></em></p><p><em><span style="font-size:1.2em">Reageer dan nu op deze vacature.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Waar jij het</span><span style="color:#0580A1"> verschil </span><span style="color:#271D6C">maakt</span></span></strong></h4><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:1.2em">Binnen het IAM Platform team van CBS zoeken we een engineer die wil bouwen aan een toekomstbestendige identity dienstverlening op basis van open standaarden en moderne platformtechnologie.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size:1.2em">In deze rol werk je aan de ontwikkeling, integratie en doorontwikkeling van ons IAM-platform. <br><br>Je richt je op identity-componenten zoals Keycloak, federatie, authenticatieflows en koppelingen met applicaties en platformen. Daarbij combineer je platformdenken met engineering: je bouwt niet alleen mee aan een stabiele voorziening, maar zorgt ook dat deze verder automatiseert, beter integreert en makkelijker schaalbaar wordt.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je werkt aan een IAM-platform dat veilig, robuust en goed beheersbaar is. <br>Daarbij:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ontwikkel en beheer je IAM-functionaliteit op basis van Keycloak en aanverwante identity-componenten;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">realiseer je koppelingen met applicaties, API’s en platformdiensten;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">werk je aan authenticatie-, autorisatie- en federatievraagstukken met standaarden zoals OpenID Connect, OAuth2 en SAML;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ontwikkel en onderhoud je maatwerk, extensies of integraties in Java;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">automatiseer je deployments, testen en wijzigingen via CI/CD en werk je met technologieën zoals Linux, Docker, Kubernetes en Helm;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">stem je af met architecten, platformteams, securityspecialisten en PKI-collega’s om consistente oplossingen te realiseren voor onder meer TLS-certificaten, truststores, mTLS en certificaatgebaseerde authenticatie.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Je</span><span style="color:#0580A1"> toekomstige </span><span style="color:#271D6C">collega's</span></span></strong></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je wordt onderdeel van het IAM Platform team van CBS. Dit team is pas opgericht en nog niet lang in deze samenstelling bij elkaar. Juist dat maakt deze fase interessant: je krijgt de kans om mee te bouwen aan een nieuw team, aan de samenwerking binnen het team en aan de technische koers van het platform.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Binnen het team werken collega’s aan verschillende onderdelen van het IAM-landschap, zoals Keycloak, PKI en cloud-native security. Samen bouwen jullie aan identity-diensten die een belangrijke bouwsteen vormen voor een veilige en toekomstbestendige IT-omgeving. In deze opbouwfase zijn samenwerking, eigenaarschap, kennisdeling en continu verbeteren extra belangrijk.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Dit ben</span><span style="color:#0580A1"> jij</span></span></strong></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Je bent een engineer die techniek begrijpt én verder kijkt dan alleen de tooling. Je voelt je thuis in een omgeving waar ontwikkeling, integratie, beheer en afstemming samenkomen.</span></p><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Daarnaast breng je mee:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ervaring met Keycloak of vergelijkbare Identity Provider-technologie;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">kennis van OpenID Connect, OAuth2, SAML en federatieve authenticatie;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ervaring met Java, bij voorkeur in een omgeving met integraties, services, extensies of maatwerkcomponenten;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">ervaring met CI/CD, containers, Kubernetes, Linux en platformengineering;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">inzicht in hoe TLS-certificaten, truststores, mTLS en PKI integreren met Keycloak-omgevingen; ervaring met certificaatgebaseerde authenticatie is een pré;</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">een proactieve houding, het vermogen om technische keuzes helder uit te leggen en een sterke samenwerkingsstijl met gevoel voor kwaliteit, continu verbeteren en eigenaarschap.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#0580A1">Feitelijk </span><span style="color:#271D6C">goed geregeld</span></span></strong></h4><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Voor onze </span><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://werkenbijhetcbs.nl/arbeidsvoorwaarden"><span style="font-size:1.2em">arbeidsvoorwaarden</span></a><span style="font-size:1.2em"> volgen wij de CAO Rijk.<br>Dat betekent dat je onder andere kunt rekenen op het volgende:<br></span></p><ul><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een salaris van minimaal € 4132,- en maximaal € 6275,- bruto per maand op basis van 36 uur. Afhankelijk van je kennis en ervaring.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">8% vakantiegeld en een 13e maand. In totaal is dit 16,5% bovenop je salaris. Dit noemen wij het Individueel Keuze Budget (IKB). Je bepaalt zelf hoe, wanneer en op welke manier je dit budget wilt inzetten.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Pensioenopbouw bij het ABP Pensioenfonds.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Een laptop (Microsoft of Apple) en mobiele telefoon (Android of iOS).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="font-size:1.2em">Twee tot drie dagen thuiswerken, de rest ben je aanwezig in ons onlangs gerenoveerde gebouw. In je team maak je daar verder afspraken over.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong><span style="font-size:1.2em"><span style="color:#271D6C">Kom werken aan</span><span style="color:#0580A1"> de feiten</span></span></strong></h4><figure><iframe height="281" width="500" src="//player.vimeo.com/video/1143350266"></iframe></figure><p>We sluiten de vacature bij voldoende kandidaten.</p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remot