hip, clear communication, and getting things done together. We move quickly, learn by doing, and continuously improve how we support our customers. Right now, we're scaling across Europe and into the US, and we need a Backend Engineer that can carry that weight.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">This is what you'll do</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">As our Backend Engineer, you'll build the engine behind our platform: designing features that hold up under enterprise traffic, optimizing the paths that can't afford to crack, and partnering closely with Frontend, Product, and DevOps to turn business needs into systems that simply work. Reliability doesn't just happen here, we design for it. You care about clean code, resilient systems, and top notch performance.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Create technical designs for features that handle enterprise traffic across regions, and optimize the critical paths for performance and reliability</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Champion operational excellence, from code quality and testing to release readiness</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate with Product Owners, UX designers, and DevOps to turn business needs into working systems, owning it end to end and flagging early when something's off track</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Mentor engineers who are growing fast</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Work in focused 6-week cycles, a deliberate post-scrum method built for builders<br></span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">This is what you'll need</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">5+ years building backend systems that hold up under production traffic, with real input into the architecture decisions behind them</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Solid experience with PHP (Symfony) and relational databases like MySQL, including hands-on query optimization</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience debugging complex code and functionality using metrics and monitoring</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A business-first thinker: familiar with Domain-Driven Design (DDD), making sure business rules are clearly and correctly implemented in code</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Comfortable with ownership: you ship it, you own it</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Proactive by default: you flag risks and blockers early, and give status updates without being asked</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with Docker and GitLab CI/CD; Kubernetes is a plus</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">What you'll get</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">At Dyflexis, you'll be part of an ambitious, energetic, and customer-focused team. We offer:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Fixed salary up to €6.500 gross per month based on a 40-hour week (skill based).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Personal development budget to level up your skills.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">25 vacation days + your birthday off in exchange for cake.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">An in-house chef surprising you daily with fresh lunch.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">The best parties, drinks &amp; trips (Winter sports, Ibiza &amp; more).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Membership at ARJ Training boxing gym (home of champion Tarik &amp; Levi Rigters).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Solid pension plan &amp; 8% holiday allowance.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Buy or sell vacation days - you decide.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Travel allowance and WFH compensation.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Friday chair